2 CONT Marriages and descent
2 CONT
2 CONT # Andeca married, firstly, '''the daughter of King Miro.'''   [2].
2 CONT # Then in his second marriage, in 584, he married Siseguta, the widow of Miro [4].
2 CONT
2 CONT No descendants of Andeca are known, neither legitimate nor illegitimate[12].
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Genealogy 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/VANDALS,%20SUEVI,%20VISIGOTHS.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT *TEODEMIRO  (-570).  He succeeded in 561 as TEODEMIRO King of the Suevi at Lugo.  He divided his territories into two ecclesiastical provinces at the assembly at Lugo, Braga and Lugo, in 569[103].  m ---.  The name of Teodemiro's 
2 CONC wife or concubine is not known.  King Teodemiro & his [wife] had one child: 
2 CONT **1.         '''MIRÓN''' (-583).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  He succeeded his father in 570 as MIRÓN King of the Suevi at Lugo. The Iohannis Abbatis Biclarensis Chronica records t
2 CONC hat "Miro Suevorum rex" made war against "Runcones" in 572[104].  He made an alliance with Leovigildo King of the Visigoths in 579, but helped the latter's son Hermenegildo after he had rebelled and been captured in Seville.  Greg
2 CONC ory of Tours records that "Mir King of Galicia" supported Hermenegildo, son of Leovigildo King of the Visigoths, against his father but died immediately after returning to his own country[105].  King Mirón was himself captured and
2 CONC  obliged to swear loyalty to the Visigothic king[106].  The Iohannis Abbatis Biclarensis Chronica records the death in 583 of "Miro Suevorum rex"[107].  m as her first husband, SISEGUTIA, daughter of ---.  The Iohannis Abbatis Bic
2 CONC larensis Chronica records that "Audeca" succeeded in 584 "in Gallaccia Suevorum regnum" and married "Sisegutiam relictam Mironis regis"[108].  She married secondly (584) as his [second] wife, Audica, who had deposed King Eborico. 
2 CONC  King Mirón & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT ***a)         EBORICO (-after 585).  The Iohannis Abbatis Biclarensis Chronica names "Eboricus filius eius" when recording that he succeeded his father in 583 "in provincia Gallacciæ"[109].  Gregory of Tours names "Euric" as son o
2 CONC f "Mir King of Galicia" when recording that he succeeded his father and sought to renew a pact with King Leovigildo[110].  He succeeded his father in 583 as EBORICO King of the Suevi at Lugo.  He was deposed in 584 by Audica[111].
2 CONC   The Iohannis Abbatis Biclarensis Chronica records that he became a monk after he was deposed[112]. 
2 CONT ***b)         '''daughter''' .  Gregory of Tours records that Audica, a relation of Euric, married the sister of the latter[113].  m as his [first] wife, AUDICA, son of ---
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/VANDALS,%20SUEVI,%20VISIGOTHS.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT AUDICA (-585). Gregory of Tours records that Audica, a relation of Euric, married the sister of the latter and deposed his brother-in-law, before marrying the widow of his father-in-law[114]. He deposed King Eborico in 584, succee
2 CONC ded as AUDICA King of the Suevi. The Iohannis Abbatis Biclarensis Chronica records that "Audeca" succeeded in 584 "in Gallaccia Suevorum regnum" and married "Sisegutiam relictam Mironis regis"[115]. The Visigoths intervened in sup
2 CONC port of ex-King Eborico, defeated and deposed King Audica in 585, annexing the Suevi kingdom for themselves[116].
2 CONT
2 CONT m [firstly] '''--- of the Suevi''', daughter of MIRON King of the Suevi. Gregory of Tours records that Audica, a relation of Euric, married the sister of the latter[117].
2 CONT
2 CONT m [secondly] (584) as her second husband, SISEGUTIA, widow of MIRÓN King of the Suevi, daughter of ---. The Iohannis Abbatis Biclarensis Chronica records that "Audeca" succeeded in 584 "in Gallaccia Suevorum regnum" and married "S
2 CONC isegutiam relictam Mironis regis"[118].
2 CONT
