1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Guerin or Gerinus; born around 608, he was a Franco-Burgogne nobleman, brother of the Merovingian court historian Bodilo, both descendants of the House of the Counts of Ardennes and King Marcomir. He was the first 
2 CONC to be titled Count of Paris.[1] He opposed Ebroin's efforts to expand Neustria's power and was killed at Arras in 676.
