2 CONT
2 CONT Father:  Adalhelm, Graf von Worms1 d. a 764 
2 CONT
2 CONT Williswinthe von Worms Founded Imperial Monastery at Lorsch, near Worms on 12 Jul 764 with son, Count Cancor. She was born at of Wormsgau, Germany. She married Robert (Rutpert) I, Count in Upper Rhine and Wormgau, Duke in the Hasp
2 CONC engau, son of Lambert (Lantbertus) II and Chrotlind of the Franks, in 730.1Williswinthe von Worms died after 768.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family:  Robert (Rutpert) I, Count in Upper Rhine and Wormgau, Duke in the Haspengau b. 689, d. bt 757 - 764 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Thuringbert (Turincbertus)+ d. a 770
2 CONT
2 CONT Rupert, Count in the Oberrheingau (Thorgau), Breisgau, and Zurichgau+ d. a 782
2 CONT
2 CONT Cancor, Count Hereswint of Haspengau+1 
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations [S54] Middle & Far East Families, Haspengau.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------
2 CONT Williswint was the daughter of Count Adelhelm.1,2,3,4 In 730 Williswint, married Rutpert I Count of the Upper Rhine and Wormsgau, son of Lambert II and Chrotlind.1,2,3,4 In 764, she was a widow.1,4 She founded the Imperial Monaste
2 CONC ry at Lorsch near Worms with her eldest son, Count Cancor on 12 July 764. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Williswint and Rutpert I Count of the Upper Rhine and Wormsgau
2 CONT
2 CONT Thüringbert+1,2,4 ( - b 767)
2 CONT
2 CONT Rutpert Count in the Thurgau, Breisgau, and Zurichgau+2 ( - a 782)
2 CONT
2 CONT Count Cancor2,3,4
