1 NOTE On 12 July 764 founded Lorsch Abbey with her son and grandson
1 NOTE Erfgename van de goederen in de Wormsgouw. Zij sticht in 764 met haar oudste zoon Cancor het rijksklooster Lorsch bij Worms. Zij wordt vermeld in oorkonden tot 768
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 2-2438
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 2-2438
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 2-2438
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 2-2438
1 NOTE 1  NAME Williswint of /Adelhelm/ 2  SOUR S033320 3  DATA 4  TEXT Date of Import: Jan 17, 2001 1  BIRT 2  DATE ABT. 675 2  SOUR S033320 3  DATA 4  TEXT Date of Import: Jan 17, 2001
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [De La Pole.FTW]
2 CONT Sources: RC 102, 169; Ancestral Roots 48; AF; Kreantzler 1608.
2 CONT    Roots: Daughter of Count Adelhelm. Widow in 764.   RC: Williswint in the Wormsgau. Heiress of lands in the Wormsgau. Founded, 12 July 764, with her eldest son, Count Cancor, the Imperial Monastery at Lorsch, near Worms. Doesn't
2 CONC  specify that Rutpert I was the father of Count Cancor.
1 NOTE Source: THE RUFUS PARKS PEDIGREE by Brian J.L. Berry, chart on page 56.
2 CONT
2 CONT !Page 57:
2 CONT
2 CONT !4.  RUTPERT I, d. bef. 764; count in the Upper Rhine and Wormsgau; mar. WILLISWINT, dau. of Count ADELHEIM and heiress of large possessions int he wormsgau.  She founded 764 the monastery at Lorsch, 17 miles from Worms; its ruins
2 CONC  may still be seen.
2 CONT
2 CONT !Availability: The libraries of Ken, Karen, Kristen, Kevin, Brian, Amy, Adam and FAL
