2 CONT '''ROBERT''' [I] ([700/10]-before 764).  The third continuator of the Gesta Abbatum Trudonensium names "Robertus comes vel dux Hasbanie" in 715, and quotes a charter dated 7 Apr 742 under which "Robertus comes, filius condam Lambe
2 CONC rti" donated property "in villa…Sarcinio…in pago Hasbaniensi…[et] Halon, Scaffnis, Felepa et Marholt" to St Trudon[525].  Comte de Hesbaie.  Comes palatinus 741/42.  Graf im Oberrheingau und Wormsgau. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FRANKSMaiordomi.htm#_Toc359686226
