2 CONT 4.  RUTPERT I, d. bef. 764; count in the Upper Rhine and Wormsgau; mar. WILLISWINT, dau. of Count ADELHEIM and heiress of large possessions in the Wormsgau.  She founded 764 the monastery at Lorsch, 17 miles from Worms; its ruins 
2 CONC may still be seen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "Ancestral Roots of Sixty Colonists" by Frederick Lewis Weis.
