1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was the thirteenth king of the Suevi, ruling probably for only a few months of 520 (the lack of sources makes his reign imprecise); he was probably assassinated by order of his immediate successor Theodemund, wh
2 CONC o would reign for the next three decades as the 14th king. After the latter's death, Carriarico/Cararico (the 15th king) would rule for the next nine years, before a member of the Royal Household regained control of the country an
2 CONC d ended the dark period.
