1 NOTE Hertog van Ruparië. De Rupariërs zijn de oostelijke Rijnse Franken
1 NOTE Nog zonder grafelijke titel vermeld 11 juni 770; nadien graaf in de Bovenrijn- en Wormsgouw; oorkondt tot 807; heer van Dienheim (795).
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 2-2438
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 2-2438
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 2-2438
1 NOTE Robert II, Rodbert or Chrodobert (770-807) was a Frank, count of Worms and Rheingau and duke of Hesbaye around the year 800. His family is known as Robertians. His son is Robert of Worms and his grandson is Robert the Strong, the 
2 CONC namegiver of the Robertians. Robert of Hesbaye is the oldest known ancestor in the line of Robertians that is thought to be certain. He is the great-grandfather of two Frankish kings, Odo and Robert, that ruled in the kingdom of W
2 CONC estern Francia. One of his descendants is Hugh Capet, who was the "last Frankish king" and the "first king of France". The descendants of Hugh Capet ruled France until the French Revolution, with a junior line having ruled Spain s
2 CONC ince 1700.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingerman and Cancor are possibly his brothers. Landrada, mother of Saint Chrodogang, archbishop of Metz, is likely his sister. His father may have been named Rodbert or, Chrodobert. He was likely the son of Thuringbert of Worms an
2 CONC d Rheingau and grandson of Robert I of Worms and Rheingau, who died in 764.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ermengarde, wife of emperor Louis the Pious was most likely his niece.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT Riché, Pierre. The Carolingians, a family who forged Europe. 
1 NOTE Robert (Rupert) II, geboren omstreeks 765. Robert is overleden op 12-07-807, ongeveer 42 jaar oud. Notitie bij Robert: Nog zonder grafelijke titel vermeld 11 juni 770; nadien graaf in de Bovenrijn- en Wormsgouw; oorkondt tot 807; 
2 CONC heer van Dienheim (795). Hij trouwde met 1816905444465 Theodorata, geboren omstreeks 765. Theodorata is overleden.
