1 NOTE {geni:about_me} infanta de Castilla, reina consorte de León en dos ocasiones (951-956) y (958-960) y reina consorte de Navarra en (970-994)., Condesa de Castilla. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urraca_Fern%C3%A1ndez
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00106637&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT Urraca Fernández (¿? – 1007) fue infanta de Castilla, reina consorte de León en dos ocasiones (951–956) y (958–960) y reina consorte de Navarra en (970–994). Era hija de Fernán González y Sancha Sánchez de Navarra.
2 CONT
2 CONT Siguiendo la política de matrimonios de conveniencia de su padre Fernán González se casó con:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * El 941 se casa en primeras nupcias con Ordoño III hijo de Ramiro II; de este matrimonio nacieron:
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Bermudo, rey de León.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT           o El infante Ordoño de León, fallecido joven
2 CONT
2 CONT           o La infanta Teresa de León, monja
2 CONT
2 CONT     * El 958 se casa en segundas nupcias con Ordoño IV de León, usurpador del trono leonés. Mediante este enlace el rey pretende legitimar su poder. De este matrimonio nacieron hijos de los cuales se conoce el nombre de uno de ell
2 CONC os:
2 CONT
2 CONT           o García Ordóñez[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * El 962 se casa en terceras nupcias con Sancho Garcés II de Navarra. De este matrimonio nacerían:
2 CONT
2 CONT           o El infante García Sánchez II de Navarra (994–1000), rey de Navarra y conde de Aragón
2 CONT
2 CONT           o El infante Ramiro de Navarra (¿?–992)
2 CONT
2 CONT           o El infante Gonzalo de Navarra (¿?–997)
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Abda (Urraca) de Navarra «la Vascona», entregada a Almanzor, y que antes de ingresar en un convento le dio un hijo, Abderramán Sanchuelo.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Urraca Fernández (died 1007), infanta of Fernán González of Castile, was the queen consort of two Kings of León and one King of Navarre between 951 and 994. She acted as regent for her son Gonzalo, who had been given the County of
2 CONC  Aragon, and later was co-regent of the Kingdom of Navarre, along with her daughter-in-law Jimena Fernández and the bishops of Navarre, of her grandson Sancho III.
2 CONT
2 CONT [source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urraca_Fern%C3%A1ndez]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Urraca Fernández (died 1007), infanta of Fernán González of Castile, was the queen consort of two Kings of León and one King of Navarre between 951 and 994. She acted as regent for her son Gonzalo, who had been given the County of
2 CONC  Aragon, and later was co-regent of the Kingdom of Navarre, along with her daughter-in-law Jimena Fernández and the bishops of Navarre, of her grandson Sancho III.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was first married by her father to Ordoño III of León in 951. Fernán's support of Sancho the Fat cost her her husband's affection and she was repudiated in 956. By him she had two, and possibly three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ordoño, who died young 
2 CONT
2 CONT Theresa, who became a nun 
2 CONT
2 CONT (perhaps) Bermudo II of León, whose maternity is subject to scholarly debate 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 958, after Ordoño's death, she was remarried to Ordoño IV. He died in 960.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her third and most important marriage was contracted in 970 to Sancho II of Pamplona. Both Sancho and Urraca were grandchildren of Sancho I of Pamplona, because Urraca's mother was Sancho I's daughter Sancha. With Sancho, she had 
2 CONC several children:
2 CONT
2 CONT García Sánchez II of Pamplona 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ramiro (died 992) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gonzalo, who ruled the County of Aragon with Urraca as regent 
2 CONT
2 CONT Abda (Urraca) the Basque, given to Almanzor before entering a convent
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Urraca Fernández
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Urraca Fernández (died 1007), infanta of Fernán González of Castile, was the queen consort of two Kings of León and one King of Navarre between 951 and 994. She acted as regent for her son Gonzalo, who had been given the County of
2 CONC  Aragon, and later was co-regent of the Kingdom of Navarre, along with her daughter-in-law Jimena Fernández and the bishops of Navarre, of her grandson Sancho III.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was first married by her father to Ordoño III of León in 951. Fernán's support of Sancho the Fat cost her her husband's affection and she was repudiated in 956. By him she had two, and possibly three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ordoño, who died young
2 CONT
2 CONT Theresa, who became a nun
2 CONT
2 CONT (perhaps) Bermudo II of León, whose maternity is subject to scholarly debate
2 CONT
2 CONT In 958, after Ordoño's death, she was remarried to Ordoño IV. He died in 960.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her third and most important marriage was contracted in 970 to Sancho II of Pamplona. Both Sancho and Urraca were grandchildren of Sancho I of Pamplona, because Urraca's mother was Sancho I's daughter Sancha. With Sancho, she had 
2 CONC several children:
2 CONT
2 CONT García Sánchez II of Pamplona
2 CONT
2 CONT Ramiro (died 992)
2 CONT
2 CONT Gonzalo, who ruled the County of Aragon with Urraca as regent
2 CONT
2 CONT Abda (Urraca) the Basque, given to Almanzor before entering a convent
2 CONT
2 CONT Urraca Fernández de Castilla
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Fernán, conde de Castilla b. circa 910, d. June 970
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother	Urraca Garcés de Navarra b. circa 944?
2 CONT
2 CONT Charts	Descendants of Charlemage
2 CONT
2 CONT      Urraca Fernández de Castilla was the daughter of Fernán, conde de Castilla and Urraca Garcés de Navarra. Urraca Fernández de Castilla was a witness where Ordoño III Ramírez "el Bueno", rey de León husband of, correcting Bisho
2 CONC p Pelayo's facts, Urraca Fernández, daughter of Fernán González, count of Castile (931-970).1 Urraca Fernández de Castilla was wife of, correcting Bishop Pelayo's facts, Ordoño III of León.1 She married Ordoño III Ramírez "el Buen
2 CONC o", rey de León, son of Ramiro II "el Feroz Guerrero", rey de León and Adosinda Gutiérrez; Her 1st.2 Urraca Fernández de Castilla married rey de León Ordoño IV Alfonsez "el Malo", son of rey de León Alfonso IV Ordoñez "el Monje" a
2 CONC nd Oneca Sánchez de Navarra; Her 2nd. Urraca Fernández de Castilla married Sancho II "Abarca", rey de Pamplona y conde de Aragón, son of García II Sánchez, rey de Navarra and Andregota Galíndez, condesa de Aragón; His 2nd. Her 3rd
2 CONC .3 Urraca Fernández de Castilla was buried in the Church of Saint Mary, Oviedo, Asturias, Iberian peninsula. Reburied to avoid destruction of her tomb by the army of Almanzor. She was laid to rest with her father-in-law, King Rami
2 CONC ro II, and her husband (correcting Bishop Pelayo), King Ordono III, in the third coffin.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Ordoño III Ramírez "el Bueno", rey de León b. circa 926, d. 955
2 CONT
2 CONT Child	
2 CONT
2 CONT Bermudo II Ordoñez "el Gotoso", rey de Galicia y de León+ b. c 953, d. Sep 999
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 2
2 CONT
2 CONT rey de León Ordoño IV Alfonsez "el Malo" b. circa 926, d. 962
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 3
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho II "Abarca", rey de Pamplona y conde de Aragón b. circa 935, d. December 994
2 CONT
2 CONT Child	
2 CONT
2 CONT García III "el Temblón", rey de Navarra+ b. c 962?, d. b 8 Dec 9993
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S1074] Bishop Pelayo "the Fabulist" of Oviedo, "CRL", 79.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S1074] Bishop Pelayo "the Fabulist" of Oviedo, "CRL", 79 - correcting Bishop Pelayo.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S882] Armerías ilustres, online http://members.xoom.com/chema, Corona de Navarra.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Urraca Fernández (died 1007), infanta of Fernán González of Castile, was the queen consort of two Kings of León and one King of Navarre between 951 and 994. She acted as regent for her son Gonzalo, who had been given the County of
2 CONC  Aragon, and later was co-regent of the Kingdom of Navarre, along with her daughter-in-law Jimena Fernández and the bishops of Navarre, of her grandson Sancho III.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was first married by her father to Ordoño III of León in 951. Fernán's support of Sancho the Fat cost her her husband's affection and she was repudiated in 956. By him she had two, and possibly three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Ordoño, who died young
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Theresa, who became a nun
2 CONT
2 CONT     * (perhaps) Bermudo II of León, whose maternity is subject to scholarly debate
2 CONT
2 CONT In 958, after Ordoño's death, she was remarried to Ordoño IV. He died in 960.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her third and most important marriage was contracted in 970 to Sancho II of Pamplona. Both Sancho and Urraca were grandchildren of Sancho I of Pamplona, because Urraca's mother was Sancho I's daughter Sancha. With Sancho, she had 
2 CONC several children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * García Sánchez II of Pamplona
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Ramiro (died 992)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Gonzalo, who ruled the County of Aragon with Urraca as regent
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Abda (Urraca) the Basque, given to Almanzor before entering a convent
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
