1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Franconia:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FRANCONIA.htm#Robertdied866A
2 CONT
2 CONT ROBERT [II] (-12 Jul 807).  "Turincbertus et filius meus Rotbertus" donated property "in pago Rinensi in villa…Birstat" to Lorsch by charter dated Jun 770[601].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf im Wormsgau und Oberrheingau 795/807.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Herr zu Dienheim 795.  
2 CONT
2 CONT [same person as…?  RADBERT (-807).  Einhard records that "Radbertus missus imperatoris" died in 807 after returning from the Orient[602].  It is possible that "Radbertus" refers to "Rodbertus".]  
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly THEODERATA, daughter of --- (-before 789).  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly ISENGARDE, daughter of ---.  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.  789.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert [II] & his first wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i) ROBERT [III] (-before 19 Feb 834).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the English Wikipedia page on Wormsgau:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wormsgau
2 CONT
2 CONT The Wormsgau or pago wormatiensi was in the Middle Ages a county, which extended itself not only in the surroundings of the city of Worms, Germany, but concurrently along the Rhine widely in northern direction until short of reach
2 CONC ing Coblenz. The city of Mainz belonged likewise to it as to the start of the 9th century also Boppard, which in reality ca. 825 was already lost again...
2 CONT
2 CONT Robertians
2 CONT
2 CONT Second Robertian Count in Wormsgau:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert II (Rutbert II o. Hruodbertus) (770 attested, † 12 July 807), his grandson, 795/807 Count in Worms- and Oberrheingau, 795 Lord to Dienheim, ∞ I Theoderata (Tiedrada) (766/777 attested, † before 789), ∞ II Isengarde, 789
2 CONT
2 CONT Third Robertian Count in Wormsgau:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert III (Rutpert III) († before 834) his son, 812/830 Count in Wormsgau, Count in Oberrheingau, 825 imperial missus in Bishopric of Mainz, ∞ ca. 808 Wiltrud (Waldrada) of Orléans, 829/834 heiress of possessions in Orléans, daug
2 CONC hter of Count Hadrian and of Waldrat from the House of the Widonen
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://craveirolopes.familytreeguide.com/getperson.php?personID=I194&tree=T1
