1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Leudwinus''' ('''St. Leudwinus''', '''Leutwinus''', '''Lievin''', '''Liutwin''', '''Ludwin''') (about 660 - 722), was Count and bishop of Trier, 697-715 or 685-704. His parents were Warinus, Count of Poitiers (6
2 CONC 38-677) and Kunza of Metz, daughter of Clodoule, Bishop of Metz, making him the great-grandson of Arnulf of Metz. He was buried at Mettlach.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married a daughter of Chrodobertus II and they had a daughter, Rotrude of Treves who married Charles Martel.
