1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Warinus of Poitiers (Warin, Guerin, Gerinus, Varinus) (d. 677) was the Franco-Burgundian Count of Poitiers and Count of Paris who became Saint Warinus, Martyr of the Franks.] He was the son of Saint Sigrada of Sain
2 CONC te-Marie de Soissons and the brother of Saint Leodegarius. He was also the father of Saint Leudwinus.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 677 Warinus was stoned to death near Arras because of a feud between his brother, Leodegarius, and Ebroin, the Frankish Mayor of the Palace of Neustria.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Warinus
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT AI Summary - 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dido, also known as Desiderius, was a Bishop of Poitiers who lived in the 7th century. He was the maternal uncle of Saint Leodegar (also known as Saint Leger) and the brother of Saint Sigrada. He played a role in the Merovingian p
2 CONC olitical landscape, particularly through his influence on Leodegar, who became a prominent figure in the Merovingian church and kingdom. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Connections:
2 CONT Dido belonged to a prominent Frankish aristocratic family. He was the brother of Saint Sigrada, and maternal uncle to Saint Leodegar (Bishop of Autun) and Saint Warinus. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He served as Bishop of Poitiers from sometime before 656 until after 670. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dido's life was intertwined with the political turmoil of the Merovingian era. His nephew, Leodegar, became involved in disputes with the Neustrian Mayor of the Palace, Ebroin, which led to Leodegar's persecution and martyrdom. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dido played a key role in Leodegar's early life, providing him with an education and likely shaping his path toward a religious and political career. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Some genealogies suggest that Dido and his sister Sigrada might have been descendants of Senator Ansbertus and Tonantius Ferreolus. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FRANKSMaiordomi.htm#BerswindaMAthicus
2 CONT
2 CONT Two siblings, parents not known: 
2 CONT *1.         DIDO (-after 673).  Bishop of Poitou.  … The Passio Leudegarii names "Didone…Pectavi urbe episcopo" as "avunculo" of "Leodegarius urbis Agustedunensis episcopus"[503]. 
2 CONT *2.         [sister] (Saint Sigrada).  The Chronicon Ebersheimense names "Didone Pictavensi…episcopo" when recording that he was "avunculus" of "sanctum Leudegarium"[504], which would indicate that Leudegar's mother was Dido's sis
2 CONC ter, assuming that "avunculus" is used in its strict sense of maternal uncle.  m ---.  Three children: 
2 CONT            **a)         LEUDEGAR (-murdered 676).  
2 CONT            **b)         GARINUS [Warin] (-murdered 676).  
2 CONT            **c)         daughter .  m ---.  [Two] children: 
2 CONT                          ***i)          [daughter .  The sources cited below under Berswinda state that she was "sororem…regina", but it is not known to which queen this may refer.  m --- King of the Franks.] 
2 CONT                         ***ii)         BERSWINDA .  The Cronica Hohenburgensis records the marriage of "Athicum seu Adalricum" and "Berswindam…filiam sororis sancti Leodegarii, sororem videlicet regina"[511].  The Chronicon Ebersh
2 CONC eimense names "Berswindam, filiam sororis Leodegarii episcopi…et Garini comitis Pictavensis, sororem videlicet regina" as the wife of Athicus[512].  m ADALRICUS [Athicus], son of LEUDESIUS maior domus & his wife --
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Catholic_Archdiocese_of_Poitiers
2 CONT * Brucker, Pierre-Paul. ''L'Alsace et l'Eglise au temps du Pape Saint Léon IX'' (Bruno d'Eguisheim). Tome Premier (Paris, France: Retaux-Bray, 1889) p. 299. Berswinde, born about 1640, married Etichon during the reign of Childeric
2 CONC  II (660-673) and their daughter Sainte Odile was born circa 660. Brucker gives a good chronology in the book, and cites the chronicle of Ebersheim and a handwritten notice from the 9th century formerly preserved at the abbey of S
2 CONC aint-Grégoire, and which make Berswinde the niece of Saint Léger d'Autun (sister of Saint Léger was born circa 620 and Berswinde circa 640 or slightly after).
