1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Warinus of Poitiers (Warin, Guerin, Gerinus, Varinus) (d. 677) was the Franco-Burgundian Count of Poitiers and Count of Paris who became Saint Warinus, Martyr of the Franks. He was the son of Saint Sigrada of Saint
2 CONC e-Marie de Soissons and the brother of Saint Leodegarius. He was also the father of Saint Leudwinus.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 677 Warinus was stoned to death near Arras because of a feud between his brother, Leodegarius, and Ebroin, the Frankish Mayor of the Palace of Neustria.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Gunza von Treves, a Frankish noblewoman in France. His wife came from an influential Frankish family. She was the sister of Saint Basinus of Treves. They had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Doda of Poitiers''' (circa b. 659 - circa d. 678)
2 CONT * Leudwinus, Count of Poitier (b. 660 - d. 722)
2 CONT * Grimgert, Count of Paris (circa b.667)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Warinus
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT == MedLands ==
2 CONT
2 CONT CHRODBERT [Robert] [II] (-before 12 Sep 677).  According to Europäische Stammtafeln[519], Chrodbert [II] was the son of "Lambert [I] nobilis in Neustria †after 650", who in turn was the son of Chrodbert [I] (see above).  No refere
2 CONC nce has been found to "Lambert [I]" in any of the primary sources so far consulted and it has been decided to omit him until a positive identification can be made.  "Chlodovius rex Francorum" confirmed the privileges of the abbey 
2 CONC of St Denis by charter dated 22 Jun 653, subscribed by "…Chradoberctus…"[520].  Chancellor for King Clothar III 658.  "Childericus rex Francorum, Chadicho duce, Rodeberto comite" donated property to the monastery of St Gregory in 
2 CONC Alsace by charter dated 4 Mar 673, the editor of the compilation identifying "Rodeberto comite" as "comes Alsatiæ superioris sive Sundgaviæ"[521].  Comes palatinus 2 Oct 678.  m '''DODA''', daughter of --- (-before 12 Sep 677).  T
2 CONC he Vita Leudegarii names "Rotpertus et uxor Tota"[522].  "Theudericus rex Francorum" donated property held by "Detta relicta Chrodoberctho quondam" to "Chainoni diacono" by charter dated 12 Sep 677[523].  Chrodbert [II] & his wife
2 CONC  had [one possible child]: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >a)         [LAMBERT [II] (-before 741). 
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FRANKSMaiordomi.htm#_Toc359686226
