1 OCCU Conde de Castilla (995 al 1017), Conde Soberano de Castela, Greve, Conde de Castilla, Count of Castile, Conde, Conde de Castilla. Llamado "el de los buenos fueros"., Count of Castile and Álava., Señor de Vizcaya, Conde Soberano de
2 CONC  Castilla (995-1017)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sancho García http://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sancho_Garc%C3%ADa
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho García, el de los Buenos Fueros (?-1017). Conde de Castilla del 995 al 1017. Hijo de García Fernández y su mujer Ava de Ribagorza. Sucedió a su padre al frente del condado tras su muerte aunque protagonizó una sublevación c
2 CONC ontra él con apoyo de Almanzor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contrajo matrimonio con Urraca Gómez de la familia condal Banu Gómez de Saldaña: 1) García Sánchez (1010-1028), conde de Castilla. 2) Muniadona de Castilla, condesa de Ribagorza y de Castilla, casada con Sancho III de Navarra. 3) 
2 CONC Sancha de Castilla (1006-1027), casada con el conde de Barcelona Berenguer Ramón I. 4) Trígida Sánchez, abadesa en el Monasterio de San Salvador de Oña. 5) Urraca Sánchez ( ? -1041) casada con Sancho Guillermo, duque de Gascuña, c
2 CONC onde de Burdeos.
2 CONT
2 CONT En el año 1000 Almanzor ataca Castilla, Sancho García sale a su encuentro y es derrotado en la Batalla de Cervera no sin antes causar un gran número de bajas en las filas de Almanzor. Participó junto con Sancho III de Navarra y Al
2 CONC fonso V de León en la famosa batalla de Calatañazor donde Almanzor sufrió su primera derrota importante.
2 CONT
2 CONT Apoyó a Sulaiman al-Mustain en las luchas civiles cordobesas, recibiendo a cambio varias plazas en la línea del Duero (Osma, San Esteban de Gormaz, Clunia, Berlanga de Duero, Sepúlveda, Peñafiel) Conocido como "el de los Buenos Fu
2 CONC eros" por los privilegios que dio a diversas poblaciones de Castilla. Fue el fundador del Monasterio de San Salvador de Oña en 1011, donde actualmente está enterrado.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sancho García (d. 1017), called of the Good Laws (in Spanish, el de los Buenos Fueros), was the count of Castile and Álava from 995 to his death. He was the son of Count García Fernández, against whom he rebelled with the support 
2 CONC of Almanzor, the effective ruler of Córdoba. This resulted in the partition of the county between Sancho and his father, and the county was not reunited until his father's death five years later. He was succeeded by his own son Ga
2 CONC rcía.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife was named Urraca, whose origin has been subject to speculation. The current consensus makes her his cousin, the daughter of count Gómez Díaz of Saldaña, head of the Beni Gómez family, by Muniadona Fernández of Castile. Th
2 CONC ey had:
2 CONT
2 CONT Muniadona Mayor, eldest daughter, married Sancho III of Navarre, through whom right to the county eventually passed.  Ferdinand, died before 2 March 999  Tigridia, abbess of San Salvador de Oña  Sancha, married Berenguer Ramon I, 
2 CONC Count of Barcelona  García, who succeeded his father  They may also have been parents of:
2 CONT
2 CONT Urraca, wife of Sancho VI William of Gascony
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sancho García (d. 1017), called of the Good Laws (in Spanish, el de los Buenos Fueros), was the count of Castile and Álava from 995 to his death. He was the son of Count García Fernández, against whom he rebelled with the support 
2 CONC of Almanzor, the effective ruler of Córdoba. This resulted in the partition of the county between Sancho and his father, and the county was not reunited until his father's death five years later. He was succeeded by his own son Ga
2 CONC rcía.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife was named Urraca, whose origin has been subject to speculation. The current consensus makes her his cousin, the daughter of count Gómez Díaz of Saldaña, head of the Beni Gómez family, by Muniadona Fernández of Castile. Th
2 CONC ey had:
2 CONT
2 CONT Muniadona Mayor, eldest daughter, married Sancho III of Navarre, through whom right to the county eventually passed. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ferdinand, died before 2 March 999 
2 CONT
2 CONT Tigridia, abbess of San Salvador de Oña 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancha, married Berenguer Ramon I, Count of Barcelona 
2 CONT
2 CONT García, who succeeded his father 
2 CONT
2 CONT They may also have been parents of:
2 CONT
2 CONT Urraca, wife of Sancho VI William of Gascony
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sancho García (died 1017), called of the Good Laws (in Spanish, el de los Buenos Fueros), was the count of Castile and Álava from 995 to his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho was the son of count García Fernández and his wife Aba of Ribagorza. He rebelled against his father with the support of Almanzor, the effective ruler of Córdoba. This resulted in the partition of the county between father a
2 CONC nd son, and the county was not reunited until his father's death five years later. He renewed the Reconquista by rebelling against Almanzor, alongside García Sánchez II of Pamplona and García Gómez of the Banu Gómez. Sancho led th
2 CONC e coalition that was defeated at the Battle of Cervera in July 1000, but in early September successfully turned back the Córdoban invasion of his county. Almanzor was again campaigning against Sancho in 1002 when another battle oc
2 CONC curred, remembered by the Christians as the Battle of Calatañazor and Muslims as the Pedroso expedition. The two sides report different outcomes to the battle itself, but Almanzor died of injuries received in the conflict, removin
2 CONC g Sancho's primary antagonist and leaving the Caliphate of Córdoba in crisis. Sancho ruled for another 15 years, and was succeeded by his own son García.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife was named Urraca, whose appears to have been his cousin, the daughter of count Gómez Díaz of Saldaña, head of the Beni Gómez family, by Muniadona Fernández of Castile. They had:
2 CONT
2 CONT Muniadona Mayor, eldest daughter, married Sancho III of Navarre, through whom right to the county eventually passed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ferdinand, died before 2 March 999
2 CONT
2 CONT Tigridia, abbess of San Salvador de Oña, which he founded for her to direct.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancha, married Berenguer Ramon I, Count of Barcelona
2 CONT
2 CONT García, who succeeded his father
2 CONT
2 CONT They may also have been parents of:
2 CONT
2 CONT Urraca, wife of Sancho VI William of Gascony
2 CONT
