2 CONT Sources: RC 349; "The Franks" by Edward James; Kraentzler 1657, 1778, 1780, Pfafman.   RC 349 continues this line back another five generations, but with the warning that 1980 research does not carry this line beyond Chilperic. Wi
2 CONC ll add two more generations from Kraentzler line 1778, just so they won't get lost.
2 CONT    K: Chilperic, King of Bourgogne.   K-1657: Chilperich de Bourgogne, King of Geneve, later of Lyon.
2 CONT    Pfafman: Chilperic of Burgundy.
1 NOTE Chilperic II, King of the Burgundians
2 CONT Third son of Gundioc, King of the Burgundians. After succeeding hisfather with his three brothers, he was killed by his brother Gundobad,along with his wife, and his two daughters were driven into exile.
