1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marriage year 644 instead of 745?
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Adèle de Trèves, Abbess of Pfalzel'''. She was not a daughter of King Dagobert. The primary source that names her as a daughter of Bodilon and Sigarde is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Catholic Encyclopedia'' says about her grandson, St. Gregory of Utrecht, "Gregory was born of a noble family at Trier. His father Alberic was the son of Addula, who, as widow, was Abbess of Pfalzel (Palatiolum) near Trier. On ac
2 CONC count of the similarity of names, and in consequence of a forged last will, Addula has been frequently confounded with Adala (Adela), daughter of Dagobert II of Austrasia--thus falsely making Gregory a scion of the royal house of 
2 CONC the Merovingians." [http://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07021a.htm "St. Gregory of Utrecht" in ''Catholic Encyclopedia''].
2 CONT
2 CONT According to online sources, she was a daughter of Bodilon and Sigarde:
2 CONT
