2 CONT 2.          Saint Sigrada [sister] b,Kingdom of Burgundy. d. 679 Soissons  The Chronicon Ebersheimense names "Didone Pictavensi…episcopo" when recording that he was "avunculus" of "sanctum Leudegarium"[504], which would indicate t
2 CONC hat Leudegar's mother was Dido's sister, assuming that "avunculus" is used in its strict sense of maternal uncle.  m -Count Bodilon of Poitiers. She became ancestor of the Franco-Lombard dynasty of Widonids (lambertiners)
2 CONT **a)         LEUDEGAR (-murdered 676).  
