2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Merovingian-102
2 CONT
2 CONT “Parentage from Sigebert III has been removed, as purely fanciful.”
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigebert_III
2 CONT
2 CONT The Mayor of the Palace Grimoald managed to convince the young Sigebert, who was childless at the time, to adopt as his heir Grimoald's son Childebert the Adopted. However, the king married Chimnechild of Burgundy and had a son of
2 CONC  his own, the future king Dagobert II. He also had a daughter, Bilichild, the future Queen of Neustria and Burgundy.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT “Berchinde Berswinde Meroving (daughter of Sigebert King of Merovingian and Hymnegilde) died date unknown.”.  No longer accepted. (See below.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Not listed by Medlands as daughter of Sigebert lll:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEROVINGIANS.htm#SigebertIdied575B
2 CONT
2 CONT King Dagobert I had one illegitimate child by Mistress (1):
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         SIGEBERT ([9 Oct 630/19 Jan 631]-1 Feb 656, bur Metz, basilique de Saint-Martin).  Fredegar records the marriage of King Dagobert in the eighth year of his reign to "puella nomen Ragnetrudæ" and the birth of "filium…Sig
2 CONC ybertum" in the same year[403].  … He was canonised by the Catholic church in 1170.  m CHIMNECHILDIS [Himnilde/Emnehilde], daughter of --- (-676 or after).  
2 CONT
2 CONT King Sigebert III & his wife had [two] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         DAGOBERT ([652/56]-murdered Woëvre forest 23 Dec 679, bur Stenay, basilique Saint-Rémi).  On the death of his father, Grimoald, maior domus in Austrasia, exiled Dagobert to Ireland where he may have lived at the abbey o
2 CONC f Slane[413].  … After a brief period of conflict, it was agreed that King Theoderich should retain Neustria and Burgundy while Dagobert succeeded as DAGOBERT II King of the Franks in Austrasia.  "Dagobertus rex Francorum" names "
2 CONC genitor noster Sigibertus rex" in his charter dated 1 Aug 677[415].  He was murdered on the orders of maior domus Ebroin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         [BILICHILDIS (-murdered forest of Lognes, near Chelles [18 Oct/10 Nov] 675, bur Paris, Saint-Germain-des-Prés).  … m ([666/8 Sep 667]) CHILDERICH II King of the Franks, son of CLOVIS II King of the Franks & his wife Bat
2 CONC hildis --- (-murdered forest of Lognes, near Chelles [18 Oct/10 Nov] 675, bur Paris, Saint-Germain-des-Prés).] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~havens5/p29565.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Weis' "Ancestral Roots . . ." (181:1) is silent regarding her parentage. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Some sources, e.g. Turton's "Plantagenet Ancestry," show her as a daughter of Sigebert III, King of Austrasia, but there has never been a descent from the Merovingian kings documented to the  satisfaction of serious genealogists, 
2 CONC and this is among those no longer accepted. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Settipani's "La prehistoire de Capetiens" p.106 says (in French): 
2 CONT
2 CONT >"In the 12th century, the Chronicle of Ebbersheim affirmed that Bereswinda, niece of St. Leger of Autun, wife of the duke of Alsace Adalric Ethic, was the sister of a queen. Chronologically, the  queen in question, who cannot be 
2 CONC identified as Baldechildis, of humble Saxon origin, nor as Bilichildis, daughter of king Sigebert III could well be Chimnechildis [wife of Sigebert III and of unkown origin]."6 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT “possibly a dau. of the sister of Dido (Merovingian), Bishop of Poitou”  2.
