1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00020375&tree=LEO
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ''Europäische Stammtafeln'' says he was son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Lambert-I/6000000078883627553 Lambert I], who was son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-I/6000000078883152658 Robert I].
2 CONT
2 CONT == MedLands ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''CHRODBERT''' [Robert] [II] (-before 12 Sep 677).  According to Europäische Stammtafeln[519], Chrodbert [II] was the son of "Lambert [I] nobilis in Neustria †after 650", who in turn was the son of Chrodbert [I] (see above).  No 
2 CONC reference has been found to "Lambert [I]" in any of the primary sources so far consulted and it has been decided to omit him until a positive identification can be made.  "Chlodovius rex Francorum" confirmed the privileges of the 
2 CONC abbey of St Denis by charter dated 22 Jun 653, subscribed by "…Chradoberctus…"[520].  Chancellor for King Clothar III 658.  "Childericus rex Francorum, Chadicho duce, Rodeberto comite" donated property to the monastery of St Grego
2 CONC ry in Alsace by charter dated 4 Mar 673, the editor of the compilation identifying "Rodeberto comite" as "comes Alsatiæ superioris sive Sundgaviæ"[521].  Comes palatinus 2 Oct 678.  m DODA, daughter of --- (-before 12 Sep 677).  T
2 CONC he Vita Leudegarii names "Rotpertus et uxor Tota"[522].  "Theudericus rex Francorum" donated property held by "Detta relicta Chrodoberctho quondam" to "Chainoni diacono" by charter dated 12 Sep 677[523].  Chrodbert [II] & his wife
2 CONC  had [one possible child]: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >a)         [LAMBERT [II] (-before 741).  
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FRANKSMaiordomi.htm#_Toc359686226
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke of Neustria, Comte Palatin de Bavière
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
