2 CONT AUDOIN 547-560, ALBOIN 560-572
2 CONT
2 CONT [---] . (Unknown)  King of the Pissa. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m MENIA ---.  The Historia Langobardorum names "mater…Audoin…Menia uxor fuit Pissæ regis"[149].  This wording suggests that "Pissæ regis" was not the father of Audoin, presumably Menia's second husband.  It is assumed that "Pissæ"
2 CONC  indicates that he was king of a tribe of that name. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [King of the Pissa] & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.   AUDOIN (-in Pannonia 560).  
2 CONT *The Historia Langobardorum names "Audoin ex genere…Gausus" and his mother "Menia uxor…Pissæ regis"[150].  
2 CONT *He was installed as AUDOIN King of the Lombards in Hungary in [547] in succession to King Walthari.  The Origo Gentis Langobardorum records that "Auduin" reigned after Walthari, specifying that he brought the Lombards into Pannon
2 CONC ia and, in a later passage, stating that they remained in Pannonia for 43 years[151].  Byzantium encouraged the Lombards to consolidate their position in Pannonia by granting them the city of Noricum and other strongholds, though 
2 CONC it is reported that they celebrated by raiding Dalmatia and Illyricum[152].  
2 CONT *The war with the Gepids, which started in [547], was settled by a peace treaty imposed by Emperor Justinian in 552, under which the Lombards sent troops to Italy to help Narses rout the Ostrogoths[153].  
2 CONT *The Historia Langobardorum records that Audoin died in Pannonia[154].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly RODELINDA [Roddenda], daughter of ---.  
2 CONT *The Origo Gentis Langobardorum names "Roddenda" as mother of "Albuin filius [Auduini]"[155].  The Historia Langobardorum names "Rodelenda" as mother of Alboin[156].  Paulus Diaconus names "Rodelindam" as wife of Audoin and mother
2 CONC  of Alboin[157].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly --- of the Thuringians, daughter of HERMINAFRID King of the Thuringians & his wife Amalaberga the Ostrogoth.  
2 CONT *Procopius records that "Amalafridus, vir Gotthus, ex filia nepos Amalafridæ sororis Theoderici Gotthorum regis et filius Hermenefridi regis Thoringorum…sororem eius” married "Anduino Langobardorum regi"[158].  The Codex Theodosia
2 CONC nus records that the daughter of Amalaberga became the second wife of King Audoin[159].  
2 CONT
2 CONT King Audoin & his first wife had [two] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)  ALBOIN (-murdered 28 Jun 572).  
2 CONT *The Origo Gentis Langobardorum names "Albuin" as son of "Auduin"[160].  Paulus Diaconus names "Alboin, filius Audoin" when recording his succession[161].  He succeeded in 560 as ALBOIN King of the Lombards in Pannonia.  He was cr
2 CONC owned ALBOIN King of the Lombards in Italy at Milan in [570]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         [---.  m ---.]  (or father of...) GISULF .  
2 CONT *Shield-bearer of Alboin King of the Lombards, who installed him as duke in the region of Friuli after the Longobard migration into Italy in [569][162].  Paulus Diaconus records that King Alboin installed "Gisulfum…suum nepotem" a
2 CONC s "ducem…[in] Foroiulanæ civitati"[163].  The Chronicle of Andreas Bergomatis records that Alboin conceded Friuli to "nepoti sui Gisolfi"[164].  The precise relationship between Gisulf and King Alboin is unknown and may have been 
2 CONC more remote than implied by "nephew" if the word nepos if translated strictly in these passages. 
2 CONT
