2 CONT
2 CONT SAINT GONDOLFUS (Munderic5, Cloderic the Parricide of COLOGNE4, Siegbert the Lame3, Childebert2, Clovis the Riparian1), son of Munderic and Arthemia _____, was born before 599, and died between 599 and 679.
2 CONT
2 CONT Consecrated Bishop of Tongres 599. He, not Bodegisel I, was almost certainly the father of Bodegisel II. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Child:
2 CONT
2 CONT i.	BODEGISEL II7; m. ODA.
2 CONT
2 CONT --Laurel Logan
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Suffix : Biskop av Tongres 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT St. Gondolfus of Tongres (545 - 599) was born in 545 in Aquitaine, France. He was the younger son to Munderic, Lord of Vitry and Arthemia of Perthois. He married Palatina of Troyes and they had a son named Borogiso II of Aquitaine
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT As a son of Munderic, a Prince of Cologne, Gondolfus was the younger son and therefor not able to rule unless his older brother Borogiso I, were to meet an untimely death. Instead Gondolfus was coronated as the Bishop of Tongres i
2 CONC n Gaul, a very prestigious and lofty position. He died in Bourges in 599.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gondolfus's only known son, Borogiso II became the Governor of Aquitaine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gondolfus has been cannonized as a Catholic Saint and has a feast day of June 17th.
2 CONT
2 CONT His name can be found spelled as "Saint Gundulphus" in many catholic references.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography by; Shanna Landgrave, Descendent of St. Gundulphus and Palatina of Troyes
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Consecrated 599. Was Brother of Bodegeisel I. He was the father of Bodegeisel II.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p843.htm#i25318
