2 CONT
2 CONT Chlothar II (or Chlotar, Clothar, Clotaire, Chlotochar, or Hlothar, giving rise to Lothair; 584 – 629), called the Great (le Grand) or the Young (le Jeune), King of Neustria, and, from 613 to 629, King of all the Franks, was not y
2 CONC et born when his father, King Chilperic I died in 584. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His mother, Fredegund, was regent until her death in 597, at which time the thirteen-year-old Chlothar began to rule for himself. As king, he continued his mother's feud with Brunhilda, queen of Austrasia, with equal viciousness a
2 CONC nd bloodshed.
2 CONT
2 CONT The first wife of Chlothar II was Haldetrude (ca 575–604). She was the mother of Dagobert I. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Chlothar's second wife was Bertrada. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His third wife was Sichilde, who bore him Charibert II and a daughter, Oda.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
