2 CONT
2 CONT    Merovingian king of Neustria and sole ruler of the Franks from 613. Aninfant when his father, Chilperic I, was assassinated in 584, he wasassured the succession by the power of his mother, Fredegund, and by theprotection of his
2 CONC  uncle, Guntram, king of Burgundy. Fighting off anattack by his cousin Childebert II of Austrasia-Burgundy in 592, Chlotarhimself seized territory from Childebert's young successors, TheodebertII and Theodoric II, in 596 but lost 
2 CONC much of his realm to them in 599 or600. In 613, however, when both were dead, Austrasian hostility towardBrunhild, great-grandmother of Theodoric's young son, Sigebert II,allowed Chlotar to seize both Austrasia and Burgundy and th
2 CONC us to reunitethe Frankish lands. He killed both Sigebert and Brunhild.
2 CONT    Chlotar enjoyed a high reputation among churchmen, relations with whomwere regulated in a wide-ranging edict issued at the Council of Paris inOctober 614 and intended to settle the problems arising from the longyears of turmoil
2 CONC . Apart from some trouble in Burgundy, the years after613 were in fact peaceful. Chlotar did not unify the administration,however; he maintained separate mayors of the palace for the threedistricts over which he ruled, and in 623 
2 CONC he established his son,Dagobert I, as king of Austrasia.
2 CONT
2 CONT To cite this page: "Chlotar II" Encyclopædia Britannica
2 CONT <http://www.britannica.com/eb/article?eu=84441&tocid=0&query=chlotar%20ii>
2 CONT 584King of Neustria
2 CONT 613King of France
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT KING CLOTHAIRE II OF SOISSONS (Chilperic I , Clothaire I, Clovis I,Childeric I, Merovaeus, Clodion), son of King Chilperic I and Fredegonda,was born in 584, and died in 628 in Paris. He married Altrude.
2 CONT King of Soissons 584-613
2 CONT Sole king of the Franks 617-628
2 CONT He signed the "Perpetual Constitution" 614/5 (an early Magna Charta)
2 CONT Children: i. DAGOBERT I King of France & AUSTRASIA, b. in 602; d. in 638.
2 CONT    ii. Charibert II, Duke of AQUITAINE
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Chlothar II of The Franks King of Franks , son of Chilperic I De SoissonsKing of Franks and Fredegonde, Queen of The Franks (of Soisson), was bornin 584 and died in 629, at age 45. Another name for Chlothar wasClothaire II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Noted events in his life were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Fact 1: Acceded: 613. King of Neustria. Sole King 613-629.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fact 2: Had Three Wives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Chlothar married Brynhild.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children from this marriage were:
2 CONT
2 CONT         i. Merovech of The Franks ()
2 CONT         ii. St. Ode of The Franks ()
2 CONT        iii. Charibert II of The Franks Duc d'Aquitaine (died in 632)
2 CONT
2 CONT Chlothar next married Haldetrude Haldetrude. Haldetrude was born about585 and died in 604, about age 19.
2 CONT
2 CONT Noted events in her life were:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Ref: Royalty For Comm. 1995, 303-48.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children from this marriage were:
2 CONT
2 CONT i. Dagobert I of Austrasia King (born about 605 - died in 639)
