1 NAME Maldras
2 GIVN Maldras
1 NAME Maldras, king of the Suevi
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE FEB 460
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maldras
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Maldras''' (or Masdras) (died February 460) was the Suevic king of Galicia from 456 until his death. After the execution of Rechiar by the victorious Visigoths, the Suevi are said to have established Maldras on the throne. Duri
2 CONC ng his reign the Suevic nation became fragmented.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maldras was the son of Massilia (or Massila) and was not said to be related to the dynasty of Hermeric, which had ruled the Suevi since 406.[1] The wording of the contemporary chronicler Hydatius may be taken to signify that the S
2 CONC uevi population had some part in electing Maldras.[1] They certainly had a part in dividing the kingdom in 457, when part of them refused to accept him as their leader and chose instead Framta.[1] The two Suevic kings acted indepe
2 CONC ndently and on Framta's death within a few months his followers are found led by Rechimund, though scholars dispute whether or not the two parties rejoined.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 457, while Framta was still ruling, Maldras led his people in a large raid on Lusitania.[2] They sacked Lisbon by pretending to come in peace and, once admitted by the citizens, plundering the city.[3] Maldras is also accused o
2 CONC f having murdered his brother. In 458 he received envoys from the Visigoths and the Vandals.
2 CONT
2 CONT His people continued to plunder western Lusitania until Maldras was strangled, perhaps by his own men, in February 460.[2] Maldras' people turned to Frumar as their war-leader then.[2] Afterwards Remismund became king and reunited
2 CONC  the Suevic people. He is claimed by Isidore of Seville to be a son of Maldras, but there is some doubt on this.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/VANDALS,%20SUEVI,%20VISIGOTHS.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT *1.         MASSILA .  m ---.  The name of Massila's wife or concubine is not known.  Massila & his [wife] had two children:
2 CONT **a)         MALDRA (-killed Feb 460).  He succeeded in 456 as '''MALDRA King of the Suevi in Spain'''.  Isidor's Historia Gothorum, Wandalorum, Sueborum records that "Maldram Massilæ filium" succeeded as King of the Suevi in Spai
2 CONC n after the death of Requiario but that he was soon killed[89].  The Chronicon of Bishop Idatius records that “Rechiario” was killed in Dec 456 and that “Rex Theudoricus” succeeded “de Gallæcia ad Lusitaniam” but that the Suevi “i
2 CONC n extrema parte Gallæciæ” installed “Massiliæ filium…Maldram” as their king[90].  The Chronicon of Bishop Idatius records that “Maldras” was murdered in Feb 460[91]. 
2 CONT **b)         son (-killed 459).  The Chronicon of Bishop Idatius records that “Maldras” killed “germanium suum fratrem” in 459 and invaded “Portucale castrum”[92]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
