1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Albéric de Landen'''. In an article about his son, St. Gregory of Utrecht, ''Catholic Encyclopedia'' says, "[Gregory's] father Alberic was the son of Addula, who, as widow, was Abbess of Pfalzel (Palatiolum) nea
2 CONC r Trier. On account of the similarity of names, and in consequence of a forged last will, Addula has been frequently confounded with Adala (Adela), daughter of Dagobert II of Austrasia--thus falsely making Gregory a scion of the r
2 CONC oyal house of the Merovingians." [http://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07021a.htm "St. Gregory of Utrecht" in ''Catholic Encyclopedia''].
