1 NOTE He was Duke of Allemania, Suevia and Upper Germany from 662 to 690. He obtained the Duchy of Alsace in 662.
1 NOTE He was Duke of Allemania, Suevia and Upper Germany from 662 to 690. He obtained the Duchy of Alsace in 662.
1 NOTE Source: THE RUFUS PARKS PEDIGREE by Brian J.L. Berry, chart on page  57.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 58:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  ADALRIC (ATTICH, ETTIC, ETHIC), b. bef. 662-d. 20 Feb. 690; head of the Alsatian House of the Ethiconides, duke of Alsace from 662 and Mayor of the Palace and Bishop of Autun 663-77, so that he would have served under the Mero
2 CONC vingian Kings Clothaire III, Childeric II and Thierry (Theuderic) III.  An account of the sainthood of his daughter Odile (Ottilia), suggests that he also had two sons.  Allegedly she was born blind by at least the year 678, and w
2 CONC as rejected by her father.  Her mother, BERSWINDE arranged for her care at a distant nunnery where she accepted Christianity and miraculously recovered her sight.  When a brother, Hugh, invited her to return home, ADALRIC struck h
2 CONC im dead, relented and gave her his castle at Hohenburg and turned it into a monastery where she became abbess.  Her shrine and abbey were objects of great devotion during the Middle Ages, and were favored by CHARLEMAGNE and many o
2 CONC f his successors.  She was venerated as the patron saint of Alsace from the 16C. Her mother, BERSWINDE, was an aunt of Count WARINUS. 
2 CONT
2 CONT !Availability: The libraries of Ken, Karen, Kristen, Kevin, Brian, Amy, Adam and FAL.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "Ancestral Roots of Sixty Colonists" by Frederick Lewis Weis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 154 line (180-1):
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.    Adelric, (or Ethic), obtained the Duchy of Alsace 662, d. 20 Feb. 690, head of the Alsatian House of the Ethiconides, Duke of Alsace 662-690; m. Berswinde.
