1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Batticho, son of Eticho (Aldaric I), Duke of Alsace (d. after 04 Sep 677 or after 25 Jun 692) and his wife Berswinde.
2 CONT
2 CONT m. UNKNOWN. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Boro (d. after 748)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ALSACE.htm#Etichodiedafter677
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ETICHO [Chadicho/Adalrico], son of LEUDESIUS maior domus & his wife --- (-after 4 Sep 677, maybe after 25 Jun 692).  … m BERSWINDA, daughter of -  The Cronica Hohenburgensis records the marriage of "Athicum seu Adalricum" and "Ber
2 CONC swindam…filiam sororis sancti Leodegarii, sororem videlicet regina"[15].  The Chronicon Ebersheimense names "Berswindam, filiam sororis Leodegarii episcopi…et Garini comitis Pictavensis, sororem videlicet regina" as the wife of At
2 CONC hicus[16]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eticho/Adalrico & his wife had five children: 
2 CONT *1.         ADALBERT [I] .  A 15th century genealogy included in the cartulary of Honau names "Adelbertum, Battichonem, Hugonem, Hechonem" as the four sons of "Adalrici ducis vel alio nomine Hettichonis"[17].  Duke in Alsace.  He 
2 CONC is named "ducis Adelberti" in the Annales Murbacenses as father of Eberhard[18]. 
2 CONT * 2.         BATTICHO .  A 15th century genealogy included in the cartulary of Honau names "Adelbertum, Battichonem, Hugonem, Hechonem" as the four sons of "Adalrici ducis vel alio nomine Hettichonis"[19].  m -.  
2 CONT * 3.         HUGO [I] .  A 15th century genealogy included in the cartulary of Honau names "Adelbertum, Battichonem, Hugonem, Hechonem" as the four sons of "Adalrici ducis vel alio nomine Hettichonis"[28].  m -.  The name of Hugo´
2 CONC s wife is not known.   …
2 CONT * 4.         HAICHO (-after 17 Sep 723).  .. m -.  The name of Haicho´s wife is not known.  Haicho & his wife had two children:  ..
2 CONT * 5.         ODILA (-after 28 Dec 708).  The Cronica Hohenburgensis names "Odilam" as the daughter of "Athicum seu Adalricum" & his wife, recording that she was born blind and recovered her sight after baptism by "Herhardo Ratispo
2 CONC nensem episcopo et Hylelulfo Treverensi"[53].  A 15th century genealogy included in the cartulary of Honau names "sanctam Otiliam" as the daughter of "Adalrici ducis vel alio nomine Hettichonis"[54].  The testament of “Odilia…abba
2 CONC tissa in Hohenburc”, dated 28 Dec 708, names “pater meus dux Adalricus”[55]. 
2 CONT ----
