1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [LAMBERT [II] (-before 741).  According to Europäische Stammtafeln[524], Lambert [II] was the son of Chrodbert [II] but no reference to Lambert or this alleged relationship has been found in any of the primary sour
2 CONC ces so far consulted.] m ---.  '''The name of Lambert’s wife is not known.'''  Lambert [II] & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          ROBERT [I] ([700/10]-before 764).  The third continuator of the Gesta Abbatum Trudonensium names "Robertus comes vel dux Hasbanie" in 715, and quotes a charter dated 7 Apr 742 under which "Robertus comes, filius condam
2 CONC  Lamberti" donated property "in villa…Sarcinio…in pago Hasbaniensi…[et] Halon, Scaffnis, Felepa et Marholt" to St Trudon[525].  Comte de Hesbaie.  Comes palatinus 741/42.  Graf im Oberrheingau und Wormsgau. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FRANKSMaiordomi.htm#_Toc359686226
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Chrotlind''' might have been a daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Th-od-ric-III-King-of-the-Franks/6000000002228883916 Théodéric III] (de Vajay, Chaume & Kelley), although she is not named by Schwennicke or Isenburg. ''How
2 CONC ever, the identity of her mother is disputed.''
2 CONT
2 CONT # Maurice Chaume says her mother was Théodéric's wife [http://www.geni.com/people/Chrothildis-de-Metz/6000000002106239063 Chrothildis] (''Études carolingiennes I: La famille de saint Guillaume de Gellone''). 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Prof. David Kelley says, "In fact, I have found a considerable amount of data suggesting that Chrotlind, the mother of the Count Theuderic of 720, was indeed the daughter of Theuderic III (by his wife [http://www.geni.com/people
2 CONC /Saint-Amalberge-of-Neustria-640-692/6000000000957281690 Saint Amalaberga]) and was the wife of Lantpert and mother of Rotpert, ancestor of the Robertins. This material involves considerations of onomastics, property inheritance, 
2 CONC and the sometimes dubious texts of the lives of the Frankish saints, and is both too involved and too extensive to present here...." (David H. Kelley, "Holy Blood, Holy Grail: Two Reviews").
2 CONT
2 CONT For a discussion of this issue, see "Meroving Line 2" (April 19, 1999) at soc.genealogy.medieval <https://groups.google.com/forum/?hl=en#!searchin/soc.genealogy.medieval/chrotlind/soc.genealogy.medieval/ETIm6QrZNaw/2nj2kFUl8FUJ>
