2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lope_D%C3%ADaz_I_de_Haro Wiki - Lope Díaz I de Haro]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lope Diaz de Haro I (? - † May 6 of 1170). Son of Diego López de Haro I and Ms Almicena. Was fourth Lord of Biscay between 1124 and 1170.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Life
2 CONT
2 CONT He was faithful to Urraca of Leon and Castile as had been his father, which could not intervene in La Rioja, which had seized the husband of Urraca, Alfonso I of Aragon, even though after the death of this, his son Alfonso claimed
2 CONC  the throne of Castile. Lope At this time lost the lordship over castles Haro and Buradón for the Aragonese.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1130 he settled with his family in the town of Najera, where he will live his successors to the Lordship of Biscay, to the entrance of the first woman to him, after the death of Diego Lopez de Haro V childless. In this village 
2 CONC improved Abbey Hospital, which had begun to build the King Alfonso VII.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Alfonso of Aragon in 1134 without issue, along with other Lope Rioja Najera rebounded the kingdom to give to Alfonso VII, King of Leon. As a reward Alfonso was given the title of count and confirmed in the lords
2 CONC hip of the town of Haro, as reflected by a privilege given by the October 10, 1134, which gave the monastery of San Millán various churches and estates, in which began: "Lope Diaz confirmed by his great qual ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1141 was awarded to Santo Domingo de la Calzada privilege of population, appearing in all documentation Lope as governor of La Rioja.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was entitled Alferez Real, as it appears since 1158.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Alfonso VII, Lopez continued to serve his successors, first to Sancho el Deseado and only a year later Alfonso VIII of Castile, son of the former which was only three years old when he ascended the throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1163 building on the minority of Alfonso VIII, Sancho VI the Wise occupy part of the territory of La Rioja, leaving Logroño, Trains, Navarrete, Ausejo, Arnedo, Quel and Resa in the hands of Navarra. A Lope as governor of La Rio
2 CONC ja touch you face them in 1163 and 1167, and afterwards his heir in office, his son Pedro Ruiz in 1174.
2 CONT
2 CONT He coined a currency called lobis or Lobres, referring to the wolves the symbol of his lineage that contained therein.
2 CONT
2 CONT =============================
2 CONT Lope Díaz I de Haro (fallecido 6 de mayo de 1170​), llamado el Rubio o el de Nájera, fue hijo de Diego López I de Haro y la condesa María Sánchez, hija del conde Sancho Sánchez de Erro y la condesa Elvira García, hija legítima del
2 CONC  conde García Ordóñez. Fue el IV señor de Vizcaya entre los años 1124 y 1170.
2 CONT
2 CONT En 1169 él y su mujer, donaron a unas monjas benedictinas de Santo Domingo de la Calzada unas tierras en Cañas , para ayudarlas a construir allí una abadía con la condición de que pasasen a cumplir la orden cisterciense . Thus beg
2 CONC an building the monastery of Santa Maria de San Salvador de Cañas.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lope_D%C3%ADaz_I_de_Haro
2 CONT ===================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT Lope came in 1169 purse Zorita with other men, to support the King Alfonso VIII, without this I asked him. Do not let the king to hand him a salary for their assistance, so in gratitude I give the government of the town of Najera,
2 CONC  Earl besides this.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1170 and was buried in the cloister of the Knights of the monastery of Santa Maria la Real de Najera.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Edit] Nicknames
2 CONT
2 CONT He called himself Count D Lope Diaz de Haro, having resided in the town of Haro be furnished after his father. The nickname "Haro" would be used since then by their descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the book History of Spain's King Alfonso X the Wise is referred to as Count Don Lope de Navarra, because they settled in La Rioja, which had belonged to the kingdom of Navarre.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is also sometimes named as Don Lope de Najera, that tube in government ownership and the town of Najera, of great importance for having been Head of the Kingdom.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Edit] Descendants
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Aldonza Rodriguez de Castro (some call Mencia) daughter of Rui Fernandez Calvo and Stephanie Perez de Trava, taking by children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Diego López de Haro II, his successor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lope Lopez. Lord of Miranda de Ebro and Almenara married Maria de Urgel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alonso Lopez de Haro. Commander of San Salvador de Soria, the Order of Calatrava.
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin Lopez de Haro
2 CONT
2 CONT Probably had another son named Lope Diaz de Haro would have been bishop of Segovia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Urraca López de Haro, third wife of King Ferdinand.
2 CONT
2 CONT Toda Lopez de Haro, who died on December 1 of 1122
2 CONT
2 CONT Inheritance
2 CONT
2 CONT At his death he divided his estate, leaving his son Pedro Ruiz as governor of the Rioja Alta. His son Lope Lopez continue with the office of Mayor Murphy and his firstborn Diego Castilla lord of Biscay.
2 CONT
