2 CONT From http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SOUTHERN%20ITALY,%20PRE-NORMAN.htm#_Toc375827717
2 CONT
2 CONT  Prince Adelchis & his wife Adeltruda had [ten] children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 '''AIO''' (-Oct 891) The Cronica de Monasterio Sanctissimi Benedicti record that "Aio frater Radelchis" succeeded in 884 as AIO Prince of Benevento[237]. The Byzantines, under Nikephoros Phokas, launched a major campaign in sout
2 CONC hern Italy between late 883 and 885, recapturing most of Calabria from Benevento and Salerno[238]  Byzantine forces attempted to capture Beneventan towns in [888] and Prince Aio responded by seizing Bari, although the town was rec
2 CONC aptured within a year. This was followed by an invasion of Beneventan territory by Naples[239]Â  The Cronica de Monasterio Sanctissimi Benedicti record war between Capua and Naples "in Liburia ad sanctum Cartium" in the second yea
2 CONC r of the reign of Atenolf Count of Capua, that Atenolf "indictione 6 post dies undecim" captured "Berelais", but that in the same week he was defeated by "Aio princeps cum quodam patricio Constantinopolitano"[240] "Aio Langobardor
2 CONC um gentis princeps" donated property which belonged to "Potoni fi[lii] Potitionis infra finibus Alifanis et Telesinis", for which he had killed "dom Adelchis princip genitori nostro", to Montecassino, at the request of "Ladelchis 
2 CONC germani nostri", by charter dated May [885][241] The Chonicon Monasterii Beneventani records the death in Oct 891 of "Aio Princeps"[242Â  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' --- The name of Aio's wife is not known.  Prince Aio & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         URSUS (-892 or after). .. ... 
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aiulf_II_of_Benevento
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Aiulf II''' (also Aio, Ajo, or Aione) reigned as Prince of Benevento (884 – 891) during a particularly stormy period for the independent principality.
2 CONT
2 CONT He deposed his elder brother, Radelchis II, in 884 or 885 at a time when the Byzantines, under Nicephorus Phocas the Elder, had been reconquering Calabria since 883. Nicephorus concentrated his attacks on territory around Benevent
2 CONC o and Aiulf responded by capturing Bari. Bari was recaptured within the year.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aiulf also had to deal with an invasion by the Duchy of Naples.
