1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT VICOMTES de MÂCON
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BURGUNDIAN NOBILITY.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         RACULF (-after 893).  A document of Lothar II King of Lotharingia dated 865 relating to the king's reacceptance of his wife Theotberga names "de comitibus Milo, Ratherius, Erlandus, Theutmarus, Weremboldus, Rocolfus com
2 CONC es" as those swearing allegiance[1404].  Vicomte de Mâcon .  Guillaume "le Pieux" Duke of Aquitaine appointed Raculf as Vicomte de Mâcon.  "Raculfi vicecomitis" signed a charter dated [1/9] Nov 893 under which "Hava…Christi famula
2 CONC " gave "quondam villam meam…Cluniacum…in pago Matisconense" to "Wilelmo fratri meo"[1405].  m ---.  The name of Raculf's wife is not known.  Raculf & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         TOLANA de Mâcon .  The genealogy of the Comtes de Mâcon, included in the cartulary of Saint-Vincent de Mâcon, names "Albericus Narbonensis" and his marriage to "filiam Raculfi vicecomitis post mortem domini Bernonis Mat
2 CONC iscensis episcopi", after which he made himself first Comte de Mâcon[1406].  "Tolosane" is named as wife of Alberic in a charter of her son Letaud dated [12 Apr] 935 and "Etolane" mother of Letaud in the latter's charter dated 8 M
2 CONC ay [955][1407].  942.  "Letaudus comes et uxor mea Berta" donated property to Saint-Vincent-de-Mâcon for the souls of "patris mei Alberici…et matris mee Tolane…Irmengardis quondam uxoris sue" by charter dated to [941] subscribed b
2 CONC y "Alberici filii sui"[1408].  m AUBRY [Alberic] de Narbonne Comte de Mâcon, son of (-[10 Sep] 945, bur Besançon Saint-Etienne). 
2 CONT
2 CONT brother of Raculf?
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         ETIENNE (-after 923).  Vicomte de Mâcon.  Vicomte Etienne subscribed a charter dated to before 923 relating to Saint-Vincent de Mâcon[1409]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
