1 NAME Hugues I, II. seigneur des Baux
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 981
2 PLAC France
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 21 OCT 1059
1 OCCU sire des Baux (2e, Hugues I, après 1000-après 1059), Seigneur d'Orange
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Voir [http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugues_Ier_des_Baux '''Wikipedia...''']
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/provaixmar.htm#HuguesIIBauxB
2 CONT
2 CONT '''HUGUES [II] [de Baux],''' son of [GUILLAUME & his wife ---] (-after 13 Oct 1059).  As explained above, it is unlikely from a chronological point of view that Hugues, husband of Inauris, was the same person as Hugues [I] who is 
2 CONC named above, although the reference to “castrum...Balcius” relating to Hugues [I] (see above) indicates that they were related.  An undated charter records a donation made to Marseille Saint-Victor in the presence "domni Ugonis de
2 CONC  Balcio et sue mulieris Inauris..."[843].  A charter dated 1033 records that "Gauzfredus et Ugo et Pontius et Ot[b]ertus cum uxoribus suis cum filiorum illorum" built "ecclesiam...sancte Marie [et] sancti Johannis Babtiste"[844]. 
2 CONC  "Domnus Ugo et uxor sua Inaurs" donated land “in comitatu Arelatense in valle Marignana in locum...Aquosa” to Marseille Saint-Victor by charter dated 19 Jan 1045[845].  "Gauzfredus et Vugo et uxores nostre…Scocia cum filiis nostr
2 CONC is Vuillelmo et Pontio, et Inauris cum suis filiis Vuillelmo et Vugone et Pontio, et Vuilelmus juvenis nepos noster et uxor sua Adalgrada et filii sui Fulcho et Gauzfredus et Pontius et Aicardus, necnon et Amelius Fossanus cum sua
2 CONC  uxore Garsia" donated "ecclesiam sancte Marie [et] sancti Johannis...in territorio castri...Sparronis" to Marseille Saint-Victor by charter dated 13 Oct 1059[846]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (after [1035]) INAURIS d'Apt, daughter of GUILLAUME Seigneur d'Apt & his wife Adelais --- (-after 13 Oct 1059).  "Willelmus et uxor mea Adelaicis...et filii nostri Rostagnus et Wilelmus et filie Inauris et Constancia" dona
2 CONC ted property “in comitatu Cabilonensi...ecclesia sancti Michahelis...in vaslle Liminica...” to Saint-Victor de Marseille by charter dated 30 Nov 1031, subscribed by “Inauris mater Wilelmi...”[847].  "Willelmus et uxor mea Adelaici
2 CONC s...et filii nostri Rostagnus et Willelmus et filie Inauris et Constancia" confirmed “in comitatu Cabilonensi...ecclesia sancti Michahelis in Laus...” to Saint-Victor de Marseille by charter dated 24 Dec [1035][848].  Inauris and 
2 CONC her sons Guillaume-Hugues, Pons and Hugues, sons of Hugues, donated property to the monastery of Saint-Césaire by undated charter dated to [1026/59][849].  "Domnus Ugo et uxor sua Inaurs" donated land “in comitatu Arelatense in va
2 CONC lle Marignana in locum...Aquosa” to Marseille Saint-Victor by charter dated 19 Jan 1045[850].  "Gauzfredus et Vugo et uxores nostre…Inauris cum suis filiis Vuillelmo et Vugone et Pontio..." donated "ecclesiam sancte Marie [et] san
2 CONC cti Johannis...in territorio castri...Sparronis" to Marseille Saint-Victor by charter dated 13 Oct 1059[851]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Hugues [II] & his wife had three children: 
