1 OCCU Sire des Baux (3e, Guillaume I, après 1059-1110), Seigneur de Berre
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/provaixmar.htm#HuguesIIBauxB
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         '''GUILLAUME-HUGUES de Baux''' ([1036/45]-after 1091).  Inauris and her sons Guillaume-Hugues, Pons and Hugues, sons of Hugues donated property to the monastery of Saint-Césaire by charter dated to [1026/59][852].  Cons
2 CONC idering the dates of the documents in which their sons are named, it is unlikely that Guillaume-Hugues could have been born much earlier than [1030/45].  Guillaume-Hugues and his wife Vierne bought property from Pons de Rians and 
2 CONC his wife Adalgarde by charter dated 1046[853], although the dating of this charter is suspect given Guillaume-Hugues's likely birth date range.  "Gauzfredus et Vugo et uxores nostre…Inauris cum suis filiis Vuillelmo et Vugone et P
2 CONC ontio..." donated "ecclesiam sancte Marie [et] sancti Johannis...in territorio castri...Sparronis" to Marseille Saint-Victor by charter dated 13 Oct 1059[854].  Guillaume-Hugues donated property, previously owned by his father Hug
2 CONC ues de Baux, to the church of Saint-Trophime d'Arles, with the consent of Vierne his wife and their sons Hugues and Raymond by charter dated 1091[855].  A charter dated May 1110 refers to earlier donations to Lérins by "Guillelmus
2 CONC  Ugonis et uxor eius Vierna et filiis eius Raimundus" and the current donation by "Raimundi de Balcio et mater sua"[856].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' VIERNE, daughter of --- (-after May 1110).  Guillaume-Hugues and his wife Vierne bought property from Pons de Rians and his wife Adalgarde by charter dated 1046[857].  Guillaume-Hugues, Vierne his wife and Hugues their son
2 CONC  donated property to the church of Arles by charter dated 1088[858].  Guillaume-Hugues donated property, previously owned by his father Hugues de Baux, to the church of Saint-Trophime d'Arles, with the consent of Vierne his wife a
2 CONC nd their sons Hugues and Raymond by charter dated 1091[859].  A charter dated May 1110 refers to earlier donations to Lérins by "Guillelmus Ugonis et uxor eius Vierna et filiis eius Raimundus" and the current donation by "Raimundi
2 CONC  de Balcio et mater sua"[860]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Guillaume & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
