1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Belgian sources sthat that Vincent Vadelgarus was born in Strépy, Belgium, sometime in the late 6th or early 7th century; died 677 in Soignies; and was a Benedictine monk who established two monasteries in Hainaut.
2 CONC  One of these was at Hautmont (now in France), the other at Soignies.
2 CONT
2 CONT Madelgarus was sent by Dagobert I to Ireland. His wife was Waltrude.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, according to John O'Hanlon, his real name was Maelceadar (Mael Ceadar), he was a Count of Hainault, and he was a native of Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vincent_Madelgarus
