2 CONT Ramiro II de Aragón apodado el Monje (24 de abril de 1086 - 16 de agosto de 1157), rey de Aragón entre 1134 y 1157.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ramiro «Munken» var konge av Aragon 1134 - 1137.
2 CONT
2 CONT Han var først munk, ble konge av Aragon i 1134, men resignerte 11.11.1137. 121
2 CONT
2 CONT 121 Erich Brandenburg: Die Nachkommen Karls des Grossen. Leipzig 1935. Mogens Bugge: Våre forfedre, nr. 1070. Bent og
2 CONT
2 CONT        Vidar Billing Hansen: Rosensverdslektens forfedre, side 14, 16.
2 CONT
2 CONT   Ramiro II Sánchez "el Monje", rey de Aragón also went by the name of Ramiro "the Monk". He was born in 1075. The third son.3 He was the son of Sancho I, rey de Aragón y de Pamplona and Felicité de Roucy.2 Ramiro II Sánchez "el M
2 CONC onje", rey de Aragón was was a monk, known as San Pedro el Viego de Huesca between 1093 and 1134. He was bishop-elect of Barbastro before 1134.3 He selected by the Aragonese nobles to replace his brother, he renounced his vows, ma
2 CONC rried, and ascended the throne of Aragon in 1134.3,4 King of Aragón at Spain between 1134 and 13 November 1137.3,5,6 He witnessed the will of Alfonso I Sánchez "el Batallador", rey de Aragón y Navarra in 1134; He left his kingdom 
2 CONC to an order of Knights, something which the Aragonese nobles rejected and so they chose Alfonso's brother, Ramiro, to succeeded him.4 Ramiro II Sánchez "el Monje", rey de Aragón married Agnes de Poitiers, daughter of Guillaume IX 
2 CONC "le Troubadour", duc de Guyenne, comte de Poitiers and Mahaut, comtesse de Toulouse, in November 1135 at Jaca, Huesca Province, Aragón, Spain; His 2nd. Her 2nd (widowed).7 Ramiro II Sánchez "el Monje", rey de Aragón was the Ramiro
2 CONC  II of the Bell of Heusca legend (Ramiro II's 12th-century massacre of mutinous nobles). He abdicated in favour of his daughter and son-in-law in 1137.3 He was returned to the cloister in 1137. He died in 1157 at Huesca, Aragón, S
2 CONC pain, at age 82 years.2
2 CONT
