2 CONT
2 CONT *https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berta_(reina_de_Le%C3%B3n)  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT # Según [https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pelayo_de_Oviedo ''Pelayo, obispo de Oviedo''](...-1153) continuando la Crónica de Sampiro, Berta era «[https://www.geni.com/path/Boson-d-Arles-margrave-of-Tuscany+is+related+to+Guglielmo-I-i
2 CONC l-Grande-conte-di-Borgogna?from=6000000007043482057&path_type=blood&to=6000000000716998561 natural de Toscana]». ​[2][3]  
2 CONT # /!\ El [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Szabolcs_de_Vajay ''genealogista Szabolcs de Vajay''](1921-2010) opina que fue hija de [https://www.geni.com/people/Amedeo-II-conte-di-Savoia/6000000000196218118  Amadeo II de Saboya],[4]​ 
2 CONT # mientras que otras fuentes aseguran que en realidad era hija de [https://www.geni.com/people/Guglielmo-I-il-Grande-conte-di-Borgogna/6000000000716998561 '''Guillermo I de Borgoña'''], conde de Borgoña y Mâcon.'' ''' [a] ''' ''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ''  [2] Martínez Díez, 2003, p. 162.''
2 CONT ''   [3] Elorza et al., 1990, p. 55.''
2 CONT ''  '''[a]''' En la Crónica General, dice que «don Enrique, el que casó con doña Teresa, hija de Alfonso VI, tuvo a doña Berta como natural de Borgoña». En un diploma datado el XV kalendas noviembre de 1096 en la Colección Diplomá
2 CONC tica de San Martín de Jubia (977-1199), documento XV, p. 67, consta en la datación «Regnante rex Adefonsus in Toleto et coniuge sua de genere francorum.»
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT _ _ _  _ _ _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _  _ _ _ _
2 CONT {Solution 1 & 3 are not contradictory, they match because [https://www.geni.com/path/Boson-d-Arles-margrave-of-Tuscany+is+related+to+Guglielmo-I-il-Grande-conte-di-Borgogna?from=6000000007043482057&path_type=blood&to=6000000000716
2 CONC 998561 Guglielmo I "il Grande" conte di Borgogna is Boson d'Arles, margrave of Tuscany's third great grandson!]  }
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bertha''' (c. 1070- 1098/1100), wife of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Alfonso-VI-el-Bravo-rey-de-Le%C3%B3n-y-de-Castilla/6000000000665380375 Alfonso VI]'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT "By April 1095, Alfonso married Bertha. Chroniclers report her as being from Tuscany, Lombardy, or alternatively, say she was French. Several theories have been put forward regarding her origin. Based on political considerations, 
2 CONC proposals make her daughter of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/William-the-Great-Count-of-Burgundy/6000000000716998561 William I, Count of Burgundy]''' or of ''[http://www.geni.com/people/Am%C3%A9d%C3%A9e-II-comte-de-Savoie/6000000
2 CONC 000196218118 Amadeus II of Savoy]''. She had no children and died in late 1099 (Alfonso first appears without her in mid-January 1100)."
2 CONT
