1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ageltrude
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/ageltrude_(Dizionario-Biografico)_
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Adelchis, prince of Benevento, and Adeltrude, she was a Langobard and married with Wido III of the Widonides, marquis of Camerino, in the 880s. Soon she bore him a child, Lambert II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wido III had a brilliant rise inheriting the duchy of Spoleto in 882/3, bdding for the crown of West Francia in 888, conquering the crown of Italy in 889 and the imperial one in 891. He died, however, in 894, leaving a young heir.
2 CONC  Ageltrude stepped in as regent of her son, had pope Formosus forced to recognise him emperor, and directed the supporters of her family in a war against Berengar of Friuli, ultimately preserving the kingdom for her son, who died 
2 CONC in 898 without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are few information about the destiny of Ageltrude after that: Spoleto and Camerino lost to vassals of Berengar and other properties taken by enemies, she might have returned to Benevento under the protection of her family. 
2 CONC She died on August 27th, 923.
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT GUIDO (855-River Taro 12 Dec 894, bur Parma Cathedral). The Chronica Mon. Casinensis names "Lambertum ducem et fratrem eius Guidonem" in 876[941]. The Gesta regum Francorum names "Wito filius Lantberti" when recording that he prop
2 CONC osed himself in 888 as king of "Galliam Belgicam necnon Provinciam"[942]. He became Duke of Camerino in 876, and succeeded his nephew in [882/83] as GUIDO III Duke of Spoleto[943]. He was called to France by nobles opposed to Empe
2 CONC ror Charles III "le Gros", and consecrated King of France at Langres by Bishop Gilon in [Jan/Feb] 888. He returned to Italy after the election of Eudes as King of France 29 Feb 888. He was elected GUIDO I King of Italy at Pavia 12
2 CONC  Feb 889, in opposition to Berengario Marchese di Friulia. During this time he transferred the duchy of Spoleto to his [cousin] Duke Guido IV. Crowned Emperor at Rome 21 Feb 891 by Pope Stephen V[944]. "Vuido et Lantbertus…imperat
2 CONC ores augusti" granted "cortem…Lemennis in comitatu Bergomensi" to "Cohunradum…patruum ac patruelem nostrum…marchionem…et uxori eius Ermengundi et filiis…eorum", at the request of "Ageltrudim…coniugem nostrum imperatricem augustam"
2 CONC , by charter dated 1 May 892[945]. He died after a blood haemorrhage. m ([875/76]) '''AGELTRUDA of Benevento, daughter of ADELCHIS Prince of Benevento & his wife --- (-after 27 Aug 923).''' Herimannus names "Angildruda" widow of G
2 CONC uido and mother of Lambert, but does not give her origin[946]. The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified. "Vuido…imperator augustus" confirmed earlier donations to the church of Parma by "coniugi 
2 CONC nostræ Ageltrudi" by charter dated 21 Feb 891[947]. The Annales Fuldenses name "Ageldrudis vidua Widonis" in 896[948]. A document dated 1 Dec 898 records a peace agreement reached between Berengar King of Italy and "Ageltrudæ reli
2 CONC cta quondam Widoni imperatoris" and "filio eius Lamberto [imperatoris]"[949]. Duke Guido & his wife had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT i) LAMBERT ([876]-near Marengo 15 Oct 898, bur Piacenza). Lambert is named as son of Guido in the Guidonis Chronica[950]. His father appointed him as LAMBERT associate King of Italy in May 891, and 30 Apr 892 he was crowned co-Emp
2 CONC eror by Pope Formosius[951]. "Vuido et Lantbertus…imperatores augusti" granted "cortem…Lemennis in comitatu Bergomensi" to "Cohunradum…patruum ac patruelem nostrum…marchionem…et uxori eius Ermengundi et filiis…eorum", at the reque
2 CONC st of "Ageltrudim…coniugem nostrum imperatricem augustam", by charter dated 1 May 892[952]. "Lanbertus cæsar imperator augustus" granted property "in comitatu et pago Placentino" to "fideli nostro Amalgiso", at the request of "Evu
2 CONC rardus comes" and with the advice of "Sigefredi comitis", by charter dated Jan 895[953]. Supported by his mother, Lambert took advantage of the illness of Emperor Arnulf and was recognised as King of Italy by Pope Stephen VI in 89
2 CONC 6, confirmed at the Synode of Ravenna in May 898[954]. He died following a fall from his horse[955].
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CENTRAL%20ITALY.htm#LambertIdied836B
