2 CONT
2 CONT The following is a post-em by Curt Hofemann, curt_hofemann@yahoo.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT ID: I01374 Bernard II Plantevelue Comte d'Auvergne
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard was Count of Aquitaine and the Auvergne, Marquis of Gothie, Count of Autun, Count of Rodez.
2 CONT
2 CONT As far as Count of Aquitaine, Ronald F. Malan in _The Genealogist_ vol. xi in an article titled: "The Ancestry of Dhouda, Duchess of Septamani" did state this. To my knowledge, Aquitaine in this period was a duchy not a county, th
2 CONC e duke being Charles III son of Charles II king of Franks, HRE (grandson of Charlemagne). Note: I do not know if there was a "County of Aquitaine" within the duchy, but in this period of the beginnings of titles & meanings of same
2 CONC , I’d think it doubtful.
2 CONT
2 CONT As to where the sources of the titles you give: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard Plantevelue Count of Auvergne [Ref: Bouchard, ES III:731, Dillange, Keats-Rohan Family Trees p247, Nat Taylor 23 May 1997, Nat Taylor-Sant Wm p205-223] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Count of Autun, Count of Auvergne and Rovergue, 872: Marquis of Toulouse [Ref: Moriarty p215]
2 CONT
2 CONT Barnard Hairyfoot, Count of Auvergne; styled Duke by 898 [Ref: McBride2] Note: considering that he died in 885/6… 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marquis of Gothie; Count of Autun, Count of Rodez [Ref: CP II:731, Keats-Rohan Family Trees p211-267]
2 CONT
2 CONT Dillange = Michael Dillange, Les comtes de Poitou, ducs d'Aquitaine (778-1204), Geste Editions, Geste Editions, 1996.
2 CONT
2 CONT Regards,
2 CONT
2 CONT Curt
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT Title: The Plantagenet Ancestry, by William Henry Turton, 1968
