2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard Plantapilosa or Bernard II of Auvergne (22 March 841 – 886[1]), or Plantevelue, son of Bernard of Septimania and Dhuoda, was the Count of Auvergne (as Bernard II) from 872 to his death. The Emperor Charles the Fat granted 
2 CONC him the title of Margrave of Aquitaine in 885.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family He married Ermengard, daughter of Bernard I of Auvergne (or perhaps of Guerin I). 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had at least two children:
2 CONT *William I of Aquitaine
2 CONT *Adelinda, who married Acfred I of Carcassonne
2 CONT
2 CONT Plantapilosa is often claimed to mean "Hairyfeet" or "Hairypaws".[2] This is based on the Latin meaning "sole of foot" of planta.
