2 CONT ** "The mint, a royal monopoly par excellence, is a good example. As early as 560-580, the first private minters did not hesitate to put their own names on coins in place of the king's name. Charlemagne in 790 reclaimed all his ri
2 CONC ghts in this respect and forbade individuals to strike coinage. But with Eudes, the first non-Carolingian king, the plundering returned, and a few years before 918 a former functionary, Guillaume, duke of Aquitaine, had a denier s
2 CONC truck at Brioude."
