1 OCCU Comte de Mâcon par mariage, Sgr de Salins, graaf van Mâcon
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BURGUNDIAN%20NOBILITY.htm 
2 CONT
2 CONT AUBRY [Alberic] de Narbonne, son of MAYEUL Vicomte de Narbonne & his wife --- (-[10 Sep] 945, bur Besançon Saint-Etienne).  A charter dated 15 Jun 911, under which Arnust Archibishop of Narbonne donated property to Saint-Paul de N
2 CONC arbonne, names "infantes Majolo vicecomite et uxori suæ Raymundæ...Walchario et...Albericho vicecomite", the wording implying that the parents were deceased at that date[1170].  A genealogy of the Comtes de Mâcon, included in the 
2 CONC cartulary of Saint-Vincent de Mâcon, names "Albericus Narbonensis" and refers to his marriage to "filiam Raculfi vicecomitis post mortem domini Bernonis Matiscensis episcopi", stating that he subsequently installed himself as firs
2 CONC t Comte de Mâcon[1171].  Comte de Mâcon, Sire de Bracon et de Salins.  "Berno episcopus" donated property to "Albericus comes" by charter dated "die Martis Kal Jan anno VIII regnante Rodulfo rege" [930] subscribed by "comes Letald
2 CONC us, uxor eius Berta"[1172], although, as noted below, the reference to Letaud's wife Berta suggests that this charter is misdated.  "Albericus comes" donated property to Saint-Vincent de Mâcon by charter dated [936/41] subscribed 
2 CONC by "Letaudi, Ermentrudis coniugis sue"[1173].  The necrology of Mâcon Cathedral records the death "IV Id Sep" of "Albericus comes"[1174], although this entry could alternatively refer to Count Aubry [II] (see below). 
2 CONT
2 CONT m TOLANA de Mâcon, daughter of RACULF Vicomte de Mâcon & his wife ---.  The genealogy of the Comtes de Mâcon, included in the cartulary of Saint-Vincent de Mâcon, names "Albericus Narbonensis" and refers to his marriage to "filiam
2 CONC  Raculfi vicecomitis post mortem domini Bernonis Matiscensis episcopi"[1175].  "Tolosane" is named as wife of Alberic in a charter of her son Letaud dated [12 Apr] 935 and "Etolane" mother of Letaud in the latter's charter dated 8
2 CONC  May [955][1176].  942.  "Letaudus comes et uxor mea Berta" donated property to Saint-Vincent-de-Mâcon for the souls of "patris mei Alberici…et matris mee Tolane…Irmengardis quondam uxoris sue" by charter dated to [941] subscribed
2 CONC  by "Alberici filii sui"[1177]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Aubry & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         LETAUD [Leotold] de Mâcon (915-3 Nov 961).  The genealogy of the Comtes de Mâcon, included in the cartulary of Saint-Vincent de Mâcon, names "Letaudus filius eius [Alberici Narbonensis]"[1178].  He succeeded his father 
2 CONC as Comte de Mâcon. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         HUMBERT de Mâcon (-before 958).  "Leutaldus atque et Umbertus filii…Alberici [comitis]" are named in an undated charter of Saint-Vincent de Mâcon[1179].  "Albericus comes…filii mei Letboldus et Umbertus" donated propert
2 CONC y to Saint-Vincent de Mâcon by charter dated [930][1180].  "Unberti fratris eius" consented to the donation of Letald Comte de Mâcon dated Feb 944[1181].  Sire de Salins. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         ADELA [Tolana] de Mâcon (-after Jun 944).  "Attale" is named as sister of "Letaudus comes" in the latter's donation to Cluny dated Jun 944[1182].  
2 CONT --------------------
