2 CONT Notes [JW]
2 CONT
2 CONT The following post to SGM, 16 May 1997, by Jim Stevens, indicates some of the debate and confusion among the sources as to the parents of Gerberga. I am sticking with Lietaud and Berta for a while.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: Jim Stevens (jstevens@IQUEST.NET)
2 CONT
2 CONT Subject: Parents of Gerberga, wife of Adalbert of Italy
2 CONT
2 CONT Newsgroups: soc.genealogy.medieval
2 CONT
2 CONT Date: 1997/05/16
2 CONT
2 CONT If one accepts Letalde as father, there is little consensus as to Gerberga's mother. Letalde m. (1) Ermengarde of Chalon; (2) Berta, possibly dau. of Garnier\Warinus, Count of Troyes; and (3) Richilde, dau. of Richard of Autun. Wi
2 CONC nkhaus lists Ermengarde as Gerberga's mother; Moriarty lists Berta; and ES (in vol. iii) lists either Berta or Richilde.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT Title: The Plantagenet Ancestry, by William Henry Turton, 1968
2 CONT
2 CONT Page: 6
2 CONT
2 CONT Title: Newsgroup: soc.genealogy.medieval, at groups - google.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Page: Jim Stevens, 16 May 1997
2 CONT
2 CONT Title: Newsgroup: soc.genealogy.medieval, at groups - google.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Page: Jim Stevens, 16 May 1997
2 CONT
