1 NAME Gilbert I, vicomte de Millau et Gévaudan
1 SEX M
1 OCCU unknown
2 PLAC Viscount of Carlat
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1110
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00120774&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gilbert_Ier_de_G%C3%A9vaudan
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert Ier de Gévaudan, ou Gilbert Ier de Millau, né vers 1055, assassiné en 1111 fut vicomte de Millau et de Lodève, puis comte de Gévaudan et, par mariage, comte de Provence. Il était fils de Bérenger, vicomte de Millau et de R
2 CONC odez, et d'Adèle de Carlat, vicomtesse de Carlat et de Lodève.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biographie
2 CONT
2 CONT Il partagea les titres de ses parents avec son frère Richard : il reçut Millau et Lodève, tandis que son frère eut Rodez et Carlat. Possédant différentes terres dans le Gévaudan, il en profita pour relever le titre de comte de Gév
2 CONC audan, tombé en désuétude depuis moins d'un siècle.
2 CONT
2 CONT En 1073, il épouse Gerberge (1060 † 1115), comtesse de Provence, fille de Bertrand, comte de Provence, et de Mathilde. Ils eurent au moins trois filles :
2 CONT  Douce (1090 † 1130), mariée en 1112 à Raimond Bérenger III (1082 † 1131), comte de Barcelone.
2 CONT  Étiennette († ap.1160), mariée à Raymond († 1150), seigneur des Baux. Leur fils émettra des prétentions sur le comté de Provence, débutant ainsi les Guerres Baussenques.
2 CONT  Sibylle mariée à Guy III de Sévérac1.
2 CONT
2 CONT En 1096, à l'occasion de la refondation de l'église de Toulon, Gilbert prévoit la création d'un monastère dans les îles Stoechades, ces trois îles qui se trouvent au sud d'Hyères. Après son assassinat survenu en 1111, ce furent sa
2 CONC  fille Douce et son gendre Raymond-Bérenger II qui lui succédèrent.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: Viscount of Milhaud  He shared the title of his parents and his brother Richard, he received Millau Lodeve, while his brother was Rodez Carlat . With different land in the Gevaudan, it took the opportunity to take the 
2 CONC title of Count of Gevaudan, obsolete less than a century.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1073, he married Gerberge ( 1060 † 1115) , Countess of Provence , daughter of Bertrand , Count of Provence, and Matilda . They had at least three daughters :
2 CONT
2 CONT Douce ( 1090 † 1130) , married in 1112 to Raymond Berenger III ( 1082 † 1131 ) , Count of Barcelona . Étiennette ( † ap.1160 ) , married to Raymond ( † 1150) , Lord of Baux . Their son will issue claims on the county of Provence a
2 CONC nd Baux starting the wars . Sibyl married to Guy III Sévérac1 .
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1096 , during the rebuilding of the church of Toulon , Gilbert provides for the establishment of a monastery in Stoechades islands, three islands that lie south of Hyères. After his assassination occurred in 1111 , it was his d
2 CONC aughter and son- Sweet Raymond Berenger II succeeded him 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/toulnoreast.htm#GilbertGevaudandied1110A
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         GIRBERT [Gilbert] (-[1110/3 Feb 1112]).  “Berengarius vicecomes de Cartlato et uxor mea Adila et mater uxoris meæ Nobilis” founded Montsalvy monastery, with the consent of “filii nostri Ricardus, Girbertus, Raimundus”,
2 CONC  by charter dated to [1060/71][1205].  “Allebertus de Caniliaco” swore allegiance to “Berengario nec ad filios tuos Ricard et Girbert” for the château of Canillac and others by undated charter, probably dated to [1080/97][1206].  
2 CONC Vicomte de Millau, de Gévaudan, et de Carlat (part).  "Gerberti vice comitis" subscribed the charter dated 1100 under which "Petrus Virgilius et frater meus Raimundus" donated "æcclesiam sancti Martini…Priscus…[et] mansum de Roque
2 CONC ta…" to Conques[1207].  "...Richardi vicecomitis et fratris eius Girberti..." subscribed the charter dated 1103 under which "nobili...Guidone" donated property to Saint-Chaffre[1208].  The Brevi Historia Comitum Provinciæ records 
2 CONC the death "circa 1110" of "Gilberto comite Provinciæ" who left a widow "Tiburgia…comitissa" and "Dulcia unica filia"[1209].  It should be noted that no primary source has been identified in which Girbert is recorded as comte de Pr
2 CONC ovence during his lifetime.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' GERBERGE Ctss de Provence, daughter of --- ([1078/84]-[3 Feb 1112/Jan 1118]).  The doubts concerning the parentage of Gerberge are discussed in the document PROVENCE.  The Brevi Historia Comitum Provinciæ records the death
2 CONC  "circa 1110" of "Gilberto comite Provinciæ" and that he was survived by his widow "Tiburgia…comitissa" and "Dulcia unica filia"[1210].  “Girberga comitissa” donated “comitatum...Provinciæ et Gavaldanensis et Carladensis et...hono
2 CONC rem...in comitatu Rutenensi”, which came to her “voce parentum meorum et largitione viri mei Girberti comitis patris tui”, to “Dulciæ filiæ meæ” by charter dated 1 Feb 1112[1211].  “Gerberga comitissa Arelatensis” granted “filiam 
2 CONC meam in conjugium...Dulcem” to “Raymundo Berengarii comiti”, together with “omni honore meo et cum...honore qui fuit Girberti comitis patris puellæ”, by charter dated 3 Feb 1112[1212].  -         COMTES de PROVENCE. 
