1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Clotilde, Queen Consort of the Visigoths
2 CONT * Reign: c. 526 – 531
2 CONT * Born: c. 500
2 CONT * Died: 531
2 CONT * Burial: Paris (basilique des Saints-Apôtres, later called the Abbey of Saint Genevieve) 
2 CONT * Father: King [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clovis_I Clovis I] of the Franks 
2 CONT * Spouse: 	[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amalaric Amalaric] (526–524)
2 CONT * Issue: none known 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clotilde_(died_531) '''Clotilde'''] (or Chrodechildis) (c. 500–531) was the daughter of King [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clovis_I Clovis I] of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franks Franks] and
2 CONC  Queen [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clotilde Clotilde] , and was the queen of the Visigothic King Amalaric. She was born circa 500. The favorite child of her parents, she was saddened by her father's death in 511.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Clotilde married Amalaric in about 526,[1] and ties between both families were initially positive.[2] Clotilde was a Catholic, while Amalaric and his fellow-Visigoths were Arians. Clotilde refused to adopt her husband's religious 
2 CONC practices and complained to her kin that she was persecuted for her faith. Amalaric was subsequently kicked out from Narbonne.[2] War ensued in 531 between her brother, King [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Childebert_I Childebert I
2 CONC ], and her husband,[1] at Barcelona, Spain.[2][3] According to Isidore of Seville, Amalaric was eventually defeated, and then assassinated by his own men [4] while Clotilde traveled to Francia with the Frankish army,[1] but died o
2 CONC n the journey. Her cause of death was not recorded. Childebert I brought her corpse to Paris for burial. Her death was greatly mourned by her mother and siblings.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/TOULOUSE.htm#_Toc225040395
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Alaric-II-king-of-the-Visigoths/6000000006244496074?through=4068297799740031007 ALARIC] ([458]-killed in battle Poitiers late summer 507).   m ([494][122]) [https://www.geni.com/people/Theodegotha-Visi
2 CONC goth-queen-consort/6000000003649751712?through=4068297799740031007 THEODEGOTHA] [Thiudigotho] the Ostrogoth,
2 CONT
2 CONT King Alaric II & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Amalarico-I-rey-de-los-Visigodos/4068297799740031007?through=4068314641700010384 AMALRIC] (502-murdered Barcelona 531).  Iordanes names "Amalricus" as the son of "Alarico Vesegotharum" & his
2 CONC  wife[125].  Procopius records that the mother of “Amalricus” was "filiam Theoderici"[126].  Gregory of Tours relates that Amalric, son of Alaric, escaped from the battle in which his father was killed and fled to Spain[127].  He 
2 CONC succeeded his father in 507 as AMALRIC King of the Visigoths, challenged by his half-brother.  After his father's defeat, only Arles and Carcassonne remained under Visigoth control in France.  In Jun 508, King Amalric's maternal g
2 CONC randfather Theodoric King of Italy arrived in France, relieved the siege of Arles, recaptured Marseille and re-established Visigoth hegemony over Septimania[128].  King Theodoric acted nominally as regent for King Amalric, althoug
2 CONC h he proclaimed himself King of the Visigoths in 511 after defeating King Gesalic.  Amalric was defeated by his brother-in-law Childebert King of the Franks at Narbonne in 531, and fled to Barcelona where he established his capita
2 CONC l but was murdered soon after by his cousin Theudis.  The Chronica Regum Visigotthorum records that “Amalricus” reigned for five years[129]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (511) CHROTHIELDIS [Clotilde] of the Franks, daughter of CLOVIS I [Chlodovech] King of the Franks & his second wife Chrotechildis [Clotilde] of Burgundy (-531, bur Paris, basilique des Saints-Apôtres [later église Sainte-Geneviè
2 CONC ve]).  Gregory of Tours refers to the marriage of the (unnamed) sister of the four brothers Theoderic, Chlodomer, Childebert and Lothar with Amalric King of the Visigoths, arranged after the death of their father, specifying that 
2 CONC she was sent to Spain "with a great dowry of expensive jewellery"[130].  Procopius records that “rex…Visigotthorum Amalaricus” married "Regis Theodeberti sororem"[131].  Gregory names her Clotilde in a later passage which records 
2 CONC that she was maltreated by her husband, brought back to France by her brother King Childebert who attacked and defeated King Amalric, but died on the journey and buried in Paris beside her father[132]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
