1 OCCU King of Neustria and Burgundy 639-658, King of the Franks 640-657, King of Neustria and Burgundy, koning der Franken, koning der Merovingers
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''Notice some uncertainty in his dates. 
2 CONT *French Wikipedia says he was born in 635 and died on 31 October  657. 
2 CONT *German Wikipedia says he was born 634 and died on 11 October 657. 
2 CONT *English Wikipedia says he was born 637 and died on 27 November 657 or 658''
2 CONT
2 CONT Clovis II (637–27 November 655 or 658) succeeded his father Dagobert I in 639 as King of Neustria and Burgundy. His brother Sigebert III had been King of Austrasia since 634. He was initially under the regency of his mother Nanthi
2 CONC ld until her untimely death in her early thirties in 642. This death allowed him to fall under the influence of the secular magnates, who reduced the royal power in their own favour. Clovis' wife, Balthild, was an Anglo-Saxon aris
2 CONC tocrat sold into slavery in Gaul. She had been owned by Clovis' mayor of the palace, Ebroin, who gave her to him to garner royal favour. She bore him three sons who all became kings after his death. The eldest, Chlothar, succeeded
2 CONC  him and his second eldest, Childeric, was eventually placed on the Austrasian throne by Ebroin. The youngest, Theuderic, succeeded Childeric in Neustria and eventually became the sole king of the Franks.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clovis was a minor for almost the whole of his reign. He is sometimes regarded as king of Austrasia during the interval 656-657 when Childebert the Adopted had usurped the throne. He is often regarded as an early roi fainéant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clovis II was buried in Saint Denis Basilica, Paris.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clovis_II
2 CONT
