2 CONT ===''Medilands: Alsace'' [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ALSACE.htm#Liutfrieddied864B Liutfried (Family of Hugues Comte de Tours)]===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''LIUTFRIED [II]''', son of HUGUES Comte [de Tours] [Etichonen] & his wife Ava --- (-[864/66]).  
2 CONT An agreement between Charles II "le Chauve" King of the West Franks and his brother Ludwig II "der Deutsche" King of the East Franks dated Jun 860 names "''nobilis ac fidelibus laicis…Chuonradus, Evrardus, Adalardus, Arnustus, War
2 CONC narius, Liutfridus, Hruodolfus, Erkingarius, Gislebertus, Ratbodus, Arnulfus, Hugo, item Chuonradus, Liutharius, Berengarius, Matfridus, Boso, Sigeri, Hartmannus, Liuthardus, Richuinus, Wigricus, Hunfridus, Bernoldus, Hatto, Adalb
2 CONC ertus, Burchardus, Christianus, Leutulfus, Hessi, Herimannus, item Hruodulfus, Sigehardus''"[172].  
2 CONT The ''Annales Bertiniani'' name "''Liutfrido avunculo suo et Waltario''" recording their support for "''Hlotharius [rex]''" when he purported to marry "''Waldradam concubinam''" in 862 and crown her[173].  
2 CONT The testament of "''Gerardus [comes]''" names "''consanguinitate, affinitate et propinquitate etiam nobis junctis, id est Leufredi et Adalardi Comitum''"[174].  
2 CONT '''Signor di Monza'''.  '''Lay abbot of Moutier-Grandval.'''  
2 CONT The ''Annales Alamannicorum'' record the deaths of "''Ebarhart, Liutolf, Erchanker, Liutfrid, Rudolf regni principes''" in 864[175].  
2 CONT The ''Annales Weingartenses'' record the death in 864 of “''Eberht, Liutolf, Erchanger, Liutfrid, Ruadolf, Purghart et alii quam plurimi istius regni Principes''”[176].  
2 CONT The ''Annales Xantenses'' record the death in 866 of "''Liudolfus comes''"[177].  
2 CONT '''m ---'''.  The name of Liutfried´s wife is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >1. HUGUES (-before 20 Sep 884, maybe before 6 Mar 870..
2 CONT >2. '''LIUTFRIED [III]''' (-after 5 Mar 912, maybe killed 916).  An agreement dated 6 Mar 870 between Charles II "le Chauve" King of the West Franks and his brother Ludwig II "der Deutsche" King of the East Franks names "''Leutfri
2 CONC dus comes''" as representative of the latter and, as present, "''Adalelmus comes, Ingelramnus comes, Liutfridus comes, Theodericus comes, item Adalelmus comes''"[180].  An agreement dated Feb 876 of Charles II "le Chauve" King of 
2 CONC the West Franks names "''Bosonis…ducis et sacri palatii archiministri atque imperiali missi, Richardi comitis, Walfridi comitis, Liutfridi comitis, Alberici comitis, Supponis comitis, Hardingi comitis, Bodradi comitis palatii, Cun
2 CONC iberti comitis, Bernardi comitis, Airboldi comitis''" as present in Italy with the king[181].  '''Signor di Monza 879'''.  '''Graf im Sundgau'''.  '''Lay abbot of Moutier-Grandval''': Emperor Karl III confirmed the donations to Mo
2 CONC utier-Grandval made by Lothaire II King of Lotharingia, at the request of “''Liutfridi comitis''”, by charter dated 20 Sep 884[182].  King Arnulf confirmed an exchange of property between Kloster Stablo "''qualiter Liutfridus come
2 CONC s''" and "''viro Ricario''" by charter dated 30 Oct 891[183].  Emperor Arnulf granted property "''in pago…Lobotengoue in comitatu Liutfridi in villa…Uirninheim''" to "''vassallo nostro…Reginbodo''" on the request of "''Liutboldi c
2 CONC omitis''" by charter dated 18 Oct 898[184].  "''Zendeboldus…rex''" donated land "''in pago Arduennense…Bysanch''", formerly held by ''"Liutfridus…comes noster''", to Kloster Stablo by charter dated 30 May 895[185].  The charter da
2 CONC ted 28 Apr 900 of Ludwig "''das Kind''" King of Germany granting property to monk Sigolf states that Kloster Lorsch is "''in pago Lobotingouue in comitatu Liutfridi''"[186].  “''Lutfridus''” donated property “''quod ego et fratre 
2 CONC meo Hugone in partem hereditariam possedi”'', with the consent of “''filiis meis Huntfrido, Lutfrido, Hugone''”, to St Trudpert´s monastery, by charter dated 21 Feb 903[187].  “''Albertus comes de Habesburg. Lantgravius Alsatie''”
2 CONC  confirmed the privileges of “''monasterii Sancti Trudperti...in Nigra Silva''” founded by “''prædecessorum et progenitorum nostrorum Lutfridi comitis, Otperti et Ramperti''”, by charter dated 1186, which quotes the earlier charte
2 CONC r dated 21 Feb 903 (“''anno III regnante Ludevico filio Arnolfi, sub comite Wolfilino''”) under which “''Luitfridus...et fratre meo Hugone''” confirmed the foundation by “''antecessoribus meis Otperto...et Ramperto''”, with the co
2 CONC nsent of “''filiis meis Hunfrido (...in Norgauwe), Luitfrido (...in Sungawa), Hugone (...in Eginsheim)''”[188].  "''Hludowicus…rex''" confirmed privileges to Kloster St Gallen by charter dated 24 Jun 903 in which among "''fidelium
2 CONC  nostrum''" was listed "''comites…Liutfrid''"[189].  The ''Chronicon Laureshamense'' records an exchange of property between "''Hattonis archiepiscopi et abbatis de Riamnis''" dated "''904 XVIII Kal Iul''" witnessed by "…''Liutfri
2 CONC dus comes''"[190].  "''Hludowicus…rex''" confirmed an exchange of properties between Kloster Fulda and Kloster Echternach after consulting "''fidelium nostrorum comitum vero Kebeharti, Liutpoldi, Burcharti, Eginonis, Liutfredi, Ir
2 CONC ingi et Cunpoldi''" by charter dated 19 Mar 907[191].  "''Chuonradus…rex''" made donations by charter dated 5 Mar 912 with the consent of "''fidelium nostrorum comitum vero Sigihardi, Arnolfi, Erchangarii, Odalrici, Perchtoldi, Ch
2 CONC uonradi, Herimanni, Luitfredi atque Iringi''"[192].  Konrad I King of Germany granted property "''in pago Lobotungouue in comitatu Liutfridi comitis''" to the monk Sigulf of Heiligenberg, and after his death to Kloster Lorsch, at 
2 CONC the request of "''Erkangeri comitis ac…Erlolfi et Folnandi''" by charter dated 23 Aug 912[193].  The ''Annales Alamannicorum'' record that "''Erchanger, Perahtolt et Liutfrid''" were killed in 916[194], although it is not known wh
2 CONC ether this refers to the same Liutfried.  '''m ---.'''  The name of Liutfried´s wife is not known.  '''Liutfried [III] & his wife had four children:'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>a) '''HUNFRIED''' (-after 21 Feb 903).  “''Lutfridus''” donated property “''quod ego et fratre meo Hugone in partem hereditariam possed''i”, with the consent of “''filiis meis Huntfrido, Lutfrido, Hugone''”, to St Trudpert´s mon
2 CONC astery, by charter dated 21 Feb 903[195].  “''Albertus comes de Habesburg. Lantgravius Alsatie''” confirmed the privileges of “''monasterii Sancti Trudperti...in Nigra Silva''” founded by “''prædecessorum et progenitorum nostrorum
2 CONC  Lutfridi comitis, Otperti et Ramperti''”, by charter dated 1186, which quotes the earlier charter dated 21 Feb 903 (“''anno III regnante Ludevico filio Arnolfi, sub comite Wolfilino''”) under which “''Luitfridus...et fratre meo H
2 CONC ugone''” confirmed the foundation by “''antecessoribus meis Otperto...et Ramperto''”, with the consent of “''filiis meis Hunfrido (...in Norgauwe), Luitfrido (...in Sungawa), Hugone (...in Eginsheim)''”[196]. 
2 CONT >>b) '''LIUTFRIED [IV]'''.  “''Lutfridus''” donated property “''quod ego et fratre meo Hugone in partem hereditariam possedi''”, with the consent of “''filiis meis Huntfrido, Lutfrido, Hugone''”, to St Trudpert´s monastery, by cha
2 CONC rter dated 21 Feb 903[197].  “''Albertus comes de Habesburg. Lantgravius Alsatie''” confirmed the privileges of “''monasterii Sancti Trudperti...in Nigra Silva''” founded by “''prædecessorum et progenitorum nostrorum Lutfridi comi
2 CONC tis, Otperti et Ramperti''”, by charter dated 1186, which quotes the earlier charter dated 21 Feb 903 (“''anno III regnante Ludevico filio Arnolfi, sub comite Wolfilino''”) under which “''Luitfridus...et fratre meo Hugone''” confi
2 CONC rmed the foundation by “''antecessoribus meis Otperto...et Ramperto''”, with the consent of “''filiis meis Hunfrido (...in Norgauwe), Luitfrido (...in Sungawa), Hugone (...in Eginsheim)''”[198].  [The ''Chronicon Ebersheimense'' r
2 CONC ecords that, during the reign of Emperor Otto I, “''Liutfridus comes de nobili Burgundionum genere''” donated “''allodium suum in Artolsheim''”[199].  It is not known with certainty that the donor was Liutfried [IV].]  [The ''Casu
2 CONC s Sancti Galli'' names "''in Alsatiam…Luitfrido''" as in "''terræ illius potentissimo''" when recording that Alsace was devastated by "''Ungri''"[200], presumably referring to the Magyars.  The passage is undated.  It is not known
2 CONC  whether this Magyar raid into Alsace occurred before or after their first important defeat at the hands of Heinrich I "''der Vogelsteller''" King of Germany at Riade near Merseburg in 933[201].  The immediately following passage 
2 CONC names "''Burgundionum rex Chuonradus, adolescens floridus''" which suggests dating to the late 930s/early 940s.  The chronology suggests that this text refers to Liutfried [IV], although this is not beyond all doubt.] 
2 CONT >>c) '''HUGO'''.  “''Lutfridus''” donated property “''quod ego et fratre meo Hugone in partem hereditariam possedi''”, with the consent of “''filiis meis Huntfrido, Lutfrido, Hugone''”, to St Trudpert´s monastery, by charter dated
2 CONC  21 Feb 903[202].  “''Albertus comes de Habesburg. Lantgravius Alsatie''” confirmed the privileges of “''monasterii Sancti Trudperti...in Nigra Silva''” founded by “''prædecessorum et progenitorum nostrorum Lutfridi comitis, Otper
2 CONC ti et Ramperti''”, by charter dated 1186, which quotes the earlier charter dated 21 Feb 903 (“''anno III regnante Ludevico filio Arnolfi, sub comite Wolfilino''”) under which “''Luitfridus...et fratre meo Hugone''” confirmed the f
2 CONC oundation by “''antecessoribus meis Otperto...et Ramperto''”, with the consent of “''filiis meis Hunfrido (...in Norgauwe), Luitfrido (...in Sungawa), Hugone (...in Eginsheim)''”[203]. 
2 CONT >>d) '''ADELAIS'''.  The necrology of Brixen records that "''Liutfrid comes tradidit filiam suam Adelei''"[204].  Nun at Brixen. 
2 CONT >3. [AVA. According to Europäische Stammtafeln[205], the wife of Unruoch was the possible daughter of Liutfried [I].  This affiliation is suggested presumably only for onomastic reasons, her name being the same as that of her supp
2 CONC osed paternal grandmother.  The primary source which corroborates the name of Unruoch's wife has not been identified.  '''m UNRUOCH''', son of EBERHARD Marchese of Friulia & his wife Gisela [Carolingian] ([840]-874 after 1 Jul).] 
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT ==='''''Wikipédia français''''' (31 jan 2022)'' [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luitfrid_II_de_Sundgau "'''Luitfrid de Sundgau'''"]===
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''FR''': Luitfrid II de Sundgau, né vers 745 et mort en 802, est un grand seigneur alémanique de la famille des Etichonides, comte de Sundgau vers l’an 788.
2 CONT >'''EN''': Luitfrid II of Sundgau, born around 745 and died in 802, was a great Alemannic lord of the Etichonides family, Count of Sundgau around the year 788.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Biographie====
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''FR''': Luitfrid II de Sundgau est le fils de Luitfrid Ier d'Alsace (700-767), duc d'Alsace, et d’Hiltrudis.
2 CONT >'''EN''': Luitfrid II of Sundgau is the son of Luitfrid I of Alsace (700-767), Duke of Alsace, and Hiltrudis.
2 CONT >'''FR''': Lorsque le roi Pépin le Bref disgracie les membres des Etichonides, l’Alsace se trouve divisée en deux comtés, le Nordgau et le Sundgau : Luitfrid est chargé de ce dernier. 
2 CONT >'''EN''': When King Pepin the Short disgraces the members of the Etichonides, Alsace finds itself divided into two counties, Nordgau and Sundgau: Luitfrid is in charge of the latter.
2 CONT >'''FR''': Luitfrid II de Sundgau épouse Hiltrude, dont l'identité est l'objet de discussion : elle est parfois présentée comme fille d’Otbert III1, mais pour un certain nombre d’historiens et de généalogistes, elle est Hiltrude d
2 CONC e Wormsgau, peut-être fille du comte Robert VI et de Chiltrude de Bavière, petite-fille de Charles Martel.
2 CONT >'''EN''': Luitfrid II of Sundgau married Hiltrude, whose identity is the subject of discussion: she is sometimes presented as the daughter of Otbert III1, but for a certain number of historians and genealogists, she is Hiltrude o
2 CONC f Wormsgau, perhaps daughter of Count Robert VI and Chiltrude of Bavaria, granddaughter of Charles Martel.
2 CONT >'''FR''': Luitfrid II de Sundgau, descendant du duc Etichon-Adalric d'Alsace, possède des terres du côté du Petit Rombach à Sainte-Croix-aux-Mines qu'on appelle plus tard Belmont et Echéry. Ce comte du Sundgau est rappelé dans le
2 CONC  diplôme de Lothaire le jeune pour le couvent d’Eschery, comme père du comte Leutard et de son frère Hugues. Il meurt vers l’an 8022.
2 CONT >'''EN''': Luitfrid II of Sundgau, a descendant of Duke Etichon-Adalric of Alsace, owned land near Petit Rombach in Sainte-Croix-aux-Mines, later called Belmont and Echéry. This Count of Sundgau is mentioned in the diploma of Loth
2 CONC aire the Younger for the convent of Eschery, as the father of Count Leutard and his brother Hugues. He died around the year 8022.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Descendance:''' Luitfrid II d'Alsace et Hiltrude de Wormsgau ont quatre enfants:
2 CONT * [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugues_de_Tours Hugues III de Tours] et de la Haute Alsace (765-837)
2 CONT * [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luitgarde_d%27Al%C3%A9manie Luitgarde d'Alémanie] (776-800)
2 CONT * Leuthard de Sundgau (782-830), comte, époux de Grimilde, issue du sang royal de Bourgogne. Il n’est pas le père de Girart de Roussillon, qui est le fils de Leuthard Ier, comte de Fezensac, puis comte de Paris (816) et un membre 
2 CONC de la famille des Girardides. Mais il est le père d’Otbert, évêque de Strasbourg. ['''''EN''''': count, husband of Grimilde, issue of the royal blood of Burgundy. He is not the father of Girart de Roussillon, who is the son of Leu
2 CONC thard I, Count of Fezensac, then Count of Paris (816) and a member of the Girardides family. But he is the father of Otbert, bishop of Strasbourg.]
2 CONT * Basilie (790-871), abbesse de l’abbaye Saint-Étienne de 845 à 871. Dans un diplôme de l’empereur Lothaire II concernant cette abbaye, elle est appelée par une interpolation manifeste découverte par Schöpflin. L’empereur la nomme
2 CONC  sa parente. ['''''EN''''': In a diploma of Emperor Lothair II concerning this abbey, it is called by a manifest interpolation discovered by Schöpflin. The emperor calls her his relative.]
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Bibliographie====
2 CONT
