2 CONT >m  [https://www.geni.com/people/Ingina-an-Alsatian/6000000007331410656?through=6000000007331640433 INGINA], daughter of ---.  Her name is confirmed by the charter dated 5 Feb 737 under which “Liutfrudus…dux” sold property “in Aun
2 CONC ulfouuilare quicquid Ingina genitore meo”[58]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Adalbert & his wife had six children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>1.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Luitfried-I-duke-of-Alsace/6000000007331733313?through=6000000007331410656 LUITFRIED] [I] (-after [740/41]).  
2 CONT >>2.      [https://www.geni.com/people/Eberhard-Duke-of-Alsace/6000000010123436999?through=6000000007331410656   EBERHARD] [I] (-747, bur Murbach).  The Chronicon Ebersheimense names "duos fratres Eberhardus [et] Maso", specifying
2 CONC  that Eberhard was "in castro Egenesheim" without wife or heirs[66].  A 15th century genealogy included in the cartulary of Honau names "Lutfridum et Ebrohardum" as the two sons of "Adelbertus"[67].  The Annales Murbacenses record
2 CONC  the foundation of the monastery in 715 by "comes…Eberhardus, filius ducis Adelberti", and his donations following the death of "filio predicti comitis", with the consent of "fratris sui Leudofredi et coniugis sue Emeltrudis", and
2 CONC  his burial in the monastery[68].  "Theudericus rex Francorum" donated property "in alodo fidele nostro Ebrochardo comite" to the monastery of "Vosagus in loco Vivario…sive Muorbach in pago Alsacinse" by charter dated 12 Jul 727[6
2 CONC 9].  “Ebrohardus et coniunx mea Chimildrudis” donated property to Weissenburg monastery by charter dated 23 Mar [736/37][70].  The Annales Alammanici record the death of "Eburhardus" in 747[71], although it is not known whether th
2 CONC is was the same person because of the difficulty in dating the reference in the Chronicon Ebersheimense.  "Pippinus rex Francorum" confirmed the privileges of Kloster Murbach by undated charter, placed in the compilation with char
2 CONC ters dated [762/63], which records that "Eberhardi" founded the monastery[72].  m [https://www.geni.com/people/Amaltrude-de-Paris/6000000003095223603?through=6000000010123436999  '''EMELTRUDIS'''], daughter of ---.  The Annales Mu
2 CONC rbacenses record the foundation of the monastery in 715 by "comes…Eberhardus, filius ducis Adelberti", and his donations following the death of "filio predicti comitis" with the consent of "fratris sui Leudofredi et coniugis sue E
2 CONC meltrudis"[73].  “Ebrohardus et coniunx mea Chimildrudis” donated property to Weissenburg monastery by charter dated 23 Mar [736/37][74].  Eberhard & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
