1 OCCU King of the Franks from AD 768 to 814 and 'Emperor of the Romans' from 800 to 814, Konung och Kejsare, RÖMISCHER KAISER (800 - 814); 768 König des Fränkischen Reiches, Rex Francorum & Imperator, Charles the Great, King of Franks, 
2 CONC Holy Roman Emperor
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlemagne#/media/File:Karldergrossesignatur.svg '''Charlemagne's signature'''] -monogram of Charlemagne, from the subscription of a royal diploma:''
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000208614436835&size=large}}
2 CONT [http://www.geni.com/projects/Charlemagne-Emperor-of-the-West-Direct-Family-Line/1550  '''Charlemagne'''](English: Charles the Great, German: Karl der Grosse, French: Charles le Grand, Latin: Carolus Magnus, Dutch: Karel de Grote)
2 CONC ,''' King of Neustria (768-771), King of the Franks (771-814), King of the Lombards (774-814), and Emperor of the Romans (800-814)''' 
2 CONT * Old Low Franconian: Karl thie Mikili, Frankana Kunink
2 CONT * Latin: Carolus Magnus, Rex Francorum
2 CONT * Old Gallo-Romance: Karlus li Magnus, Regis de les Frankes
2 CONT * Old French: Charles li Magne, Rei des Francs
2 CONT * Middle French: Charlemagne, Roi des Francs
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Eldest son of Pippin III and Bertrada of Laon'''. 
2 CONT '''Charlemagne titled himself:''' 'Carolus serenissimus augustus a Deo coranatos magnus pacificus imperator, Romanum gubernans imperium, qui et per misericordiam Dei rex Francorum atque Langobardorum' Davis, RHC: ''A History of Me
2 CONC dieval Europe'', Longman 1977 p155
2 CONT
2 CONT >Translation:  Charles August, the most serene – crowned by God of Peace, is a great commander, who governs the Roman empire, & who also, by the mercy of God, is the king of the Franks and the Lombards
2 CONT
2 CONT ==We Are All Descendants of Charlemagne in the West==
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/2002/05/olson/2497  According to this article '''all Europeans are descended from Charlemagne'''.] Here's [http://www.sarahwoodbury.com/were-all-descended-from-charlemagne-and-related-t
2 CONC o-each-other/ another one], & another [http://sandwalk.blogspot.com/2009/10/are-you-descedant-of-charlemagne.html one], & another [http://www.nbcnews.com/science/all-europeans-are-related-if-you-go-back-just-1-6C9826523 one]. And 
2 CONC here's a quick reference [http://dgmweb.net/Ancillary/OnE/NumberAncestors.html table] for the number of ancestors each of us has per given generation.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Birthdate & Place unknown==
2 CONT [http://www.geni.com/discussions/145711?msg=1006146 See Discussion]. Birthdate is traditionally taken as April 2 742; but 747 & 748 have also been proposed by scholars.  Amongst conjectures for Birthplace:  
2 CONT *Herstal, Liege (present Belgium) 
2 CONT *Aachen, near Aix-La-Chapelle (present Germany). 
2 CONT *Ingelheim (present Germany)
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000208613953888&size=medium}}
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlemagne#/media/File:Aachener_Dom_BW_2016-07-09_13-49-15.jpg '''''Charlemagne's throne in Aachen Cathedral''', by Berthold Werner]''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==By the "sword and the cross”, Charlemagne became master of western Europe.==
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000208614701878&size=large}}
2 CONT ''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlemagne#/media/File:Frankish_Empire_481_to_814-en.svg '''Charlemagne's additions to the Frankish Kingdom'''] by Sémhur'' 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Description of Charlemagne’s crowning by the Pope on 23 December 800''', in the Frankish ''Royal Annals'' (the earliest description we have, probably written c 801 by Angilbert the chaplain). Note: this is subtly different from
2 CONC  the papal description given in ''Liber Pontificalis'', which is written to suggest a far greater authority vested in the Pope than the Frankish point of view, here:
2 CONT
2 CONT 'On that very and most holy day of Christmas, when the king at Mass before the confession of the blessed Peter the apostle, was rising from prayer, Leo the pope put [a/the] crown on his head, and acclamation was made by all the pe
2 CONC ople of the Romans: ‘To Charles Augustus, crowned by God, great and pacific emperor of the Romans, Life and Victory!’ And after the ‘praises’ (laudes), he was ‘adored’ by the apostolic [bishop] in the manner of ancient princes, an
2 CONC d discarding the name of patrician, he was called Emperor and Augustus.' Davis, RHC: ''A History of Medieval Europe'', Longman 1977 p149-50
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000208615102821&size=medium}}''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlemagne#/media/File:Karel_Leo.jpg '''Pope Leo III crowning Charlemagne'''. From Chroniques de France ou de Saint Den
2 CONC is, volume 1, France, second quarter of the 14th century]''
2 CONT
2 CONT =Ancestry=
2 CONT Please see: [https://www.geni.com/projects/Ancestors-of-Charlemagne/4914 The 14 Proved Ancestors of Charlemagne] Project.
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000220549239837&size=medium}}
2 CONT
2 CONT =Descent= 
2 CONT Please see: [https://www.geni.com/projects/Charlemagne-Direct-Descent-Line/1550 Charlemagne: Direct Descent Line] Project.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charlemagne had twenty children over the course of his life with eight of his ten known wives and concubines. Nonetheless, he only had four legitimate grandsons, the four sons of his third son Louis, plus a grandson who was born i
2 CONC llegitimate, but included in the line of inheritance.
2 CONT
