2 CONT '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Pepin-de-Landen/6000000000490564196 Pepin I d639]''', 'The Elder' 'of Landen', Mayor of the Palace of Austrasia m Itta,; maternal grandfather of [http://www.geni.com/people/Pepin-II-d-H%C3%A9ristal-M
2 CONC ayor-of-the-Palace-of-Austrasia/5535353244920040751   Pepin II   d714] , through [http://www.geni.com/people/St-Beggue-of-Austrasia/6000000000860259173?through=5535353244920040751 Begga]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Pepin, the Grandfather of Pepin I''' - Does he exist? '''(Input  [http://www.geni.com/discussions/110536 here], please – [http://www.geni.com/people/Sharon-Doubell/6000000005776584613 Sharon])'''
2 CONT - http://globalgenealogy.com/globalgazette/gazxs/gazxs46.html has NN parents for Pepin I, with a Pepin as one of their parents. But  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pepin_I] names his father as Carloman and NN for his mother, & no gr
2 CONC andparents. On our tree, Pepin I's mother is Gertrudis (whose father is Garibald, not Pepin), & his father is Carloman (whose father is Charles, not Pepin) [http://www.geni.com/people/Sharon-Doubell/6000000005776584613 MY] DECISIO
2 CONC N WOULD BE TO REMOVE PEPIN, GRANDFATHER OF PEPIN I ,  because the source for this:  http://globalgenealogy.com/globalgazette/gazxs/gazxs46.htm] also gets the Heristal/Landen Pepins wrong, so I feel I shouldn’t trust it. THAT MEANS
2 CONC  WE’RE GOING WITH THE WIKIPAEDIA VERSION OF THE FATHER AS CARLOMAN,;BUT THAT DOESN’T GET AS FAR BACK AS THE GRANDPARENTS – A LTHOUGH OUR TREE DOES.
