2 CONC the monastery of San Pedro de Arlanza[162].  This date appears early for the document to refer to children of García García de Aza.]  Salazar y Castro records his parentage, citing a donation by "Pedro García…con sus hermanos Góme
2 CONC z, Ordoño, Gonzalo" of Talavera to the Order of Calatrava, by undated charter[163].  Mayordomo of Alfonso VIII King of Castile Mar 1161 to 7 Feb 1172, and 8 Dec 1195 to 25 Jan 1198.  Salazar y Castro cites a charter of Alfonso VII
2 CONC I King of Castile dated 1 Oct 1177 confirmed by (in order) "Petrus Garsiæ, Gomez Garsiæ, Ordonius Garsiæ"[164].  Mayordomo of Alfonso IX King of Leon 8 Jul 1188 to 18 Dec 1188[165].  "…Petrus Garsie de Lerma…" subscribed the chart
2 CONC er dated Dec 1199 under which Alfonso VIII King of Castile donated the monastery of Las Huelgas de Burgos to the Order of Cistercians[166].  "…Petrus Garsie de Lerma…" confirmed the charter dated 12 Sep 1201 under which Alfonso VI
2 CONC II King of Castile confirmed the purchase of houses in Toledo by "Ferrando Sancii…repostario meo"[167].  m SANCHA Ponce, daughter of conde PONCE de Minerva & his wife condesa Estefanía Ramírez (-after 26 Feb 1189).  “La condesa Ma
