2 DATE 25 NOV 1120
2 PLAC Aboard the White Ship off the coast of Barfleur
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Conde de Perche, Sieur, de Pevensey
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Son of Richer de l'Aigle and Judith d'Avranches
2 CONT * died aboard the White Ship off the coast of Barfleur, France along with two of his sons and several hundred others on 25 November 1120. [Source: James Henry Ramsay, ''The Foundations of England'', Vol. 2,  (S. Sonnenschein & Co.
2 CONC , Ltd., 1898), p. 292.]
2 CONT
2 CONT ====FMG: Normandy: [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMANDY%20NOBILITY.htm#RicherLaigledied1084 Alençon, Evreux, Meulan, Perche]
2 CONT * b) RICHER de Laigle (-killed in battle Sainte-Suzanne 18 Nov 1085, bur Monastery of St Sulpice-sur-Risle)....'''m''' JUDITH d'Avranches, daughter of RICHARD Goz d'Avranches & his wife ---. Richer & his wife had [six or more] chi
2 CONC ldren:...
2 CONT ** i) GILBERT de Laigle (-[1118]).  Orderic Vitalis names “Gislebertum Aquilensem et Engenulfum et Mathildem et alios plures filios et filias” as the children of “Richerium de Aquila Engenulfi filium” and his wife[1250].  Domesday
2 CONC  Book records the land of “Gilbert fitzRicher de l’Aigle” in Witley, Surrey[1251].  "…Gillebert de l’Aigle…" witnessed the undated charter under which Robert III Duke of Normandy donated property to Saint-Etienne de Caen[1252].  "
2 CONC Robertus…" donated property to Chartres Saint-Père by charter dated to [1101/17], confirmed by "Gisleberti…de Aquila" and witnessed by "Gisleberti de Aquila, Julite eiusdem matris et Juliane uxoris ipsius"[1253].  "…Gislebertus de
2 CONC  Aquila…" subscribed a charter dated 8 Aug 1111 under which Henry I King of England confirmed the episcopate of Somerset at Bath[1254]. 
2 CONT ** '''m''' ([1092]) '''JULIANE du Perche''', daughter of GEOFFROY Comte de Mortagne et Comte du Perche & his wife Beatrix de Ramerupt [Roucy] (-after 1132).  Orderic Vitalis names “Margaritam...Julianam” as the daughters of “Goisf
2 CONC redus Rotronis Mauritaniæ comitis filius” and his wife “Beatricis”, adding that Juliane married “Gisleberto de Aquila oppido”[1255], in another passage describing her husband as “Gislebertum Aquilensem” son of “Richerium de Aquila
2 CONC  Engenulfi filium”[1256].  The marriage is dated from a third passage in Orderic Vitalis which records that “Goisfredus Mauritaniæ comes” granted “Julianam filiam suam” in marriage to “Gisleberto Aquilensi nepote eius” after “Gisl
2 CONC eberto Ingenulfi de Aquila” was killed, dated to [1092][1257].  "Rotrocus comes Perticensium" donated property to the abbey of Sainte-Trinité de Tiron by charter dated [1119] subscribed by "Juliane soror mea, Richerii filius eius"
2 CONC [1258].  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis names "Rotaldum eiusdem loci comitem et Iulainam de Aquila matrem regine Navarrensis, et Margaretam uxorem Gisleberti de Novo-burgo" as children, incorrectly, of "Rotaldo comiti de P
2 CONC ertica" & his wife Beatrix de Roucy, specifying that Marguerite had children "Rotaldum Ebrodiensem episcopum cum aliis liberis utriusque sexus"[1259].  "Robertus…" donated property to Chartres Saint-Père by charter dated to [1101/
2 CONC 17], confirmed by "Gisleberti…de Aquila" and witnessed by "Gisleberti de Aquila, Julite eiusdem matris et Juliane uxoris ipsius"[1260].  "Domine Juliane" recognised rights of Saint-Denis de Nogent  by charter dated to [1122/33], s
2 CONC pecifying that she was governing Perche while the count was absent in Spain, witnessed by "Gislebertus puer filius prefate Juliane"[1261].  Gilbert & his wife had seven children:  
2 CONT ** '''Gilbert & his wife had seven children:'''
2 CONT *** (a) RICHER de Laigle ([1095]-[24 Aug] 1176, bur Saint-Sulpice-sur-Risle). Orderic Vitalis names “Richerium et Engenulfum ac Goisfredum et Gislebertum” as the children of “Gislebertum Aquilensem” and his wife[1262]. "Rotrocus c
2 CONC omes Perticensium" donated property to the abbey of Sainte-Trinité de Tiron by charter dated [1119] subscribed by "Juliane soror mea, Richerii filius eius"[1263].  He claimed his father's lands in England from King Henry but was r
2 CONC efused on the excuse that his brothers were serving in the royal household troops and expecting the honor.  It was eventually granted to him after the intervention of his uncle Comte Rotrou, but Louis VI King of France attacked La
2 CONC igle and forced Richer to hand it to him 3 Sep 1118[1264]. — see below. 
2 CONT *** (b) ENGENULF de Laigle (-drowned 25 Nov 1120). Orderic Vitalis names “Richerium et Engenulfum ac Goisfredum et Gislebertum” as the children of “Gislebertum Aquilensem” and his wife, adding that “duo medii” died “cum Willelmo A
2 CONC delino Henrici regis filio” in the shipwreck[1265]. 
2 CONT *** (c) GEOFFROY de Laigle (-drowned 25 Nov 1120). Orderic Vitalis names “Richerium et Engenulfum ac Goisfredum et Gislebertum” as the children of “Gislebertum Aquilensem” and his wife, adding that “duo medii” died “cum Willelmo A
2 CONC delino Henrici regis filio” in the shipwreck[1266]. 
2 CONT *** (d) GILBERT de Laigle. Orderic Vitalis names “Richerium et Engenulfum ac Goisfredum et Gislebertum” as the children of “Gislebertum Aquilensem” and his wife[1267].  "Domine Juliane" recognised rights of Saint-Denis de Nogent  
2 CONC by charter dated to [1122/33], specifying that she was governing Perche while the count was absent in Spain, witnessed by "Gislebertus puer filius prefate Juliane"[1268].  Seigneur du Lac. 
2 CONT *** (e) ROGER. The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified. Abbé de Saint-Ouen, Rouen. 
2 CONT *** (f) GUERIN. The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  Monk. 
2 CONT *** (g) MARGUERITE de Laigle (-25 May 1141). The primary source which confirms her parenage has not yet been identified. "Garsias Ranimiriz" confirmed the rights and privileges of the church of Pamplona on the advice of "uxoris me
2 CONC e Margarite regina" by charter dated 1135[1269]. '''m''' (after 1130) as his first wife, don GARCÍA VI Ramírez “el Restaurador” King of Navarre, son of RAMIRO Sánchez [de Navarra] Señor de Monzón & his wife doña Elvira [Cristina] 
2 CONC Rodríguez de Vivar ([1105]-Lorca, Navarra 25 Nov 1150, bur Pamplona, Cathedral Santa María).  
2 CONT
2 CONT ===<nowiki>——————————————————————————————————————————</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT http://homepages.rootsweb.com/~cousin/html/p359.htm#i6493
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert, Seigneur de l'Aigle was born circa 1061. He was the son of Richer de Laigle and Judith d' Avranches. Gilbert, Seigneur de l'Aigle was listed as a tenant in England in the Domesday book in 1086 at England. He married Julie
2 CONC nne du Perche, daughter of Geoffroy II, comte de Mortagne and Beatrix de Roucy, in 1091.1 Gilbert, Seigneur de l'Aigle died in 1118.
