1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT =Richer de Laigle=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From Medlands:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMAN%20NOBILITY.htm#JulianaLaigleMGilbertTillieres
2 CONT
2 CONT '''RICHER de Laigle,''' son of GILBERT de Laigle & his wife Juliana de Mortagne ([1095]-[24 Aug] 1176, bur Saint-Sulpice-sur-Risle).  He is named and his parentage given by Orderic Vitalis2095.  "Rotrocus comes Perticensium" donat
2 CONC ed property to the abbey of Sainte-Trinité de Tiron by charter dated [1119] subscribed by "Juliane soror mea, Richerii filius eius"[2801].  He claimed his father's lands in England from King Henry but was refused on the excuse tha
2 CONC t his brothers were serving in the royal household troops and expecting the honor.  It was eventually granted to him after the intervention of his uncle Comte Rotrou, but Louis VI King of France attacked Laigle and forced Richer t
2 CONC o hand it to him 3 Sep 1118[2802].  "Richerus…dominus de Aquila" confirmed the donation of property to Notre-Dame de la Trappe by "Gerburgis mater Guillelmi Goidi de Asperis" by charter dated 1136[2803].  "…Richerius de Aquila…" w
2 CONC itnessed the charter dated to [end 1150/early Sep 1151] under which "H. dux Normannorum" granted privileges to the citizens of Rouen[2804].  The Red Book of the Exchequer records enfeoffments in the duchy of Normandy in [1172], "R
2 CONC icherius de Aquila" with 5 knights and one half "de feodo de Crepo[n] in Cadamo"[2805].  Robert of Torigny records the death in 1176 of "Richerius de Aquila" and the succession of "Richerius filius eius"[2806]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m BEATRIX, daughter of ---.  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Richer & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         RICHER de Laigle .  Robert of Torigny records the death in 1176 of "Richerius de Aquila" and the succession of "Richerius filius eius"[2807]. 
2 CONT m EDELINA, daughter of ---.  “Gillebertus dominus de Aquila” donated property to Beigham Abbey, Sussex, for the souls of “Richerii patris mei” and for the health of “dominæ Edelinæ matris meæ…”, by undated charter, witnessed by “E
2 CONC delina matre mea…”[2808]. 
2 CONT Richer & his wife had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         GILBERT de Laigle (-1231).  “Gillebertus dominus de Aquila” donated property to Beigham Abbey, Sussex, for the souls of “Richerii patris mei” and for the health of “dominæ Edelinæ matris meæ et Richerii fratris mei”, by
2 CONC  undated charter, witnessed by “Edelina matre mea, Richerio fratre meo, Engenulfo clerico, fratre meo…”[2809]. The Red Book of the Exchequer, listing scutage payments in [1190/91], records "Gilbertus de Aquila" paying "xi l i m…di
2 CONC midiam marcam pro milite" in Sussex[2810].  The Red Book of the Exchequer, listing scutage payments in [1194/95], names "Gilbertus de Aquila" paying "xxi l xvii s vi d de parvis feodis...de quolibet milite xii s vi d" in Sussex[28
2 CONC 11].  The Testa de Nevill includes a writ of King John dated 1212 which records that "Gileberti de Aquila" owned "villa de Westcot…hundredum de Wudetun" in Surrey before he left for Normandy without the king´s permission[2812].  "
2 CONC Gillebertus dominus Aquila" donated property to Notre-Dame de la Trappe by charter dated 1211[2813].  “Gislebertus dominus Aquile” donated revenue to Notre-Dame de Chaise-Dieu, with the consent of “Elisabet uxoris mee et Gislebert
2 CONC i primogeniti mei”, by charter dated 1215[2814].  His lands reverted to the crown on his death.  m ([1193]) as her second husband, ISABEL de Warenne, widow of ROBERT de Lacy, daughter of HAMELIN d´Anjou Earl of Surrey & his [secon
2 CONC d] wife Isabel de Warenne of Surrey (-before 30 Nov 1234).  A manuscript history of the Lacy family names “Isabella” as wife of “Robertus Lacy”, adding that they were childless[2815].  The Testa de Nevill includes a writ of King J
2 CONC ohn dated 1212 which records that "Gileberti de Aquila" married "comes Warennie…sorore sua" whose dowry was "villa de Westcot…hundredum de Wudetun" in Surrey[2816].  “Gislebertus dominus Aquile” donated revenue to Notre-Dame de Ch
2 CONC aise-Dieu, with the consent of “Elisabet uxoris mee et Gisleberti primogeniti mei”, by charter dated 1215[2817].   Gilbert & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          GILBERT de Laigle (-after 1215).  “Gislebertus dominus Aquile” donated revenue to Notre-Dame de Chaise-Dieu, with the consent of “Elisabet uxoris mee et Gisleberti primogeniti mei”, by charter dated 1215[2818]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         ALICE de Laigle (-bur Norton).  A manuscript history of the Lacy family names “Aliciam filiam Gilberti de Aquila” as wife of “Johannes de Lacy primus comes Lincolniæ”, adding that she was buried “apud Norton”[2819].  m
2 CONC  as his first wife, JOHN de Lacy Earl of Lincoln, son of ROGER de Lacy & his wife Maud de Clare ([1192]-22 Jul 1240[2820], bur Stanlaw, later transferred to Whalley). 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         RICHER de Laigle .  “Gillebertus dominus de Aquila” donated property to Beigham Abbey, Sussex, for the souls of “Richerii patris mei” and for the health of “dominæ Edelinæ matris meæ et Richerii fratris mei”, by undated
2 CONC  charter, witnessed by “Edelina matre mea, Richerio fratre meo, Engenulfo clerico, fratre meo…”[2821]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         ENGENULF de Laigle .  “Gillebertus dominus de Aquila” donated property to Beigham Abbey, Sussex, for the souls of “Richerii patris mei” and for the health of “dominæ Edelinæ matris meæ et Richerii fratris mei”, by undat
2 CONC ed charter, witnessed by “Edelina matre mea, Richerio fratre meo, Engenulfo clerico, fratre meo…”[2822].
2 CONT
2 CONT d)         LUCIE de Laigle (-after 1217).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  "Ricardus vicecomes Sancte Susanne" granted rights to the hospice of Raillon, with the consent o
2 CONC f "Lucie uxoris mee et Radulfi filii mei", by charter dated to [1165/77][2823].  "Radulfus vicecomes Sancte Suzanne" donated the chapel of Raillon to the abbey of Angers Saint-Aubin, for the soul of "patris mei Richardi", with the
2 CONC  consent of "matre mea Lucia vicecomitissa", by charter dated to [1200][2824].  "Lucia vicecomitissa Sancte Suzanne" donated property to Notre-Dame de la Trappe for the soul of "domini R viri mei" with the consent of "R vicecomiti
2 CONC s Belli Montis filii sui" by charter dated 1208[2825].  m RICHARD [I] Vicomte de Beaumont, son of ROSCELIN Vicomte de Beaumont & his wife Constance [of England] (-after 1199, bur Etival). 
2 CONT
2 CONT e)         --- de Laigle .  Robert of Torigny refers to the wife of "Guillermus de Curceio" as "filia Richerii de Aquila" when recording his death in 1177[2826].  m WILLIAM de Courcy, son of --- (-1177). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         ROGER de Laigle .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         ENGENULF de Laigle .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         JULIANA de Laigle .  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  m GILBERT Crispin Seigneur de Tillières, son of ---. 
