2 CONT [his father]
2 CONT GILBERT de Laigle (-[1118]).  Orderic Vitalis names “Gislebertum Aquilensem et Engenulfum et Mathildem et alios plures filios et filias” as the children of “Richerium de Aquila Engenulfi filium” and his wife[2768].  Domesday Book 
2 CONC records the land of “Gilbert fitzRicher de l´Aigle” in Witley, Surrey[2769].  "…Gillebert de l´Aigle…" witnessed the undated charter under which Robert III Duke of Normandy donated property to Saint-Etienne de Caen[2770].  "Robert
2 CONC us…" donated property to Chartres Saint-Père by charter dated to [1101/17], confirmed by "Gisleberti…de Aquila" and witnessed by "Gisleberti de Aquila, Julite eiusdem matris et Juliane uxoris ipsius"[2771].  "…Gislebertus de Aquil
2 CONC a…" subscribed a charter dated 8 Aug 1111 under which Henry I King of England confirmed the episcopate of Somerset at Bath[2772].  m ([1092]) JULIANE du Perche, daughter of GEOFFROY Comte de Mortagne et Comte du Perche & his wife 
2 CONC Beatrix de Ramerupt [Roucy] (-after 1132).  Orderic Vitalis names “Margaritam...Julianam” as the daughters of “Goisfredus Rotronis Mauritaniæ comitis filius” and his wife “Beatricis”, adding that Juliane married “Gisleberto de Aqu
2 CONC ila oppido”[2773], in another passage describing her husband as “Gislebertum Aquilensem” son of “Richerium de Aquila Engenulfi filium”[2774].  The marriage is dated from a third passage in Orderic Vitalis which records that “Goisf
2 CONC redus Mauritaniæ comes” granted “Julianam filiam suam” in marriage to “Gisleberto Aquilensi nepote eius” after “Gisleberto Ingenulfi de Aquila” was killed, dated to [1092][2775].  "Rotrocus comes Perticensium" donated property to 
2 CONC the abbey of Sainte-Trinité de Tiron by charter dated [1119] subscribed by "Juliane soror mea, Richerii filius eius"[2776].  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis names "Rotaldum eiusdem loci comitem et Iulainam de Aquila matrem 
2 CONC regine Navarrensis, et Margaretam uxorem Gisleberti de Novo-burgo" as children, incorrectly, of "Rotaldo comiti de Pertica" & his wife Beatrix de Roucy, specifying that Marguerite had children "Rotaldum Ebrodiensem episcopum cum a
2 CONC liis liberis utriusque sexus"[2777].  "Robertus…" donated property to Chartres Saint-Père by charter dated to [1101/17], confirmed by "Gisleberti…de Aquila" and witnessed by "Gisleberti de Aquila, Julite eiusdem matris et Juliane 
2 CONC uxoris ipsius"[2778].  "Domine Juliane" recognised rights of Saint-Denis de Nogent  by charter dated to [1122/33], specifying that she was governing Perche while the count was absent in Spain, witnessed by "Gislebertus puer filius
2 CONC  prefate Juliane"[2779].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert & his wife had seven children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)       RICHER de Laigle ([1095]-[24 Aug] 1176, bur Saint-Sulpice-sur-Risle).  Orderic Vitalis names “Richerium et Engenulfum ac Goisfredum et Gislebertum” as the children of “Gislebertum Aquilensem” and his wife[2780].  "Rotroc
2 CONC us comes Perticensium" donated property to the abbey of Sainte-Trinité de Tiron by charter dated [1119] subscribed by "Juliane soror mea, Richerii filius eius"[2781].  He claimed his father's lands in England from King Henry but w
2 CONC as refused on the excuse that his brothers were serving in the royal household troops and expecting the honor.  It was eventually granted to him after the intervention of his uncle Comte Rotrou, but Louis VI King of France attacke
2 CONC d Laigle and forced Richer to hand it to him 3 Sep 1118[2782]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (b)       ENGENULF de Laigle (-drowned 25 Nov 1120).  Orderic Vitalis names “Richerium et Engenulfum ac Goisfredum et Gislebertum” as the children of “Gislebertum Aquilensem” and his wife, adding that “duo medii” died “cum Willelm
2 CONC o Adelino Henrici regis filio” in the shipwreck[2783]. 
