1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Infanta doña BERENGUELA de Navarra, Queen of England ([1163/5]-[1230], bur Abbaye de l’Espan (Piété Dieu), Mans, transferred 1821 to Le Mans Cathedral)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT d/o Infante don SANCHO de Navarra & Infanta doña SANCHA de Castilla 
2 CONT
2 CONT x (Cyprus 12 May 1191) RICHARD I King of England (1157-1199)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Infante don SANCHO de Navarra, son of GARCÍA IV King of Navarre & his first wife Marguerite de Laigle (1132-Pamplona 27 Jun 1194, bur Pamplona, Cathedral Santa María).  The "Corónicas" Navarras name "el rey don Sancho de Navarra" 
2 CONC as the son of "al rey don García de Navarra, que dixieron Garçía Remíriz" and his wife "la reyna dona Margerina"[587].  He succeeded his father in 1150 as SANCHO VI "el Sabio" King of Navarre.  The "Corónicas" Navarras record the 
2 CONC death "V Kal Iul" in 1194 of "Santius…rex Navarre"[588].  The Annales Compostellani record the death in 1194 of “Sancius Rex Navarræ”[589]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (Carrión de los Condes 20 Jul 1153) Infanta doña SANCHA de Castilla, daughter of ALFONSO VII King of Castile & his first wife Berenguela de Barcelona ([1139]-5 Aug 1177, bur Pamplona, Cathedral Santa María).  The Anales Toledano
2 CONC s record the death in Aug 1177 of “la Reyna de Navarra, filla del Emperador”[590].  The "Corónicas" Navarras record the death "Non Aug" in 1179 of "Sancha…regina Navarre"[591]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT King Sancho VI & his wife had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >1.         '''Infanta doña BERENGUELA de Navarra ([1163/5]-[1230], bur Abbaye de l’Espan (Piété Dieu), Mans, transferred 1821 to Le Mans Cathedral).  The Nobiliario of Pedro Conde de Barcelos names "D. Berenguela Reina d´Ingalter
2 CONC ra, D. Blanca, D. Constança que murio en Arouca" as the daughters of "Sancho Rey de Navarra"[592].  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Berengariam" wife of "rex Anglorum Richardus" as sister of "Blancham sororis re
2 CONC gis Navarreorum"[593].  Matthew of Paris names her and calls her daughter of the king of Navarre, when he records her marriage in Cyprus[594].  The Continuator of Florence of Worcester records the marriage "IV Id Mai" in Cyprus in
2 CONC  [1191] of King Richard and "Berengariam filiam regis Navarræ"[595].  This marriage was arranged by King Richard's mother Eléonore d'Aquitaine[596].  She arrived with Queen Eléonore at Naples in early 1191 and stayed with her futu
2 CONC re husband's sister Joanna dowager Queen of Sicily. She and Queen Joanna sailed with King Richard's fleet to Palestine and landed at Limassol, Cyprus in Apr 1191[597].  She was crowned Queen of England by the Bishop of Evreux imme
2 CONC diately after her marriage[598].  She sailed from Acre for France 29 Sep 1191 with her sister-in-law Queen Joanna[599].  The Necrology of Le Mans Cathedral records the death "10 Kal Jan 1230" of "Berengaria regina quondam uxor Ric
2 CONC hardi…regis Anglorum"[600].  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines records the death "X Kal Jan 1230" of "regina Berengaria domna Cenomanensis relicta…regis Anglie Richardi"[601].  The Annals of Waverley record that “Berenga
2 CONC ria quondam regina Angliæ” founded “quandam abbatiam de ordine Cisterciensi in pago Cenomannensi…Pietatem Dei” adding that she was buried there[602].  m (Chapel of St George, Limassol, Cyprus 12 May 1191) RICHARD I King of England
2 CONC , son of HENRY II King of England & his wife Eléonore Dss d'Aquitaine (Beaumont Palace, Oxford 8 Sep 1157-Chalus 6 Apr 1199, bur Fontevrault Abbey).''' 
2 CONT >2.         Infante don SANCHO de Navarra (after 1170-Tudela 7 Apr 1234, bur Roncevalle).  
2 CONT >3.         Infanta doña BLANCA de Navarra (-12/14 Mar 1229).  
2 CONT >4.         Infanta doña CONSTANZA de Navarra.  
2 CONT >5.         Infante don FERNANDO de Navarra (-Tudela 16 Dec 1207).  
