1 OCCU Lord of Château-du-Loire and Count of Maine, Count of Maine, LORD OF LA FLECHE, COUNT OF MAINE, Greve av Maine, Greve i Maine, Comte, du Maine, Sieur, de la Flèche-en-Anjou, was the Count of Maine, Conde de Maine
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====FMG: [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MAINE.htm#HelieMainedied1110 Maine: Counts]
2 CONT * 2. '''HELIE de la Flèche''' (-11 Jul 1110, bur Saint-Pierre de la Couture[186]). Orderic Vitalis records that "''Hugo filius Herberti''" and his wife “''Bertam ipsius relictam, Tedbaldi Blesensium comitis sororem''” had “''filiu
2 CONC m...Herbertum et tres filias''”, of whom the third married “''Johanni domino castri...Flecchia''” (which would be difficult to sustain chronologically and confuses the children of Hugues [IV] Comte du Maine with his sisters) and h
2 CONC ad three children “''Goisbertum, Heliam et Enoch''”[187]. Orderic Vitalis names "''Helias, Johannis et Paulæ filius, Hugonis Cenomannorum consulis consobrinus''"[188]. A charter dated 13 Feb 1087 records donations to Angers Saint-
2 CONC Aubin by "''Johannes de Fissa''", with the consent of "''Helias filius eius''"[189]. Orderic Vitalis records that, after Ugo d´Este arrived in Maine, and was helped by “''Gaufridus Madeniensis et Helias aliique cives et oppidoni''
2 CONC ” to secure his inheritance, dated to 1090, adding that “''Helias de Flechia''” captured “''Hoellus antistes''” who opposed them and held him in chains until the newly arrived count was received “''in urbe Cenomannica''”[190].  Or
2 CONC deric Vitalis records that “''Helias consobrinus eius''”, noting his legitimate claim to Maine because “''filia Herberti comitis''” had married “''Lancelinum de Balgenceio''” by whom she had “''Lancelinum Radulfi patrem et Johanne
2 CONC m meum genitorem''” [an inaccurate description of the descent], suggested to Hugues that he returned “''in patriam tuam''” and sold him the county, which he did for “''x milia solidorum''”, dated to [1090][191]. He succeeded as ''
2 CONC 'Comte du Maine'''. Orderic Vitalis records that “''Helias'' [''de Balgenceio'']” was “''heres...soceri sui Gervasii de Castro Ligeri''” whose daughter he had married[192]. "''Comes Helyas qui totius patrie dominus est''" donated 
2 CONC property “''quia de patrimonio uxoris sue Mahildis fuit, etenim Elisabeth, matris Gervasii, patris Mahildis, conjugis sue''” to Château-du-Loir by charter dated to [1095][193]. A charter dated to [1097] records confirmation of don
2 CONC ations to Angers Saint-Aubin by "''Elias…filius eius…et frater eius Gaufridus''" after the burial of their father[194]. "''Gener suus...Cenomanice civitatis Helyas''" confirmed a donation made to Saint-Guingalois “''in castro...Le
2 CONC di fondato''” by “''supradicti castri dominum Gervasium''” to Château-du-Loir on the death of “''uxor sua Eremburgis''” by charter dated to [1097], subscribed by “...''Garsendis uxor eiusdem Gervasii''...”[195]. He delayed his dep
2 CONC arture on the First Crusade in 1097 because William II King of England threatened to capture Maine in his absence, and attacked Robert de Bellême in 1098, but was captured and handed to King William at Rouen[196].  The town of Le 
2 CONC Mans was captured by Robert, son of Hugues de Montfort, and handed to Guillaume Comte d'Evreux and Gilbert de Laigle. Helias was released, and returned to la Flèche and the castles he owned ''de iure uxoris''[197]. Helias recaptur
2 CONC ed the city in late 1100 after the death of King William II[198]. "''Helias comes Cenomanensis''" donated property to the monastery of Saint-Pierre de Couture, for the soul of "''monachatu Enoch fratris mei''", by undated charter 
2 CONC dated to [1109][199]. The Annals of Waverley record that “''Philippus de Brausa et Willelmus Malet et Willelmus Barnard et Helias comes Cenomanniæ''” were deprived of their lands in 1110[200].  The necrology of Le Mans Cathedral r
2 CONC ecords the death "''V Id Jul''" of "''Cenomannorum comes Helias''"[201]. The ''Chronicæ Sancti Albini'' records the death "''1110 V Id Ju''l" of "''Helias comes''"[202]. The ''Annales Sancti Albini Andegavensis'' record the death 
2 CONC "''V Id Jul''" in 1110 of "''Helias comes''"[203]. 
2 CONT * '''m''' firstly [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/mainnob.htm#MathildeChateauLoirdied1099MHelieMaine '''MATHILDE de Château-du-Loir'''], daughter of GERVAIS de Château-du-Loir & his first wife Eremburgis --- (-[10/25] Mar 1099).
2 CONC  Orderic Vitalis names "''Mathildem filiam Gervasii…qui Rodeberti Brochardi filius fuit''" as wife of Helias[204]. The same source records that her dowry consisted of the castles of Château-du-Loir, Mayet, Lucé-le-Grand and Outill
2 CONC é[205]. "''Comes Helyas qui totius patrie dominus est''" donated property “''quia de patrimonio uxoris sue Mahildis fuit, etenim Elisabeth, matris Gervasii, patris Mahildis, conjugis sue''” to Château-du-Loir by charter dated to [
2 CONC 1095][206]. "''Helias comes Cenomanensis''" donated his chapel at the foot of la Tour de Château-du-Loir to Saint-Guingalois for the soul of "''uxoris suæ Mathildis, ante paucos dies defunctæ''" by charter dated 27 Mar 1099[207]. 
2 CONC
2 CONT * '''m''' secondly (after 1099) as her second husband, [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/AQUITAINE.htm#Agnesdied10771093 '''AGNES d’Aquitaine'''], divorced wife of ALFONSO VI King of Castile and Leon, daughter of GUILLAUME VIII Du
2 CONC ke of Aquitaine [GUILLAUME VI Comte de Poitou] & his second wife Mathilde ---] ([1059]–[1077/93] or after 1099, bur Sahagún, León, royal monastery of Santos Facundo y Primitivo)]. Orderic Vitalis refers to this second marriage of 
2 CONC Comte Hélie and "''Agnetem filiam Guillelmi Pictavorum ducis relictam Hildefonsi senioris Galiciae regis''"[208]. However, there are indications (which are not conclusive) that King Alfonso´s wife Agnes died before his second marr
2 CONC iage (see the document CASTILE & LEON KINGS for full details). Another possibility is that Orderic´s passage misstates the name "''Agnetem''" for "''Beatricem''", and that the second wife of Comte Hélie was King Alfonso VI´s widow
2 CONC  Beatrix whose family origin is not otherwise recorded and who could therefore have been Beatrix, daughter of Guillaume VIII Duke of Aquitaine [Guillaume VI Comte de Poitou] & his third wife Hildegarde de Bourgogne [Capet], this p
2 CONC arentage being the most probable from a chronological point of view if she was the daughter of one of the dukes of Aquitaine.  
2 CONT * '''Comte Hélie & his first wife had one child:'''
2 CONT ** a) EREMBURGE du Maine ([1096]-14 Jan 1126). Orderic Vitalis names “''Eremburgem''” as the daughter of “''Helias'' [''de Balgenceio'']” and his wife “''Gervasii de Castro Ligeri...filiam''”, adding that she married “''domini sui
2 CONC  filio Fulconi Andegavorum comiti''”[209]. The ''Gesta Consulum Andegavensium'' records that "''Gosfridum Martellum''" was betrothed to "''Helias comes unicam filiam''", who later married Geoffroy’s younger half-brother[210]. A ch
2 CONC arter dated 25 Apr 1120 records that "''comes Andergavensis Fulco Fulconis et comitissa uxor eius Aremburgis filia comitis Helie''" were present at the consecration of the church of Le Mans[211]. She succeeded her father in 1110 a
2 CONC s '''Ctss du Maine'''. The necrology of Angers Cathedral records the death "XVIII Kal Feb" of "''Haremburgis Andegavorum nobilis comitissa''"[212]. 
2 CONT ** '''Betrothed''' to [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ANJOU,%20MAINE.htm#GeoffroyIVAnjoudied1106 GEOFFROY IV Comte d'Anjou], son of FOULQUES IV "le Réchin" Comte d'Anjou & his second wife Ermengarde de Bourbon ([1073]-19 May 110
2 CONC 6).
2 CONT ** '''m''' (betrothed before 14 Apr 1109, 11 Jul 1110) as his first wife, [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ANJOU,%20MAINE.htm#FoulquesVdied1144B '''FOULQUES V Comte d'Anjou'''], son of FOULQUES IV "le Réchin" Comte d'Anjou & his 
2 CONC fifth wife Bertrade de Montfort (1092-Acre 13 Nov 1144).  
2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>————————————————————————————————</nowiki>
2 CONT ====Wikipediæ
2 CONT * '''Please do not copy and paste entire biographies from Wikipedia into Geni reviews.''' Wiki biographies are updated every one to three years. Too often, these biographies contain unconfirmed information. When biographies on Wik
2 CONC ipedia include footnotes with sources, it is a good idea to check these sources to determine the reliability of the information. '''Please be content with clicking on Wikipedia links in different languages and browsing the informa
2 CONC tion.'''
2 CONT * '''de.'''Wikipedia: [https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elias_I._(Maine) Elias I. Maine]
2 CONT * '''en.'''Wikipedia: [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elias_I,_Count_of_Maine Elias I, Count of Maine]
2 CONT * '''es.'''Wikipedia: [https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/El%C3%ADas_I_de_Maine Elías I de Maine]
2 CONT * '''fr.'''Wikipédia: [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%89lie_Ier_du_Maine Élie Ier du Maine]
2 CONT * '''it.'''Wikipedia: [https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elia_I_del_Maine Elia I del Maine]
2 CONT * '''nl.'''Wikipedia: [https://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eli_I_van_Maine Eli I van Maine]
2 CONT * '''pt.'''Wikipedia: [https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elias_I_do_Maine Elias I do Maine]
2 CONT <nowiki>————————————————————————————————————————</nowiki>
2 CONT Hélie (Helias) purchased the county of Maine from his cousin count Hughes V in 1092 [OV viii, 11 (vol. 4, pp. 192-9)]. His assumption of the title of count can be dated between 29 June 1092, when Hugues V was still count [Latouche
2 CONC  (1910), 148 (#42)], and 27 July of the same year, when he subscribed a charter of Foulques IV le Réchin, count of Anjou [ibid., 149 (#43)]. Hélie obtained the lordship of Château-du-Loir on the death of his father-in-law Gervaise
2 CONC  II, lord of Château-du-Loir. On his death in 1110, both possessions passed to his daughter Éremburge and her husband Fulk of Anjou, becoming a part of the growing Angevin holdings. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://sbaldw.home.mindspring.com/hproject/prov/helia000.htm
