1 OCCU Hertuginne av Mecklenburg, Dronning, Infanta de Aragao, Nun, Rainha de Portugal, Infanta de Aragón, infanta de Aragon, Född prinsessa av Aragon (Spanien), Rainha de, Infanta de Aragão
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dulce Berenguer From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Dulce Berenguer, Princess of Aragon, Queen Consort of Portugal (1152–1198) was first daughter of Ramon Berenguer IV, Count of Barcelona and Petronila of Aragon. She was also the wife of Sancho I of Portugal. [edit]Queen of Portuga
2 CONC l
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1174 she was married to then Prince Sancho as part of an arrangement to secure an alliance between Aragon and Portugal by her brother Alfonso II of Aragon. With her husband's ascent to the throne in 1185, she became Queen Conso
2 CONC rt.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Dulce grep aldri inn i statsanliggender, men la an på å være en god hustru og var et mønster av en mor. Hun fikk ikke mindre enn 11 barn.  Hennes ben hviler i Santa Cruz de Coimbra.65
2 CONT
2 CONT 65 Dansk Biografisk Leksikon, Bind 2 (1933), side 418. Erich Brandenburg: Die Nachkommen Karls des Grossen, Leipzig 1935.
2 CONT      Mogens Bugge: Våre forfedre, nr. 1000. Odd F. Fladstad: Jøran Willumsdatter Søegaard .. og deres aner, side 46, 126. Bent
2 CONT      og Vidar Billing Hansen: Rosensverdslektens forfedre, side 25, 57.
2 CONT
2 CONT Infanta doña DULCIA de Aragón ([1160-Coimbra 1 Sep 1198, bur Church of the Cross Coimbra).  The "Corónicas" Navarras name (in order) "don Pedro…el rey don Alfonso, que ovo nombre Remón Belenguer et el conte don Pedro de Provença e
2 CONC t el conte don Sancho et a la muller del rey don Sancho de Portugal" as the children of the "conte de Barçalona…en esta su muller [dona Peyronela]", stating that the first named Pedro died in Huesca[175].  The Gestis Comitum Barci
2 CONC nonensium records the marriage of "unam filiam…Dulciam [=Raimundi Berengarii quarti]" and "Regi Sancio Portugallensi"[176].  The De Rebus Hispaniæ of Rodericus Ximenes records the marriage of "Sancius" and "Dulcem filiam Raimundi 
2 CONC Comitis  Barcinonæ et Urracæ [error for Petronillæ] Aragonensis"[177].  m (1175) Infante dom SANCHO Martino de Portugal, son of dom AFONSO I King of Portugal & his wife Mathilde de Savoie (Coimbra 11 Nov 1154-Coimbra 26 Mar 1212, 
2 CONC bur Church of the Cross Coimbra).  He succeeded his father 1185 as dom SANCHO I “o Pobledor” King of Portugal.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Queen Dulcia
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference Book: He 156.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dronning Dulcia (--?--) av Aragon was born at Aragon. She died at Portugal. She married Konge Sanco I Alfonsosen Portugal, son of Konge Alfonso I Henriksen Portugal and Dronning Mathilde (--?--) av Savoie.
2 CONT
