1 NOTE {geni:about_me} - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radelchis_I_of_Benevento (...-851)
2 CONT
2 CONT - http://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/radelchi-i_(Dizionario-Biografico)/ - (c.791-851) Tesoriere, poi successore di https://www.geni.com/people/Sicardo-principe-di-Benevento/6000000004868894796 ...ebbe dodici figli. Conosciamo i 
2 CONC nomi di sei fra loro: Orso, Radelgario, Adelchi, Aione, Ladelchi, Arechi. 
2 CONT
2 CONT == MedLands ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''RADELCHIS''', son of --- ([788/60]-849).  His birth date is estimated from the Epitaphium Radelchis Principis which records that he died aged 60[190].  He seized power in Benevento in 839 on the death of [https://www.geni.com/p
2 CONC eople/Sicardo-principe-di-Benevento/6000000004868894796  Sicard Prince of Benevento.]  During the civil war which followed, he gained control of Benevento and the northern parts of the old principality, declaring himself RADELCHIS
2 CONC  I Prince of Benevento.  The civil war was eventually settled by Louis King of Italy [Carolingian] who arranged a division of territories between the two sides under the Radelgisi et Siginulfi Divisio Ducatus Beneventani signed in
2 CONC  early 849, Benevento losing half its territory[191].  In 847, the Arabs captured Bari, where they established an emirate, and Taranto[192].  The Annales Beneventani record the death of Prince Radelchis in 849[193].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' GARETRUDA, daughter of --- (-1 Jun ---).  The Epitaphium Caretrudæ names "coniux Radelchis…hæc Caretruda", adding that she died aged 70 and had twelve children[194]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SOUTHERN%20ITALY,%20PRE-NORMAN.htm#UrsusDuxdiedbefore776
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # Numista › Coins › Lombard Kingdom › Benevento Denier - Radelchis ear of wheat < [https://en.numista.com/catalogue/pieces145309.html link] > Obverse Ear of wheat with off-springing branches surrounded by legend. Script: Latin Let
2 CONC tering: RADELCHI PRINCEPS Translation: Radelchis, Prince.  Reverse Cross with petals in each quadrant surrounded by legend. Script: Latin Lettering: ARCHANGE MICHAHEL Unabridged legend: Archangelus Michael Translation: Archangel M
2 CONC ichael.
