1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT RADELCHI I in Dizionario Biografico degli Italiani - Volume 86 (2016) < http://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/radelchi-i_(Dizionario-Biografico)/  English translation < [https://www-treccani-it.translate.goog/enciclopedia/radelchi-i
2 CONC _(Dizionario-Biografico)/?_x_tr_sl=auto&_x_tr_tl=en&_x_tr_hl=en&_x_tr_pto=wapp&_x_tr_hist=true link] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT >We know the name of Radelchi's wife, but not her ancestry: '''Garetruda''' is known from her epitaph and from her presence in some of Radelchi's diplomas, as a rogator and as the owner of a land endowment; with her Radelchi had t
2 CONC welve children. We know the names of six of them: Orso, Radelgario, Adelchi, Aione, Ladelchi, Arechi.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Medlands 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SOUTHERN%20ITALY,%20PRE-NORMAN.htm#UrsusDuxdiedbefore776
2 CONT
2 CONT ''RADELCHIS'', son of --- ([788/60]-849).  His birth date is estimated from the Epitaphium Radelchis Principis which records that he died aged 60[190].  He seized power in Benevento in 839 on the death of [https://www.geni.com/peo
2 CONC ple/Sicardo-principe-di-Benevento/6000000004868894796  Sicard Prince of Benevento.]  During the civil war which followed, he gained control of Benevento and the northern parts of the old principality, declaring himself RADELCHIS I
2 CONC  Prince of Benevento.  The civil war was eventually settled by Louis King of Italy [Carolingian] who arranged a division of territories between the two sides under the Radelgisi et Siginulfi Divisio Ducatus Beneventani signed in e
2 CONC arly 849, Benevento losing half its territory[191].  In 847, the Arabs captured Bari, where they established an emirate, and Taranto[192].  The Annales Beneventani record the death of Prince Radelchis in 849[193].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' '''GARETRUDA''', '''daughter of''' '''---''' (-1 Jun ---).  The ''Epitaphium Caretrudæ'' names "coniux Radelchis…hæc Caretruda", adding that she died aged 70 and had twelve children[194]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [194] Carmina varia XIII, MGH Poetæ Latini ævi Carolini II, p. 659. 
2 CONT
