2 CONT '''Guy III of Spoleto''' (German: Wido, Italian: Guido; died 12 December 894) was the margrave of Camerino from 880 and then duke of Spoleto and Camerino from 883. He was crowned king of Italy in 889 and emperor in 891. He died in
2 CONC  894 while fighting for control of the Italian Peninsula.
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy was married to Ageltrude, daughter of Adelchis of Benevento, who bore him a son named Lambert.  He was the second son of Guy I of Spoleto[1] and Itta, daughter of Sico of Benevento.
2 CONT
