2 CONC  request of "Ageltrudim…coniugem nostrum imperatricem augustam", by charter dated 1 May 892[965].  Interpreting the relationships referred to in this document is difficult.  If patruus is given is strict meaning of paternal uncle,
2 CONC  it is impossible to see how Konrad could have been paternal uncle to one donor while cousin to the other, when the donors were father and son.  It is assumed therefore that the relationship was one generation removed, although th
2 CONC is solution is not ideal unless "patruus" and "patruelis" are assumed to refer to Guido and Lambert in that order rather than the order in which they are named in the document.  m ERMENGUNDE, daughter of --- (-after 1 May 892).  "
