2 CONT i)          '''LAMBERT''' ([876]-near Marengo 15 Oct 898, bur Piacenza).  Lambert is named as son of Guido in the Guidonis Chronica[960].  His father appointed him as LAMBERT associate King of Italy in May 891, and 30 Apr 892 he w
2 CONC as crowned co-Emperor by Pope Formosius[961].  "Vuido et Lantbertus…imperatores augusti" granted "cortem…Lemennis in comitatu Bergomensi" to "Cohunradum…patruum ac patruelem nostrum…marchionem…et uxori eius Ermengundi et filiis…eo
2 CONC rum", at the request of "Ageltrudim…coniugem nostrum imperatricem augustam", by charter dated 1 May 892[962].  "Lanbertus cæsar imperator augustus" granted property "in comitatu et pago Placentino" to "fideli nostro Amalgiso", at 
2 CONC the request of "Evurardus comes" and with the advice of "Sigefredi comitis", by charter dated Jan 895[963].  Supported by his mother, Lambert took advantage of the illness of Emperor Arnulf and was recognised as King of Italy by P
2 CONC ope Stephen VI in 896, confirmed at the Synode of Ravenna in May 898[964].  He died following a fall from his horse[965]. 
2 CONT
