2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Lambert-I-marchese-and-duke-of-Spoleto/4966601616470103323?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1555602577806&through=6000000091253820861  LAMBERT], son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Wido-comte-et-marquis-de-Nan
2 CONC tes/6000000091234238008?through=4966601616470103323 WIDO] Comte et Marquis de Nantes & his wife --- (-Ticino 30 Dec 836).  The primary source which confirms the parentage of Lambert has not yet been identified.  He succeeded as Co
2 CONC unt of the Breton march.  The Vita Hludowici Imperatoris names "Walam et Warnarium, necnon et Lambertum sed et Ingobertum" as missi [in 813], recording that "Warnarius comes…accito nepote Lantberto" acted without the knowledge of 
2 CONC "Wala et Ingelberto"[923].  He was expelled from Aachen with his uncle Werner in 814 by King Louis I after the death of Emperor Karl I, Werner being killed in the conflict which followed[924].  The forces of "Count Lambert" defeat
2 CONC ed and killed Wihomarc who had rebelled in Brittany in 825[925].  "Lambert" was one of the supporters of the rebellion of co-Emperor Lothar I in 833/34, and consequently lost his position in the Breton march[926].  The Annales Ful
2 CONC denses record fighting with "Mahtfredo et Lantberto", during which battle "Uodo comes Aurelianensium et Theodo abbas sancti Martini Turonensis" were killed[927].  In 834 he was sent to Italy where Lothar gave him land and installe
2 CONC d him as LAMBERT I Marchese and Duke of Spoleto.  The Annales Fuldenses record the earthquake at Ticino in Italy "837 III Kal Ian" in which "plures ex primoribus Italiæ" were killed including "Lantbertus et Hugus"[928].  The Vita 
2 CONC Hludowici Imperatoris records that "Wala Corbeiensis abbas, Matfridus, Hugo, Lantbertus, Godefridus, itemque filius eius Godefridus, Agimbertus comes Pertensis…sed et Richardus" died between "Kal Sep usque ad missam sancti Martini
2 CONC " [in 836][929]. 
