2 CONC fled to Barcelona in 830[480].  The Vita Hludowici Imperatoris records that "Bernhardus" fled into exile in Spain and was deprived of his honours [in 831][481].  The same source records that "Werinus et Bernhardus comites" gathere
2 CONC d a force in Burgundy and reached "Matronam fluvium" [in 834][482].  The Annales Bertiniani record that "Bernardus comes marcæ Hispanicæ" was sentenced to death in 844[483].  The Annales Xantenses record that "Bernhardus comes" wa
2 CONC s killed "a Karolo" in 844, after which "filio Bernhardi" and "Pippinus rex Aquitainiæ, filius Pippini" defeated the king's army[484].  The Annales Fuldenses record that "Karolus" killed "Bernhardum Barcenonensium ducem" in 844 "i
2 CONC ncautem et nihil ab eo suspicantem"[485]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (Aix-la-Chapelle 24 Jun 824) DHUODA [Doda], daughter of --- (-after 2 Feb 843).  The Manual of Dhuoda records the marriage "anno XI domino nostro Ludoico VIII Kal Iul" at "Aquisgrani palatio" of Doda and Bernard[486].  The Manua
2 CONC l was written in 843 and consists of her instructions to her son. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard & his wife had [three] children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         GUILLAUME (29 Nov 826-killed in battle Barcelona 850).  The Manual of Dhuoda records the birth "in XIII anno regni eius III Kal Dec" of "fili primogenite [Willelme]" of Doda and Bernard[487].  [Comte de [Bordeaux?].  Du
2 CONC ke of Gascony [845/46].  The Chronicon Fontanellensis records in 848 that "Nortmanni" captured “Budegalim urbem...et Ducem eiusdem Guilhelmum noctu” in 848[488].  The editor of the Recueil des Historiens des Gaules et de la France
2 CONC  says that "Willelmus iste diversus esse videtur à Willelmo Bernardi Septimaniæ Ducis filio", noting that he had succeeded “Siguino Duci Wasconiæ et Comiti Burdegalens” [Seguin [II], see the document GASCONY], who had been killed 
2 CONC two years earlier “à Nortmannis”, as “Dux...Burdegalensis” (no sources cited)[489].  The primary source which confirms this information has not been identified, but once the possibility is excluded that Guillaume Duke of Gascony w
2 CONC as the son of “Bertrand comte de Bazas”, as discussed in GASCONY, it seems a reasonable assumption that it is correct.  This hypothesis assumes that Guillaume was rehabilitated quickly by the Carolingian rulers after the death of 
2 CONC his father, whose execution was ordered in 844 by Charles II “le Chauve” King of the West Franks as noted above.]  The Annales Bertiniani record that "Guilhelmus filius Bernardi" captured "Impurium et Barcinonam" in 848, and captu
2 CONC red "Aledramnum et Isembardum comites" in the march of Spain in 850 but was himself captured and killed at Barcelona[490].  The Chronicon Fontanellensis records that "Wilhelmus filius Bernardi Ducis" captured Barcelona and expelle
2 CONC d "Aledranno custode illius urbis et limitis Hispanici", dated to [849/50], in a later passage recording that "Wilhelmo invasore urbis Barcinonæ" captured "Isembardus filius Warini et Aledrannus" but that Guillaume was later defea
2 CONC ted and killed by "factione Aledranni et quorundam Gothorum"[491].  These sources do not apply the title dux/comes to Guillaume, nor do they prove that Guillaume in 850 was the same person as Guillaume in 848, but it appears to be
2 CONC  a reasonable assumption that that co-identity is correct. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         BERNARD "Plantevelue" (Uzès 22 Mar 841-[20 Jun 885/Aug 886]).  The Manual of Dhuoda records the birth "XI Kal Apr", in the year following the death of Emperor Louis, at "Uzecia urbes" of the second child [Bernard] of Do
2 CONC da and Bernard[492].  The Annales Bertiniani name "rex markiones Bernardum scilicet Tolosæ et iterum Bernardum Gothiæ, itemque Bernardum alium" in 868[493].  Lay Abbot of Brioude 857/68.  Comte d'Autun 864/69, deposed.  Comte de R
2 CONC odez 864/74.  Comte d'Auvergne after 872. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         [--- ([843/44]-).  The Chronicle of Adémar de Chabannes records that "Vulgrimnus" inherited "Aginnum...urbem" through "sororem Willelmi Tolosani" whom he had married[494].  The identity of "Willelmi Tolosani" is unclear
2 CONC .  The Histoire Générale de Languedoc speculates that he was Guillaume Comte de Bordeaux (whom it calls comte de Toulouse), son of Bernard Marquis de Septimanie and his wife Dhuoda[495].  If Vulgrin’s wife was Bernard and Dhouda’s
2 CONC  daughter, she is assumed to have been born in [842/44] as the Manual of Dhuoda states that the couple’s second son Bernard was his mother's second child [assuming that female children were not simply ignored by the Manual][496]. 
2 CONC  The editors of the third edition of the Histoire Générale de Languedoc suggest that the passage in Adhémar de Chabannes refers "probablement [à] Guillaume comte de Bordeaux" [Duke of Gascony][497].  Jaurgain suggests that this su
2 CONC ggestion is correct, on the basis that Guillaume was the son of “Bertrand comte de Bazas et d’Agen” and therefore entitled to pass Agen to his brother-in-law[498].  Unfortunately, he cites no source which confirms that Bertrand wa
2 CONC s “comte d’Agen”, nor any source which confirms beyond doubt the co-identity between Bertrand’s son Guillaume and Guillaume Comte [de Bordeaux [Duke of Gascony].  As discussed in the document GASCONY (see the section recording Duk
2 CONC e Guillaume who died in 850), the existence of this “Bertrand” in fact seems based on a misinterpretation by Marca of an undated later charter under which Vulgrin [I]’s grandson Bernard Comte de Périgord restored the abbey of Sain
2 CONC t-Sour de Genouillac (see the section Comtes de Périgord in the document ANGOULÊME, LA MARCHE, PERIGORD).  “Guillaume comte de Bordeaux” was therefore probably the same person as Guillaume, son of Bernard Comte d’Autun, Marquis de
2 CONC  Septimanie, in which case the supposedly revised suggestion in the third edition of the Histoire Générale de Languedoc was in fact the same as the suggestion made in the earlier edition.  m VULGRIN [I] Comte d'Angoulême, son of V
2 CONC ULFARD [d'Angoulême] & his wife Susanna de Paris (-3 May 886, bur Angoulême Saint-Cybard).] 
