2 CONC , Ermengaudo fratre suo, Bernardo vicecomite"[922]. 
2 CONT Comte Ermengaud & his wife had four children:
2 CONT 1.         RAYMOND [I] (-killed [Feb/9 Sep] 961]).  "Ermengaudus comes et filius suus Regimundus et Rainus vicecomes et vicarius" donated property "in pago Ruthenico in ministerio Curiense in villa…Seviniaco" to Vabres by charter 
2 CONC dated Jan [934], subscribed by "…Ugone filio Ermengaudo, Bernardo vicecomite, Ildoino, Adalone"[923].  He succeeded as Comte de Rouergue. 
2 CONT -        see below. 
2 CONT 2.         HUGUES de Rouergue (-[after 972]).  "Ermengaudus comes et filius suus Regimundus et Rainus vicecomes et vicarius" donated property "in pago Ruthenico in ministerio Curiense in villa…Seviniaco" to Vabres by charter dated
2 CONC  Jan [934], subscribed by "…Ugone filio Ermengaudo, Bernardo vicecomite, Ildoino, Adalone"[924].  Comte [de Quercy]. 
2 CONT -        COMTES de QUERCY. 
2 CONT 3.         son(s) .  The testament of "Raymundus comes", dated 961, states that the testator made donations for the souls of "…fratres meos"[925].  It is not known how many brothers he may have had, but presumably they were all de
2 CONC ceased at that date as none is named as a beneficiary. 
