2 CONT '''Conrad Ier de Bourgogne 1''', aussi appelée Conrad Le Vieux (né vers 800 - mort un 22 mars entre 862 et 866), est le fils de Welf Ier seigneur de Bavière, et de Heilwige (v. 775-833). Conrad Le Vieux, fut comte d'Argengau, de L
2 CONC inz et de Paris et fondateur de l'abbaye de Saint-Germain d'Auxerre.
2 CONT
2 CONT Il est le frère de :
2 CONT
2 CONT Rodolphe, († 866), comte de Ponthieu et de Sens, abbé laïc de Jumièges et de Saint-Riquier ; Judith de Bavière, épouse de Louis le Pieux ; Emma de Bavière, épouse de Louis II le Germanique. Avec Adélaïde d'Alsace aussi appelée Adé
2 CONC laïde de Tours, (v. 805 - † ap. 866), fille de Hugues d'Alsace, dit le Peureux († 837), comte de Sundgau et de Tours, il eut les enfants suivants :
2 CONT
2 CONT Welf II († 858) ; Hugues l'Abbé (v. 830- † 886) abbé de Saint-Germain d'Auxerre, de Noirmoutier, de Saint-Riquier, de Saint-Bertin et de Saint-Martin de Tours, archevêque de Cologne de 864 à 870 ; Conrad II de Bourgogne († 876), c
2 CONC omte d'Auxerre, duc de Bourgogne ; Judith, épouse d'Udo de Neustrie ; Probablement Emma, épouse de Robert le Fort.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conrad_Ier_de_Bourgogne
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Conrad I, Count of Auxerre'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Conrad I the Elder (died about 864) was the count of several counties, most notably the Aargau and Auxerre, around Lake Constance, as well as Paris from 859 to 862/4. He was also the lay abbot of Saint-Germaine in Auxerre. Conrad'
2 CONC s father was Welf. He was one of the early Welfs, a member of the Bavarian branch, and his sister Judith was the second wife of Louis the Pious.
2 CONT
2 CONT Between 834 and 838, Conrad married Adelaide of Tours, daughter of Hugh of Tours. They had:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh
2 CONT
2 CONT Conrad the Younger
2 CONT
2 CONT Probably his son was also Welf I count of Alpgau and Linzgau in Swabia
2 CONT
2 CONT In 858, he and his family, abandoned their sovereign Louis the German and went over to Charles the Bald, Judith's son. They were generously rewarded and Conrad was appointed to many countships. Louis the German confiscated his Bav
2 CONC arian fiefs and lands.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Miracula Sancti Germani calls Conrad Chuonradus princeps (prince, sovereign), when recording his marriage. By some accounts his wife re-married to Robert the Strong after his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conrad_I,_Count_of_Auxerre
