2 CONT ----
2 CONT HUGUES (-20 Oct 837, bur Monza)  Comte de Tours...m AVA, daughter of -- (-4 Sep 839, bur Monza). Hugues & his wife had six children: 
2 CONT >2)         '''ADELAIS (-after 866).  The Miraculis Sancti Germani name "Adheleid" as wife of "Chuonradus princeps", noting that she was “primorum et ipsa natalium perinde titulus gloriosa”[158].  A poem by Walahfridus Strabus rec
2 CONC ords the epitaph of "Adelheidam"[159].  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified.  Some secondary works[160] assert that the second husband of Adelais was Robert "le Fort" [Capet].  If this is co
2 CONC rrect, Adelais must have been Comte Robert's second or third wife as Conrad died after 862 by which date Robert's known children were already born.  The assertion appears based on the Chronicle of St Bénigne de Dijon which names "
2 CONC duo filii Rotberti Andegavorum comitis, frs Hugonis abbatis, senior Odo…Robertus alter"[161].  Settipani states that the passage is a 12th century interpolation and has little historical value, although he does suggest that it is 
2 CONC likely that the wife of Comte Robert was a close relation of Adelais without providing the basis for this statement[162].  A family connection between Comte Robert and Conrad Comte de Paris is also suggested by the former being in
2 CONC vested with the county of Auxerre in 865, after this county was confiscated from the latter (as recorded by Hincmar[163]), on the assumption that there was some basis of heredity behind the transmission of counties in France at th
2 CONC at time (which is probable, but remains unproven).  m CONRAD "l'Ancien" Comte de Paris, son of WELF I Graf in Swabia & his wife Heilwig --- (-22 Mar [862/66]).   ''' 
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ALSACE.htm#Adelaisdiedafter866
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT WELF [I], son of ROTHARD Graf & his wife -- (-[824/25]) m HEILWIG, daughter of -- (-after 17 Mar 833).  Abbess of Chelles, near Paris..after her daughter’s marriage in 819. Welf [I] & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >2.)        CONRAD "l'Ancien" (-22 Mar [862/66]).   '''m ADELAIS [de Tours], daughter of HUGUES Comte [de Tours] & his wife Ava ---.  Comte Conrad & his wife had [five] children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>a)         WELF (-before 876)
2 CONT >>b)         CONRAD (-876).   Comte d'Auxerre
2 CONT >>c)         HUGO (-Orléans 12 May 886, bur Saint-Germain d'Auxerre).  Marquis de Neustrie, Comte de Tours et d'Angers 866.  Comte d'Auxerre 
2 CONT >>d)         ?RUDOLF 
2 CONT >>e)         [JUDITH] x  UDO Graf im Lahngau, son of GEBHARD Graf im Niederlahngau [Konradiner]  
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/WURTTEMBERG.htm#ConradIParisdiedafter862
2 CONT
2 CONT ——————————————————————————————    
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelaid of Tours was born Von Sundgau in 819 to Hugo Van Tours and Bava Ava/Ada Van Tours. She was the wife of Van Beieren Koenraad. They had 11 children, Mother of Hugues l'Abbé; Conrad II "the Younger", duke of Transjurane Burgu
2 CONC ndy; Ava D'AUXERRE; Welf II, count of Argengau; Adele VAN MEAUX; Ermentrude d'Namur; Judith D'AUXERRE; Itta D'AUXERRE; Eticho IM ARGENGAU; Adalhard I, Count of Argengau; Rudolf, Abbot Of ST. RIQUIER; Evesna Argenteau VON SACHSEN; 
2 CONC Berthe DE FEZENSAC. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Robert IV le Fort Margrave of Neustria. They had 4 children, Odo (Eudes), King of France; Robert I, King of France; Bertha of Vermandois CAPET and Richard de Morvais CAPET.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Geni World Family Tree MyHeritage.com [online database]. Lehi, UT, USA: MyHeritage (USA) Inc. https://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-40000/geni-world-family-tree
2 CONT
2 CONT Record: https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40000-204407868/adelheid-van-beieren-born-van-tours-in-geni-world-family-tree Adelheid Van Beieren (born Van Tours)
2 CONT
2 CONT Citation: Adelheid Van Beieren (born Van Tours) Birth: 819 Death: 866 Father: Hugo Van Tours Mother: Bava Ava/ada Van Tours Husband: Van Beieren Koenraad i Van Beieren Child: Koenraad ii Van Beieren (born Auxene)
2 CONT  _______________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of [http://www.geni.com/people/Robert-IV-le-Fort-Marquis-de-Neustrie/6000000006036670007 Robert le Fort's] wife is not attested in primary sources. According to some modern scholars she was Adelaide or Adalais, a daughter
2 CONC  of [http://www.geni.com/people/Hugues-II-le-M%C3%A9fiant-Comte-de-Tours/6000000007331622581 Hugh of Tours] (and thus an Etichonid) and the widow of [http://www.geni.com/people/Conrad-I-le-Vieux-Comte-d-Auxerre/4932952221030036762
2 CONC  Conrad I of Auxerre] (died 862), a Welf. Since Robert already had children by 862, Adelaide would have to have been his second wife. French genealogist Christian Settipani has identified the source of this identification as the u
2 CONC nreliable twelfth-century ''Chronicle of Saint-Bénigne de Dijon'', which was interpolated into the chronicle of Alberic of Trois-Fontaines.[4] ''Europäische Stammtafeln'' has identified Robert's first wife as a certain Agane. What
2 CONC ever the facts, two of Robert's sons became kings of France: Odo and Robert. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_the_Strong
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelheid d'Alsace F, #8858 Last Edited=9 Feb 2003
2 CONT      Adelheid d'Alsace is the daughter of Hugues d'Alsace, Comte d'Alsace. Children of Adelheid d'Alsace and Conrad, Comte d'Auxerre -1. Guelph I Herzog von Bayern+ d. b 876 -2. Conrad II, Comte d'Auxerre+ d. b 876
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source: http://www.thepeerage.com/p886.htm#i8858
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.rpi.edu/~holmes/Hobbies/Genealogy/ps04/ps04_358.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT When she married Robert, Adelaide ("Aelis") was widow of Conrad I, Count of Aargau and Auxerre, who died 03-22-863.
2 CONT
2 CONT References: [AR7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref: Weis' "Ancestral Roots" (48:17), (181:6)
