2 CONT
2 CONT "While there are many conjectures regarding the wife of Robert, her identity and even her name cannot be definitively determined. Robert had two sons, in addition to several speculated daughters whose existence or identity as Robe
2 CONC rt's daughters cannot be definitively shown:[4]"
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # Odo of France, King of Western Francia[1]
2 CONT # Robert I of France, King of Western Francia.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT She cannot have been a daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Emperor-Louis-I-The-Pious-son-of-Charlemagne-Hildegard/6000000001266578142?through=6000000023738176054 Louis the Pious] & [http://www.geni.com/people/Ermengarde-de-Hes
2 CONC baye/6000000005792904234?through=6000000023738176054 Ermengarde of Hesbaye].  Their daughter Adelaide was born about 799 & Ermengarde died in 818.  Robert the Strong's son Odo was born in 852,  suggesting a mother born between 820
2 CONC -835.
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT # Detlev Schwennicke, Europäische Stammtafeln: Stammtafeln zur Geschichte der Europäischen Staaten, Neue Folge, Band II (Marburg, Germany: J. A. Stargardt, 1984), Tafel 10
