1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Guillame de Sabran was a participant of the First Crusade, in the company of Raymond of Toulouse and Adehemar le Puy::
2 CONT
2 CONT He takes the Cross and leads his vassals:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=VEo8AAAAIAAJ&pg=PA88&lpg=PA88&dq=Guillaume+I+de+Sabran+crusader&source=bl&ots=JGlj7Jtenh&sig=HLkwD7BR9d1yymfBVBh7ce2HnIM&hl=en&sa=X&ei=vNnqUZ-1L4bO9ATZ8ICoBw&ved=0CEUQ6AEwAw#v=onepage&q=Guillaume%2
2 CONC 0I%20de%20Sabran%20crusader&f=false Source: History of the Crusades Author: Joseph Fr. Michaud
2 CONT
2 CONT Particpates in the Capture of Jerusalem:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=VEo8AAAAIAAJ&pg=PA88&lpg=PA88&dq=Guillaume+I+de+Sabran+crusader&source=bl&ots=JGlj7Jtenh&sig=HLkwD7BR9d1yymfBVBh7ce2HnIM&hl=en&sa=X&ei=vNnqUZ-1L4bO9ATZ8ICoBw&ved=0CEUQ6AEwAw#v=onepage&q=Guillaume%2
2 CONC 0I%20de%20Sabran%20crusader&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: History of the Crusades Author: Joseph Fr. Michaud
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maison_de_Sabran
2 CONT
2 CONT It takes its name from the barony of Sabran near Uzes in Languedoc and Provence also had significant assets in Beaucaire and a portion of the city which fell Uzes him as a result of marriage to 1156 Rostaing II with the Roscie Cay
2 CONC lar granddaughter Elzéart d 'Uzes. The Lords of Sabran called themselves by the grace of God, constables of the Counts of Toulouse.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is proud to have two Catholic saints: Elzear de Sabran canonized in 1369, and his wife Delphine or Dauphine, beatified for their mystical love and their love of the humble, who are still subject to a procession every month Sep
2 CONC tember Ansouis, the manor belonged to the family from the tenth century, and from 1836 to 2008.
2 CONT
2 CONT Several of its members were Knights of the Order of Malta, the Kingdom of Naples marshals or senior officers in the Royal Navy.
2 CONT
2 CONT They were also Counts of Ariano, sovereign Counts of Forcalquier, counts Sabran Sabran-Pontevès then, Baron Ansouis, dukes and peers of France. The family had received the Honors of the Court.
