0 @N6000000002187576268@ NOTE Leutwinus, Bishop of Trier
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Leudwinus (St. Leudwinus, Leutwinus, Lievin, Liutwin) (660 - 722), was Count and bishop of Trier, 697-715 or 685-704. His parents were Warinus, Count of Poitiers (638-677) and Kunza of Metz, daughter of Clodoule, Bishop of Metz, m
1 CONC aking him the great-grandson of Arnulf of Metz. He was buried at Mettlach.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Marriage and issue
1 CONT He married Daughter of Chrodobertus II and they had the following:
1 CONT
1 CONT Rotrude of Treves who married Charles Martel 
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT The Royal Ancestry Bible Royal Ancestors of 300 Colonial American Families by Michel L. Call (chart 2001, 2054 & 2059) ISBN 1-933194-22-7
