1 CONC o sons of his own, he named his nephew, King Childebert II of Austrasia, his successor. A war with Guntram began and endedthis year in which Duke Desidarius took many cities from the kingdom of Burgundy. In 582, Chilperic and Fred
1 CONC egund had another son, Theuderic, who died two years later. In 584, Chilperic was assassinated. He died at peace with his brother Guntram and at war with his nephew and alleged successor Childebert, but left a son born that very y
1 CONC ear: Chlotar.
