0 @N6000000001503850162@ NOTE Weis' "Ancestral Roots . . ." (181:1) is silent regarding her parentage.
1 CONT
1 CONT Some sources, e.g. Turton's "Plantagenet Ancestry," show her as a
1 CONT daughter of Sigebert III, King of Austrasia (RIN 3709), but there has
1 CONT never been a descent from the Merovingian kings documented to the
1 CONT satisfaction of serious genealogists, and this is among those no longer
1 CONT accepted.
1 CONT
1 CONT Settipani's "La prehistoire de Capetiens" p.106 says (in French):
1 CONT "In the 12th century, the Chronicle of Ebbersheim affirmed that
1 CONT Bereswinda, niece of St. Leger of Autun [RIN 5544*], wife of the duke of
1 CONT Alsace Adalric Ethic, was the sister of a queen. Chronologically, the
1 CONT queen in question, who cannot be identified as Baldechildis, of humble
1 CONT Saxon origin, nor as Bilichildis, daughter of king Sigebert III [RIN 3709],
1 CONT could well be Chimnechildis [wife of Sigebert III and of unkown origin]."
1 CONT
1 CONT -SSMD
