0 @N6000000000943494656@ NOTE [Norvell.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT [Nix.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT [Nixon.ftw]
1 CONT
1 CONT Tentative evidence suggests that Don Rodrigo de Vivar "El Cid" Campeador [Champion] is a direct ancestor of Edward III---through his daughter, Cristina de Vivar> on to Blanche de Navarre (1177-1229)> to Isabella de France.
1 CONT
1 CONT "El Cid"'s daughter Cristina married Ramiro Sanchez, lord of Monzon (d. 1116).  They're mentioned in the Schwennicke revision of *Europaeische Stammtafeln*, Band II, Tafel 56.  The well-known (hardly "tentative") descents from the
1 CONC m to Edward III (d. 1377) go:
1 CONT
1 CONT    Ramiro and Christine -> Garcia VI -> Sancho VI -> Blanca -> Thibaut I
1 CONT    -> Enrique I -> Juana -> Isabel -> Edward III
1 CONT
1 CONT    Ramiro and Christine -> Garcia VI -> Blanca -> Alfonso VIII ->
1 CONT    Berenguela I -> Fernando III -> Leonor -> Edward II -> Edward III
1 CONT
1 CONT    Ramiro and Christine -> Garcia VI -> Blanca -> Alfonso VIII -> Blanca
1 CONT    -> Louis IX -> Philippe III -> Philippe IV -> Isabel -> Edward III
1 CONT
1 CONT    Ramiro and Christine -> Garcia VI -> Blanca -> Alfonso VIII -> Blanca
1 CONT    -> Robert -> Blanche -> Juana -> Isabel -> Edward III
1 CONT
1 CONT Rodrigo Diaz (de Vivar), male line descendant (it would seem) of Judges
1 CONT Lain Calvo and Nuno Rasura, tracing back to a 9th century Nuno
1 CONT Belchidez.  In this descent, he was linked (in the male line) with to
1 CONT some of the early (non-hereditary) Counts of Castile, the Banu Gomez,
1 CONT the Banu Morel, and the Flainez/de Cifuentes families, and (in the
1 CONT female line) to the later (hereditary) Counts of Castile.  He married
1 CONT Jimena Diaz, a descendant of the 10th century count Piniolo Gundemariz.
1 CONT
1 CONT Christina (Ruiz) de Vivar, married Ramiro Sanchez, Count of Monzon, who
1 CONT was grandson (probably through an illegitimate link) of Garcia el de
1 CONT Najera, King of Navarre.
1 CONT
1 CONT Garcia IV, King of Navarre.  He married Margaret l'Aigle, who descended
1 CONT from a Norman lord killed at Hastings (and thus one of the few proven
1 CONT Hastings descents).
1 CONT
1 CONT Blanche of Navarre, married Sancho III, the Desired, King of Castile,
1 CONT son of Alfonso VII, and great grandson of Alfonso VI, el Cid's
1 CONT contemporary, and sometimes enemy on the thrown of Leon/Castile.
1 CONT
1 CONT Alfonso VIII, King of Castile, victor at the battle of Las Navas de
1 CONT Tolosa, which forever tipped the Iberian scales in favor of the
1 CONT christians.  He married Eleanor, daughter of Henry II of England, and
1 CONT Eleanor of Aquitaine.  In addition to son Enrique I (who d.s.p.) he had
1 CONT several daughters, including the wife of Louis VIII, and
1 CONT
1 CONT Berenguela of Castile, wife of Alfonso IX, King of Leon.  This marriage
1 CONT was disolved by order of the pope (Alfonso IX and Alfonso VIII were
1 CONT first cousins), but their children were proclaimed legitimate.  These
1 CONT included Berenguela, wife of Jean, King of Jerusalem, and
1 CONT
1 CONT (St.)Fernando III, King of Castile and Leon, who was father of Alfonso
1 CONT X, the Learned, who competed for the Empire, and
1 CONT
1 CONT Leonor of Castile, wife of Edward I, whose other wife, Margaret of
1 CONT France was descended from Louis VIII.
