0 @N6000000000953533406@ NOTE
1 CONT Obtained the Duchy of Alsace 662, head of the Alsatian House of the Ethiconides, Duke of Alsace 662-690
0 @N6000000001503895723@ NOTE
1 CONT Per Weis' "Ancestral Roots . . ." (181:1), AKA Ethic; he obtained the Duchy
1 CONT of Alsace in 662. he was head of the Alsatian house of the Ethiconides.
1 CONT
1 CONT Evans's "The Origin of the Habsburgs" (The Genealogist, 1980) says:
1 CONT . "The ancestry of Eticho is uncertain. Vollmer believes that he was son
1 CONT of LEUDERIC, son of ERCHONALD, major domus and kinsman of King
1 CONT Dagobert I through his mother. If so, Levillain considers it likely that
1 CONT Erchonald was a son of Garnier, major domus, by Berthe, daughter of King
1 CONT Clotaire II by Bertethrud... Ebling believes that Adalric-Eticho was son of
1 CONT another Duke Adalric of the pagus Attoariensis (Dijon), son of Duke
1 CONT Amalgar of the same region by Aquilina, daughter of Duke Wandelin of
1 CONT the Besancon by Flavia. Dupraz notes the possibility that Flavia might
1 CONT have belonged to the great aristocratic family of the Syagrii."
1 CONT
1 CONT Settipani's "La prehistoire des Capetiens" alludes to his descent from
1 CONT ERCHINOALD, and thus seems to accept that version, as do most other
1 CONT sources.
1 CONT
1 CONT -Stevens/Southworth Medieval Database
