0 @N6000000002187721172@ NOTE Constance of Burgundy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Constance of Burgundy (1046 - 1093), was the daughter of Duke Robert I of Burgundy and Helie de Semur-en-Brionnais.
1 CONT
1 CONT She built a monastery in Burgos for Adelelmus in 1079. She married Alfonso VI of Castile on May 8, 1081. They had two children:
1 CONT
1 CONT Urraca of Castile (1082 - March 8, 1126). 
1 CONT Elvira of Castile. Considered to have died young. 
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Agnes of Aquitaine Queen Consort of Castile and Leon
1 CONT 1081–1093
1 CONT  Succeeded by
1 CONT Bertha 
1 CONT
1 CONT Retrieved from "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constance_of_Burgundy"
