0 @N6000000002187572311@ NOTE Clovis I
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Clovis I
1 CONT King of the Salian Franks 
1 CONT
1 CONT Reign 481 – 509 (King of the Salian Franks)
1 CONT 509 – 511 (King of the Franks) 
1 CONT Born c. 466 
1 CONT Died 27 November 511 
1 CONT Predecessor Childeric I 
1 CONT Successor Chlothar I (Soissons)
1 CONT Childebert I (Paris)
1 CONT Chlodomer (Orleans)
1 CONT Theuderic I (Reims) 
1 CONT Issue Chlothar I
1 CONT Childebert I
1 CONT Chlodomer
1 CONT Theuderic I 
1 CONT Dynasty Merovingian 
1 CONT Clovis I (c. 466 – 27 November 511) was the first King of the Franks to unite all the Frankish tribes under one ruler. He succeeded his father Childeric I in 481[1] as King of the Salian Franks, one of the Frankish tribes who were
1 CONC  then occupying the area west of the lower Rhine, with their centre around Tournai and Cambrai along the modern frontier between France and Belgium, in an area known as Toxandria. Clovis conquered the neighbouring Frankish tribes 
1 CONC and established himself as sole king before his death.
1 CONT
1 CONT He converted to Roman Catholicism, as opposed to the Arianism common among Germanic peoples, at the instigation of his wife, the Burgundian Clotilda, a Catholic. He was baptized in the Cathedral of Rheims, as most future French ki
1 CONC ngs would be. This act was of immense importance in the subsequent history of France and Western Europe in general, for Clovis expanded his dominion over almost all of the old Roman province of Gaul (roughly modern France). He is 
1 CONC considered the founder both of France (which his state closely resembled geographically at his death) and the Merovingian dynasty which ruled the Franks for the next two centuries.
1 CONT
1 CONT Contents [hide]
1 CONT 1 Name 
1 CONT 2 Frankish consolidation 
1 CONT 3 Christian king 
