1 CONT Charles the Great, with an unbending will to power, a readiness to fight
1 CONT resolutely against external enemies, an ability to increase his domain through
1 CONT a strength of character rooted in an unbroken conviction of being at one with
1 CONT the divine will, did so unite in one superstate nearly all the Christian lands
1 CONT of western Europe. He combined a personal piety with enjoyment of life, a
1 CONT religious sense of mission with a strong will to power, rough manners with
1 CONT intellectual growth, and intransigence against his enemies with rectitude.
0 @N6000000002240778153@ NOTE He was co-king of Franks with elder brother Charlemagne in 754 and King of
1 CONT the East Franks from 768-771. Note about Charlemagne: Besides expanding the
1 CONT political power of his empire, Charles brought a cutural renaissance in his
1 CONT empire. Although this imperium survived its founder by one generation, the
1 CONT medevial kingdoms of France and Gemany derived all their constitutional
1 CONT traditions from Charles's monarchy. Throughout medieval Europe, the person of
1 CONT Charles I was considered the prototype of a Christian king and emperor.
