1 CONT Alias:<ALIA> Charles The Great
1 CONT Charlemagne 742?-814, emperor of the West (800-814), Carolingian
1 CONT king of the Franks (768-814). The s on of PEPIN THE SHORT, he
1 CONT consolidated his rule in his own kingdom, invaded It aly in
1 CONT support of the pope, and in 774 was crowned king of the
1 CONT Lombards. He t ook NE Spain from the MOORS (778) and annexed
1 CONT Bavaria (788). After a long stru ggle (772-804) he subjugated and
1 CONT Christianized the Saxons. In 800 he restored LEO III to the
1 CONT papacy and was crowned emperor by him on Christmas Day, thus
1 CONT l aying the basis for the HOLY ROMAN EMPIRE and finalizing the
1 CONT split between the  Byzantine and Roman empires. Charlemagne ruled
1 CONT through a highly efficient adm inistrative system. He codified
1 CONT the law in his various dominions, and his cour t at AACHEN was
1 CONT the center for an intellectual and artistic renaissance. The e nd
1 CONT of his reign was troubled by raids by the NORSEMEN. His son,
1 CONT LOUIS I, was named co-emperor in 813 and succeeded on his
1 CONT father's death. Charlemagne's leg end soon enhanced and distorted
1 CONT his actual achievements, and he became the cen tral figure of a
1 CONT medieval romance cycle.
1 CONT @S1005@
1 CONT Charlemage's empire also  included most of Germany (Saxony,
1 CONT Alamannia and Bavaria) and northern Italy ( Lombardy).  Although
1 CONT charlemagne planned to subdivide the knigdom between his sons,
1 CONT all but one pre-deceased him with the result that a united
1 CONT empire was c ontinued.
