0 @N6000000002187750751@ NOTE Raymond of Burgundy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Raymond of Burgundy (Spanish and Portuguese: Raimundo) was the fourth son of William I, Count of Burgundy and was Count of Amous. He came to the Iberian Peninsula for the first time during the period 1086-1087 with Eudes I, Duke o
1 CONC f Burgundy. He came for the second time (1090) to marry Urraca of Castile, eventual heiress of Alfonso VI of Castile, King of León and Castile.
1 CONT
1 CONT He came with his cousin Henry of Burgundy, who married the other daughter of Alfonso VI, Teresa of León (or Portugal). By his marriage Raymond received the County of Galicia, the County of Portugal and the County of Coimbra. The l
1 CONC ast two were later offered to Henry of Burgundy, father of the first Portuguese King Afonso I Henriques of Portugal.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was succeeded by his son:
1 CONT
1 CONT Alfonso VII of Castile and Leon (1104/1105-1157) 
