0 @N6000000002187750714@ NOTE Sancho III of Castile
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Sancho III of Castile (1134 – August 30, 1158), called el Deseado (The Desired), was King of Castile for one year, from 1157 to 1158.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was the eldest son of King Alfonso VII of Castile and Berenguela of Barcelona. His father's will partitioned the kingdom between his two sons: Sancho inherited Castile, and Fernando inherited Leon. The two brothers had just sig
1 CONC ned a treaty before Sancho's sudden death in the summer of 1158. He left an only son and heir, Alfonso VIII of Castile, by his wife Blanca of Navarre.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Alfonso VII King of Castile
1 CONT 1157–1158 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Alfonso VIII 
