1 CONT Alfonso IX, 1171-1230, Spanish king of Leon (1188-1230), son andsuccessorof Ferdinand II. He conquerored from the Moors severalcities inEstremadura and was frequently at war with Alfonso VIII
1 CONT ofCastile. His marriages with Teresa of Portugal and BerenguelaofCastile were both annulled by the pope. He defeated (1230) the MoorsatMêA™ida. His son by Berenguela, Ferdinand III, reunited (1230)
1 CONT Leonand Castile. [The Illustrated Columbia Encyclopedia, 3rd ed., 1969]
