1 CONT GIVN Alfonso VIII of
1 CONT SURN Castile
1 CONT Alfonso VIII (Alfonso the Noble), 1155-1214, Spanish king ofCastile(1158-1214), son and successor of Sancho III. Chaos prevailedduringhis minority, but he quickly restored order after assuming
1 CONT thegovernment. He married Eleanor, daughter of Henry II of England,andtheir daughter, Blanche of Castile, married Louis VIII ofFrance.Alfonso took Cuenca (1177) and incorporated the provinces of
1 CONT ãa„“lava andGuipzèi¸Øcoa into Castile (1200). Attacked simultaneously by acoalitionof Navarre, Aragon, and Leon and by the Moors, he was defeated(1195)by the Moors. He later made peace with his former
1 CONT Christian enemiesand led them to the great victory over the Almohades atNavas deTolosa (1212). At Palencia he founded the first university inSpain(1212 or 1214). He was succeeded by his son, Henry
1 CONT I (1214-17), whowas succeeded by Ferdinand III. [The IllustratedColumbiaEncyclopedia, 1969]
