0 @N6000000002188305774@ NOTE Elias I of Maine
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Elias I (also Hélie or Élie; died 11 July 1110), called de la Flèche or de Baugency, was the Count of Maine from 1093. He was the son of the lord of La Flèche, John de Beaugency, and Paula, daughter of Herbert I of Maine.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1093, when his cousin Hugh V died, he inherited Maine. With the support of Fulk IV of Anjou, he continued the war with Robert II of Normandy. After Robert's departure with the First Crusade, Elias made peace with William Rufus,
1 CONC  Robert's regent in Normandy.
1 CONT
1 CONT Elias married Matilda, daughter of Gervais, Lord of Château-du-Loir. Their daughter, Eremburg, married Fulk V of Anjou. In 1109, Elias remarried to Agnes, the daughter of William VIII of Aquitaine and repudiated wife of Alfonso VI
1 CONC  of Castile.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Sources
1 CONT
1 CONT     * FranceBalade: les seigneurs du Maine.
1 CONT     * Foundation for Medieval Genealogy: comtes du Maine.
1 CONT     * Hélias de la Flèche.
