0 @N6000000002187927703@ NOTE Dhuoda
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Dhuoda was the wife of Bernat of Septimania and the author of the Liber Manualis.
1 CONT
1 CONT Her first son William was given hostage to Charles the Bald in 841 as a pledge of loyalty by Bernard of Septimania. Dhuoda wrote the Manual for William, but crafted the phrasing knowing that other potential enemies of the time cou
1 CONC ld/would read it.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Reference
1 CONT
1 CONT     * This article incorporates text from the public-domain Catholic Encyclopedia of 1913.
