0 @N6000000002909004900@ NOTE Acfred I (died 906) was the Count of Razès from 837 and Count of Carcassonne from 877.
1 CONT
1 CONT Acfred was the younger son of Oliba I of Carcassonne. He inherited Razès on his father's death, while his elder brother Oliba II inherited Carcassonne. Acfred and Oliba probably shared authority with each other in their two counti
1 CONC es until the elder's death in 877, when Acfred inherited both counties, probably in legally as regent for his nephew Bencion, but actually as count in his own right. Bencion nevertheless succeeded him on his death.
1 CONT
1 CONT Acfred married Adelinda, sister of William I of Aquitaine. He had three sons:
1 CONT
1 CONT William II of Aquitaine 
1 CONT Acfred of Aquitaine 
1 CONT Bernard III of Auvergne
